Russia: North Korea seeks nuclear disarmament, but US does nothing
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin has said that North Korea has made great strides toward denuclearization on the Korean Peninsula, but that Washington has done little to stop it. Insist on the elimination of nuclear weapons. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday, September 12, 2018.
Putin made the remarks while attending a meeting of the Eastern Economic Forum in Vladivostok on Wednesday. Speaking on the occasion, the Russian strongman also stressed that North Korea should receive international security guarantees and that North Korean leader Kim Jong Un could pay a visit to Russia at any time. He wants or thinks easy for him.
The Kremlin sent an invitation to Kim Jong Un to visit Russia a few days ago. But there has been no response from Pyongyang, as there are reports that Kim may visit Moscow before the end of 2018.
