Kampong Cham Police Continue to Crack Down on Illegal Fishing in Srey Santhor and Kang Meas Districts
(Kampong Cham): Illegal fishing offenses in Kampong Cham province were cracked down on by the authorities. On September 12, 2018, the police force cracked down on fishing offenses in Srey Santhor and Kang Meas districts, confiscating some exhibits in order to Burn.
According to the General Commissioner, as a result, Srey Santhor District confiscated three mosquito nets, a 90-meter-long barrier, and exhibits were kept at the Koh Andet Administrative Police Station.
Separately, in Kang Meas district, 34 nets were confiscated, 3,400 meters long barricades and 122 kilograms of mixed fish were released into natural lakes. The exhibits were burned at the head of the road behind Varin II village, Khchao commune, with the approval of the Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court.
At the same time, Major General Em Kosal also said about another operation to crack down on drugs in Trapeang Chi Neang village, Lvea commune, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province. People.
The first suspect, 32-year-old Patta, the second suspect, 30-year-old Hang Tina, and the third suspect, 27-year-old Srun Chea, confiscated seven packages of white gram powder and two mobile phones. Two motorcycles, one accessory and some packaging materials.
