(Kratie): When it comes to social work, we immediately know that most of it is humanitarian work. Social work The creators spend their own time and resources and they never want anything in return other than to seek unity and participation in the betterment of society.
Every day we see that this work is of great interest to the monks who are practicing Buddhism, especially the students who are studying at the university. They understand social work, enabling them to contribute to society and better understand society as a people of that country.
Recently, a group of monks and students devoted time to seek help from philanthropists to help people affected by the floods in Bos Leav commune, Chit Borei district, Kratie province. In addition, the humanitarian team has dedicated two days of resources and personal time to rest on the flood-hit school.
Venerable Vanthong said that he liked this work because it made people in the outside world aware of the lives of the people in the poor areas, creating a culture of sharing. In particular, this work will enable the younger generation to follow their example and help each other in times of need.
The Venerable continued that he wants the people or students to be good citizens, good students to develop our society. He thinks that even though we are poor, we still want to help those who are poorer than us.
At the same time, Ms. Srey Mey said that she wanted to learn more about society, want to know the current situation and daily life. According to this active lady, if she does not participate, she will not know the well-being of the people.
At the same time, Mr. Ly Heang said that the students really want to participate in the development of our society to be better, so this activity shows that young people do not remain silent or ignore the society. No. He said that sacrifice, loyalty and relief is the most important thing to join together for the community for education.
Venerable Meng Teang said that Buddhism is an important part of active participation in daily life and solving people's problems. In addition to humanitarian activities, many monks are working to instill knowledge, morality, and ethics in students, Buddhist education for peace, both physically and mentally, so that they better understand the values of the Khmer nation, as well as strive to abide by them. Parents themselves, too.
He added that on September 30, 2018, he will have a program to teach and educate more than 1,000 children in Mes Prachan commune, Pearang district, Prey Veng province. The monk said that the work was in dire need of materials, but the team promised teachers that it must be done, so he appealed to philanthropists to support the program.
The largest international construction and architecture fair in Cambodia in 2018, nearly 400 companies and international brands from 23 countries participated in the exhibition.
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's largest international architecture, building and building materials exhibition (CAMBUILD 18) officially opened on September 12, 2018 at the Koh Pich Gallery with nearly 400 international companies and brands from 23 Participated in the exhibition which was chaired by Mr. Pheung Sophorn, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Secretary General of the Board of Architects of Cambodia.
The construction fair runs from September 12-14, 2018, with more than 350 exhibitors from international companies and brands from 23 countries, including China, Italy, Japan, South Korea, Germany, Malaysia, Taiwan, Thailand, Singapore and Vietnam. CAMBUILD 18 brings together architects, designers, developers, engineers, contractors, suppliers and distributors, as well as a platform to supply new products with technology and the latest innovations in the construction industry.
