Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon to pay a two-day visit to Japan next week
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, will pay a two-day working visit to Japan from September 18 to 19, 2018 at the invitation of the Government of Japan. .
During his stay in Japan, the Deputy Prime Minister will also hold bilateral talks with his Japanese counterpart Taro Kono.
On the basis of long-term cooperation and friendship, the two Ministers will hold frank discussions and exchange views to strengthen bilateral cooperation that will bring mutual benefits to the people and Both countries.
The Deputy Prime Minister also plans to meet with Japanese dignitaries such as Masahiro Imamura, President of the Cambodia-Japan Parliamentary Friendship Association, Masahiko Komura, Vice President of the Liberal Democratic Party (LDP).
It should be noted that Cambodia and Japan established a strategic partnership in 2013, and Japan is an important development partner in the rehabilitation and development of Cambodia after 1993, and this visit took place after the Japanese government sent a congratulatory message to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who continues to be the Prime Minister for this new term.
