(Hanoi, Vietnam): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has said that countries in the Mekong region will become rice barns for the whole of Asia if they join together to form the Association of Rice Exporters.
He made the remarks as leaders of the Mekong countries, including Cambodia, Thailand, Laos, Vietnam and Myanmar, attended the Plenary Summit on the New Vision for the Mekong Region, hosted by the World Economic Forum in Hanoi. Vietnam on September 12, 2018 yesterday.
During the meeting, as well as answering questions related to the competition between the countries in the Mekong region, which are all rice producing and exporting rice, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that 15 years ago in the ACMECS meeting, Samdech used to Initiate the idea of the five Mekong countries (Cambodia, Thailand, Laos, Vietnam and Myanmar) to form an association of rice exporters. But so far, the initiative has not materialized.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if these five countries can form an association of rice exporters, then these countries will be able to jointly promote the development of agriculture, which will become a rice barn for the whole of Asia.
It should be noted that in that forum, the leaders of the five Mekong countries were allowed to express their respective views on the development of countries in the Mekong region and the challenges. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the Mekong countries today are not only countries that compete on agricultural products, but also help meet the needs of each other.
(Phnom Penh): According to the report from the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police, on September 12, 2018, there were 11 traffic accidents nationwide, resulting in 6 deaths. Three were slightly injured and nine were seriously injured.
