Minister of Health: Cambodia, France vow to work together to study 6 more projects
During a working meeting held at the Ministry of Health on September 12, 2018, Minister Mam Bunheng stated that the six projects to be studied together include:
1 /: Strategies for clinical trials, rapid testing, and the provision of the drug Tenofuniel to prevent the transmission of hepatitis B from pregnant women to infants.
3 /: Detailed study on the prevalence and detection of hepatitis B virus and the practice of unsafe injection for people with HIV and hepatitis in Battambang province.
4 /: Study on the history of the use of antiretroviral drugs for AIDS to find the preparation of a package of treatment called drugs in the third row.
5 /: Assessment of hepatitis based on patient health check-ups to prevent cervical cancer among women living with HIV in low-income countries
6 /: Learn about the community with the infrastructure that is being provided in the community and the services that are being done in the public health service base to improve the cases of hepatitis C in Cambodia.
He added that the project has already implemented 38 projects from 2001 to the present, with France supporting the training of human resources in the University of Health Sciences, especially for the National AIDS Agency. And hepatitis B, represented by Professor Mam Bunheng, who has been planning a project in the past to conduct research on HIV cases in Cambodia.
At the same time, Prof. Bruno Spear Ray also reaffirmed his commitment to further cooperation in the fight against HIV / AIDS and to conduct research on cases of hepatitis B and hepatitis C. Previous plans to prevent hepatitis B, a disease that can spread rapidly from mother to child.
In collaboration with France, the Ministry of Health has benefited from the use of the results in the development of policies as well as strategies and interventions in the fight against HIV / AIDS, especially the National Center for AIDS, Dermatology and STIs. Cambodia.
