General Hun Manet is determined to dare to sacrifice his life for the cause of protecting the people and the motherland
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, who has just taken office as the Commander of the Army, has vowed that he dares to sacrifice his life for the cause of protecting the people and the beloved homeland of the Cambodian nation.
The General said this during a meeting and transfer of duties of the Commander of the Army on September 12, 2018, presided over by Senior Minister Meas Sophea.
General Hun Manet congratulated General Meas Sophea on the occasion of his appointment by the King as Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions.
General Hun Manet continued, expressing his deep gratitude to Senior Minister Meas Sophea, who has been directly involved in the cause of the motherland and the nation of Cambodia since Meas Sophea was about 15 years old as a fighter. Of the Cambodian National Liberation Front in 1970 as the motherland of Cambodia fell into the flames of war.
The new Commander of the Army considers that in the life of the brave army with high dedication and struggle at all stages, Senior Minister Meas Sophea, along with many other dignitaries, has really given life, opportunity and hope for the army. All in the present and the descendants of the next generation of Cambodians.
General Hun Manet was also very proud that the King had appointed him as the Commander of the Army. He also thanked the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, and the leadership of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) for their support and cooperation in the past during his new assignment. This.
He stated that in the spirit of patriotism and in return for His Majesty's wisdom and the bestowal of His Majesty the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the highest level of trust from the Head of the Royal Government. Please make the following commitment:
1: Absolute loyalty to the nation, religion, King for life.
2. Respect and always abide by the Constitution of Cambodia.
3. Follow the leadership of the Royal Government, especially respect and implement the national policy and policy program of the Royal Government of the sixth mandate.
4: Respect and implement the principles and statutes of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as consistently as possible.
5. Strive to fulfill their roles and responsibilities and dare to sacrifice their lives without regret for the cause of protecting our people and our beloved homeland.
