(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on September 12, 2018, requested the Asian Development Bank to examine the possibility of providing technical assistance, human resource development, water management and use. Effective compilation and implementation of laws related to the agricultural sector in line with national economic growth and population growth trends.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Mahbub Ahmed praised the progress in all areas, especially the economic sector that the Royal Government has achieved in the past year under the right leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In practical terms, he praised the progress, which has contributed to improving livelihoods, boosting economic growth and reducing poverty. In the field of agriculture, he was interested in and appreciated the growth as a driving force for national economic growth.
On that occasion, the Minister, on behalf of the Royal Government and on behalf of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, would like to express his deep gratitude to the Asian Development Bank for its full support in the development process of Cambodia, especially the technical support. And funding for agricultural-related projects since 1992, totaling more than $ 450 million.
Mr. Veng Sakhon stated that as a result of those projects, Cambodia's economy has been growing steadily, including in the agricultural sector. Through Mahbub Ahmed, the Minister hopes and believes that the Asian Development Bank will continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia in developing the country further, both now and in the future.
In particular, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has been promoting the development of human resources, agricultural diversification and agricultural mechanization to help promote the processing sector to grow both now and in the future.
At the same time, the Minister of Agriculture requested the Asian Development Bank to examine the possibility of providing technical assistance, human resource development, effective water management and use, compilation and implementation of laws related to the agricultural sector in line with national economic growth trends and Population growth.
