Message from political observers: The new government of the sixth mandate under the applause of the international community!
(Phnom Penh): Many countries in the world, including major democracies, have come out to congratulate Prime Minister Hun Sen as the head of the new government of the sixth mandate.
In fact, after India and Germany, it was the turn of Japan, South Korea, which sent congratulatory messages to Prime Minister Hun Sen, who continued to be the new Prime Minister of the sixth term. So far, many countries such as China, Russia, Ukraine and ASEAN countries, as well as many friendly countries, have sent congratulatory messages to the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
This proves that the new government of the sixth mandate, which emerged from the election on July 29, 2018, has been widely welcomed by the international community, in stark contrast to the propaganda and expectations of extremist opposition groups. Acts to destroy the election and want the new government to emerge from the election without its party to be excluded by the international community.
There are many reasons why the international community welcomes the new government of the sixth mandate:
The first reason: This election reflects the will and choice of more than 83% of the Cambodian people who went to the polls, which is an overwhelming number, even though the opposition has campaigned for clean fingers to prevent people from going to the polls. And the overwhelming majority of voters voted for the CPP by more than 77%, giving the ruling party all the seats in the National Assembly.
Second reason: The election on July 29 was held in a good, peaceful and non-violent atmosphere. Not only that, this election can be considered as the first time and the situation is better in all stages, both before, during and after the election. The Cambodian people are happy without anyone protesting, but on the contrary, they are very happy to see such a good election.
Reason 3: Immediately after the election, Prime Minister Hun Sen announced a policy to better serve the people, so that government officials should double their efforts to serve the people so that the people can get more tangible benefits. This is a warm message for the people.
Reason 5: The establishment of the Supreme Advisory Council on the initiative of Prime Minister Hun Sen to allow unelected parties to have a voice in the country's policies is also a new positive sign for the democratic process in Cambodia.
