Chip Mong stands out in Cambodia's largest international architecture, building and construction expo 2018
(Phnom Penh): Cambodians all over the country know that Chip Mong is the lifeblood of the construction sector in Cambodia. Supply of quality construction products has been at the forefront since the 1980s.
To date, Chip Mong has used more than 30 years of experience in the production of construction products, creating a wide range of additional construction products to meet the needs of the Cambodian construction market, which is in need of real quality construction products.
Chip Mong presents a wide range of outstanding quality products, such as Chip Mong Ready-Mixed Concrete, with the development of the logo and new ready-mixed concrete technology, Mark V Steel, which adds new types of steel to meet the market demand for steel for modern cement buildings. Camel recycled new packaging with the latest technology from Chip Mong Inc.
At the same time, Chip Mong also introduced new construction products, concrete tiles and Chip Mong pipes made using the latest technology from Italy, with raw materials from Europe. Customers who visit the exhibition can also have the opportunity to receive special promotions and souvenirs from Chip Mong.
(Phnom Penh): Despite leaving the post of Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, General Chuon Sovann has left more than 1 billion Riel after trying to save for almost 6 years to the new Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, Lt. Gen. Thet, to prepare for supply. Forces when necessary events occur.
In addition to the budget, General Chuon Sovann, who will be the Deputy Chief of the National Authority for Combating Drugs with the rank of Minister, also left 41,000 liters of gasoline, 5,089 liters of diesel and petrol. 1,795 liters of engines and equipment used in various security missions.
Speaking at the handover ceremony and appointment of new positions on the afternoon of September 11, 2018, General Chuon Sovann, who was amazed to complete his mission for nearly 6 years, also said that in his position as Phnom Penh Municipal Commissioner, he bought 72 vehicles for transporting the army, 58 chase motorcycles and 50 Saren motorcycles.
General Chuon Sovann emphasized that all these funds came from the commission's saving efforts to be ready when there was a situation to supply the forces to prevent demonstrations.
Please be reminded that General Chuon Sovann was promoted to the position of Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner during 2012, replacing General Touch Naroth, who was appointed Director of the Bodyguard Department of the Ministry of Interior and later promoted to Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police.
It is noteworthy that during the six-year tenure of General Chuon Sovann, he has done a lot of work on maintaining security, safety and local public order in Phnom Penh in dealing with various crimes as well as Prevent demonstrations, riots and strikes from protests by opposition groups and other civil society organizations that are destructive in Phnom Penh.
In particular, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Force, under the direct command of the General, was seen as having an important role in preventing the former CNRP's anti-march movement after the 2013 election. Security and public order are of great concern without the presence of a police force.
