(Hanoi, Vietnam): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has said that ASEAN should implement four measures to capture positive development and reduce concerns.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia said so during a keynote speech at the opening ceremony of the 27th World Economic Forum in Hanoi, Vietnam on September 12, 2018.
This year's World Economic Forum in Vietnam is held under the theme "ASEAN 4.0: Entrepreneurship and the Fourth Industrial Revolution." In line with this topic, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the current of scientific and technological progress called the Fourth Industrial Revolution has become a key factor in determining the socio-economic development trends in all aspects with the establishment. Opportunity and challenges for the whole universe.
To ensure positive and stable development and alleviate those concerns at the World Economic Forum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested ASEAN to implement four measures, including:
2. Organize joint programs to strengthen human capacity through improving the quality of education, skills training, problem solving, job loss, and the establishment of a social protection system to address economic and social inequalities.
3. Improve the organization of ecosystems that support research and innovation in the region, strengthen the entrepreneurial capacity to design business models, create new jobs and orient the economy in the future.
4: Continue to improve the infrastructure, both hardware and software, especially increase the existing connectivity, as well as continue to integrate both regionally and internally to continue to build a strong foundation for the ASEAN nations to take advantage of the new growth situation in This world.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that the Royal Government is preparing and adjusting policies in line with the trend to seize opportunities, promote the growth of the technology business market, manage the business environment, as well as reduce potential risks. Eventually by these technologies.
Cambodia is also focusing on promoting entrepreneurship and developing small and medium enterprises to create new decent jobs and new orientations, especially on:
2: Business support program focusing on business consulting, information technology support, including the establishment of research and development centers.
