Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Urges People to Maintain a Culture of Solidarity with Each Other Despite Different Religious Beliefs
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, on September 12, 2018, requested the people throughout the province to continue to maintain a culture of solidarity with each other, despite different religious beliefs.
This request was made on the occasion of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun opening the workshop on Interfaith Dialogue and Sustainable Development, which was attended by 150 participants at Phnom Pros Hotel, Kampong Cham Province on the morning of September 12. 2018.
According to Ms. Sopheak, Director of the Department of Cult and Religion of Kampong Cham Province, in some parts of the world we are living with, there is peace in some areas, but in others there are many problems caused by superstitions. Each one.
The director of the Department of Cult and Religion of Kampong Cham province added that until the war broke out, all this was due to lack of control, no respect, no mutual understanding.
Ms. Sopheak stated that, but for Cambodia in general and in particular for Kampong Cham, although people have different beliefs in four religions: Buddhism, Islam, Christianity, Mahayana Buddhism, we do not Conflict arises because of different beliefs.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun stated that the opening of the workshop was aimed at strengthening the harmony of sustainable inter-faith, and that he fully supported the implementation of the current activities, which confirmed the participation of all Together from all parties to maintain peace in participating in the development of the nation.
He said that in Kampong Cham province at present, many families have been affected by the floods, and at the same time, the religious community also made donations from philanthropists to distribute to people affected by the floods without Adhere to different beliefs.
The provincial governor also requested all participants to participate in discussions on the above topics, please continue this forum to maintain a culture of solidarity between each other, despite different religious beliefs.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun continued that the most special thing is to keep one word, one great Khmer family, put it in the heart box together, and one great Khmer family word can help us to work together, talk to each other, understand each other. Respect each other by our family.
