(Phnom Penh): In March this year, in accordance with the "Plan to Deepen the Party and National Institutional Reform of China", the Central Radio and Television of China was officially established and officially launched on April 19. 2018 ago.
The Central Radio and Television of China has merged three national radio and television stations: China Central Television (China International Television), China Central People's Radio and China International Radio. In just a few months, innovation, publicity, influence and public trust have been rapidly enhanced.
Meanwhile, China Central Radio and Television has accelerated the development of media integration using the latest Internet and digital technologies, creating a new media platform for the search and development of major integrated media. Most in China.
On July 31, 2018, China International TV officially launched a comprehensive strategic cooperation with CMCC in 6 major areas, such as research and development of 5G technology, the establishment of 4K high-definition television channels. Share content, big data and capital, etc., which achieve the sharing of resources, complement each other, benefit each other and win-win.
In support of poverty from July 2018 to June 2019, the Central Radio and Television General will provide poverty alleviation resources through the promotion of more than 1 billion yuan in commercials on the basis of resource expenditure. Poverty through the promotion of 1.40 billion yuan in Chinese commercials over the last two years to support more impoverished areas in China.
As a national broadcasting platform, since its inception, China Central Radio and Television has been actively involved in building and enhancing the level of media integration in the direction of building modern and advanced national media. The international community continues to seek and constantly improve the media development mechanism to achieve more proud achievements.
