The reason why Mr. Sim Dara said this was because some local media recently reported that Mr. Sim Dara and his cronies had swindled the sale of an air plot located in Serey Sambath village, Kong Noy commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh.
The report claims that Sim Dara and two of his accomplices, Lay Samnang and Seng Dalin, were sued for $ 4,675 after finding that their group had sold the land.
According to the complaint, on June 11, 2016, the plaintiff Tha Lavi purchased a plot of land No. 405, 5 meters wide and 20 meters long, for $ 8,000, located in Serey Sambath village, Kong Noy commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh. The plaintiff claims that he bought the lot from Lay Samnang and Seng Dalin, with Sim Dara as the sales representative.
With the trust of the above three people, Tha Lavi bought the lot with the sale and purchase contract No. 053 dated June 11, 2018, with a deposit of $ 500. Later, Lavi paid $ 4,675 in installments to the land and asked to see the lot. Sim Dara and his landless party decided to file a claim for the money.
Mr. Sim Dara confirmed that "the publication is a distortion without a clear source. Spamming an attack on someone without your identification is defamatory. "I can not throw my reputation on a small plot of land, and it can not be traded with my honor, which has been building for decades."
He also stated that during 2016, he received the right from Mr. Lay Samnang and Ms. Seng Dalin to market and sell a plot of land located in Serey Sambath Village, Sangkat Kong Noy, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh. The marketing and sales of this project has long been over, with only a handful of administrative tasks remaining.
Meanwhile, Mr. Lay Samnang and Ms. Seng Dalin, the actual project owners, confirmed to Fresh News that Mr. Sim Dara was only a representative in charge of marketing and administration and was not involved in the implementation of the contractual obligations. - Do not sell with customers. And that marketing work is long over.
Ms. Seng Dalin, the owner of the plot of land in Serey Sambath village, also confirmed that the defamation did not contact her to get the true information and did not ask the local authority where the land was located. From one side only.
She also revealed that the land projects she has sold are more than 400 plots, and her clients are all highly trusted under her company's "Buy Land, Get Land" guarantee. Solid cutting for all customers.
She said that in the past, almost all customers, she favored the time to pay the installment payment after they were late for up to five months, etc. According to the contract, the delay in payment for three consecutive months without notice is correct. Punished, but she never fined, always favors and facilitates customers.
In this regard, Kong Noy commune chief Un Sok Rom confirmed that the case of Mr. Lay Samnang and Ms. Seng Dalin's split plot of land for sale was a real project, as they had already bought land from local people. Combine those solid plans into a solid layout by naming their company as well.
Mr. Sangkat Chief continued that in the geographical area of Serey Sambath Village, Sangkat Kong Noy, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh, no company came to sell the land, they are all the right company that pays real capital to buy from the people peacefully and sell to customers Their right and give confidence to his customers as well, such as the company of Mr. Lay Samnang and Ms. Seng Dalin.
"Ms. Seng Dalin's company, as far as I know, sold hundreds of lots, but there were no disputes and no complaints from me," he said. "Seng Dalin's project, people have built a lot of houses to live as well as business in the area, never had any problems."
He said that the company that has a customer to sue, in fact, he never asked for intervention or resolution from the authorities. But as far as you know, the customer intends to get his money back without buying the land under the company contract, even if his company offers or relocates to a new location next to the road, which is a more expensive location. He also refused to accept, that is, he only wanted his money, which he had just deposited more than 4,000 US dollars.
