Dr. Richner left his peaceful and prosperous homeland for Cambodia in 1991 with a black bag, another clothes bag and a small violin. Since arriving in Cambodia in 1991, Dr. Richner has worked tirelessly to rebuild Kantha Bopha Hospital, which was devastated by the flames of war.
Doctors have made every effort and everywhere to raise hundreds of millions of dollars to save the lives of Cambodian children. His sacrifice does not require any compensation from the Cambodian people. The philanthropist finally left Cambodia with a black bag he had brought with him when he left home for Cambodia in 1991.
Beat Richner sits with a black bag at Phnom Penh International Airport before leaving Cambodia for the last time in March 2017. The doctors at Kantha Bopha Hospital are deeply saddened and every time they see this commemorative photo, they can not hold back their tears.
Mr. Sothy recalled that Dr. Richner was a person who sacrificed his happiness only for the children and the people of Cambodia. He recalled that during the management of the hospital, the doctor paid the utmost attention to the children who came to be treated at Kantha Bopha Hospital, that is, almost all of his breath was only for Cambodian children.
According to Heng Sothy, before leaving Cambodia for the last time, the doctor told the hospital management and staff that he had left Cambodia for only 10 days.
The image above shows that Richner is a symbol of devotion, a symbol of humanity, a symbol of the most astonishing purity.
The death of Beat Richner, a Swiss man who sacrificed more than half of his last life, body, mind and intellect for the cause of children and mothers in Cambodia, is stirring the hearts of Cambodians of all walks of life.
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Chairman of the Board of Trustees of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia and Minister of Economy and Finance, is committed to ensuring the continued operation of Kantha Bopha Hospital despite the loss of the founder of Kantha Bopha Hospital, Professor Beat Richner.
The Deputy Prime Minister stated that the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, established by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, will continue to maintain and maintain the quality standards of the hospital's health services.
This statement was made on the occasion of the Deputy Prime Minister leading the delegation to express their deepest condolences and condolences on the death of the founder of Kantha Bopha Children's Hospital of Cambodia, Professor Beth Richner, at Kantha Bopha Hospital on Tuesday afternoon. Samreth Sak B.E. 2562 is on September 11, 2018.
