(VOVworld) - Vietnamese authorities this week asked Hanoi residents to stop eating dog meat, citing the popular dish as making foreigners look at Vietnam in a bad way and causing infections. Affects life expectancy as well. This is according to the release by the French newspaper Le Figaro on Wednesday morning, September 12, 2018.
Dog meat as well as cat meat is a popular dish with Vietnamese wine and is sold on the streets almost all over Hanoi. But despite its popularity, the Hanoi People's Committee still calls on Vietnamese people to stop eating dog and cat meat because eating these animals can cause infections and damage the country's image. .
In addition, the committee also considered that the killing of these pets is a cruel act that should be stopped, but did not specify any preventive measures. For some Western and Asian countries, slaughtering pets such as dogs and cats for meat is the most hated act.
According to Vietnamese authorities, about 493,000 dogs and cats are living in Hanoi, and as of the beginning of 2018, three people have died in Hanoi, while two have fallen ill due to Eat dog meat.
