(Phnom Penh): Mrs. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of Vital Company, a company that produces and distributes high quality drinking water and is famous for its charitable activities, visited more than 100 mothers who are being treated after giving birth to their children at the hospital. Khmer-Soviet friendship.
The event was held on September 11, 2018, with Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy also bringing 1.5 liters of drinking water and more than 100 sets of baby supplies.
It should also be noted that the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital often has between 40 and 50 mothers giving birth per day, most of whom are poor and middle-class families.
Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy said that in order to celebrate the birth of her new mother, the 25 Riel Vital Foundation has organized a package to share and to visit all women, including mothers. Everyone will receive a 1.5 liter case of drinking water with a set of baby supplies.
She added that this is not the first time for Vital to participate in such humanitarian and charitable activities, we always try to bring funds to use in different places.
She also added that Vital Drinking Water is a high quality and hygienic water that passes through a 12-stage filtration system and easily dissolves milk powder and porridge powder quickly, so Vital is best for babies both to drink and cook. Milk.
Representative of the Russian Hospital, Deputy Director General Chan Vichet, extended a warm welcome to Vital, which has initiated this valuable program for new mothers here. He added that this is not the first time for his hospital to be sponsored by Vital, and this support is invaluable.
He said that this participation reflects a good culture of sharing and perseverance in the health sector, which other companies should pay attention to participate in what Vital is doing here. Therefore, he is very grateful to Vital for taking the time and using the 25 Riel fund for the charity program at his hospital.
