Mr. Nuon Pharath: Drug victims are all those who have the opportunity to develop themselves, society, family and society
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the victims of drug abuse are all those who have the opportunity to develop themselves, their families and their society.
Mr. Nuon Pharath made this remark on the morning of September 11, 2018 at the inauguration ceremony of an 11-room My Opportunity Health Center building at the My Opportunity Center in Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. Which is a gift from Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
Mr. Nuon Pharath said that under the Pol Pot regime, the country was reduced to nothing, including human resources being killed. After 1979, Cambodia rebuilt the country with nothing. But under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has developed in all areas.
Along with this development, Cambodia also has some challenges such as traffic congestion and drug problems. The drug problem has caused some of our young people to become drug addicts, a challenge that our society must urgently address.
Mr. Nuon Pharath stated that drug addicts are like rust on the bottom of a ship, that is, if we do not take measures, the rust will corrode the bottom of the ship, causing the ship to sink.
However, drug addicts are no different from this problem, if we do not solve together, our society will have challenges and can not develop the country to prosper.
He added that drug addicts are all those who have the opportunity to develop themselves, society, family and society, important to their commitment. He said that in developed countries in the West, some drug addicts have become famous and useful in society. Therefore, Mr. Nuon Pharath asked all drug addicts to make efforts to eradicate drugs in order to work for the benefit of our society.
Ms. Mom Chandany, Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Former Youth and Youth Rehabilitation of Phnom Penh and Director of the Opportunity Center, I said that as of September 10, there are 1963 young people who use drugs are neutralizing in the Opportunity Health Center, I have 1963 people There are 133 women.
(Phnom Penh): On September 11, 2018, Ms. Kittisangbandit, Deputy Prime Minister, Men Sam An, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, met with a delegation of the Chinese Youth Federation while visiting Cambodia.
The Chinese youth delegation was led by He Junke, President of the National Youth Federation of the People's Republic of China, with the participation of Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia. During the meeting, Ms. Kittisang Dr. Men Sam An reminded about the history of friendly relations between our two countries, Cambodia and China.
Cambodia-China friendly relations have a long history dating back to antiquity, especially between the former leaders of the two countries, Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and President Mao Zedong, as well as the top leaders of the two countries in later generations. Preserve this heritage and strive to nurture the great Cambodian-Chinese friendship to continue to grow steadily from one stage to another and to this day.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that the leaders of the two countries exchanged visits regularly. In fact, Samdech Techo Hun Sen is in China and attending the China-ASEAN Expo in Nanning, Guangxi Province, China. This confirms the spirit of solidarity and good cooperation between our two countries.
Ms. Kittisangbandit further stated that the bilateral assistance and cooperation between China and Cambodia is a factor that accelerates the speed of the rehabilitation and development of Cambodia's socio-economic success and has helped to improve the living standards of the people.
She added that she was pleased that the two countries 'Youth Federations had implemented the Memorandum of Understanding to strengthen the friendship between the two countries' youths and called on both sides to work together to further strengthen cooperation. Strong.
On that occasion, Mr. He Junke, President of the National Youth Federation of the People's Republic of China, said that this is his first visit to Cambodia. The Chinese Youth Federation is cooperating with the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, led by Hun Many, which has extensive cooperation in youth work and has encouraged Cambodian youth to invest more closely together. Chinese leaders hope that the Chinese-Cambodian youth will continue to cooperate deeply with each other.
