(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the evening of September 10, 2018, told Cambodian students studying in Nanning, Guangxi Province, China that the release of Kem Sokha on bail today. Because of health problems.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed this during a meeting with more than 200 Cambodian students on the occasion of Samdech to attend the exhibition in this city for 3 days from 10 to 12 September 2018.
During the talk, Samdech raised the issue of the release of Kem Sokha on the morning of September 10 due to Mr. Kem Sokha's health reasons. With such a statement, the Prime Minister stressed that the bail of Kem Sokha is under close scrutiny by the court.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has released a letter from Kem Sokha requesting the intervention of the Ministry of Interior to provide security for Kem Sokha, whether he is in custody or out of jail.
It should be noted that Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the National Rescue Party, was released on bail at dawn on September 10, 2018 due to his health problems after being detained in Trapeang Phlong Prison. 3) For more than 1 year.
