(Phnom Penh): Mr. Suon Serey Ratha, former President of the Khmer Rouge Party, on September 10, 2018, wrote a letter to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, asking the competent ministry to temporarily suspend the activities of the Khmer Rouge Party. Claiming that his thumbprint was forged.
Mr. Suon Serey Ratha also requested the Ministry of Interior to conduct an autopsy on the documents of the First and Second Extraordinary Congress letter, which Mr. Suon Sophorn, Acting President of the Khmer Rouge Party, submitted to the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. Suon Serey Ratha stated, “Mr. Suong Sophorn falsified my signature, falsified resignation letter, lied to the founding members, members of the (Permanent) Political Council, members of the Capital / Provincial Council and members of the Local Council, and forged documents. The Ministry of Interior holds two extraordinary congresses to govern the Khmer Rouge. ”
Mr. Suon Serey Ratha added, "Not only that, Mr. Suong Sophorn has appointed two vice presidents of the party to replace the vice president of the party, who changed the party's logo and amended the party's statute and violated the statute."
