Asking for money, the mother did not pull the iron rod, beat the mother and sister, her face was swollen and her head was broken, and even threatened her mother that if she dared to sue, she would be arrested and handcuffed.
(Phnom Penh): A 50-year-old woman ran to file a complaint with tears in her eyes for the police at Post Chaom Chao 2 to intervene and take legal action against her son who used violence with a stick and an iron bar. He and his sister were injured in the head and face because they could not ask for money from their mother and even threatened not to sue their mother. The suspect threatened that if the mother dared to sue, she would be killed immediately.
This incident happened on the afternoon of September 10, 2018 at a rented house in Thmor Koul 3 village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The mother, Chheang Chentha, 50, who was staying at the scene, was a coffee maker and her sister, who asked not to be named, suffered severe injuries to her face, mouth and body.
According to the mother of the victim, she described with tears in her eyes that before the incident, the suspect, who was a child, worked as a construction worker, earning 230,000 Riels and giving 130,000 Riels to his mother before the National Assembly election. National level.
