Preah Vihear CamControl Officers Seize Outdated Goods for Sale at Ban Chey Market and Angkar AIDS Market in Choam Ksan District
(Preah Vihear): In order to protect food safety as well as the health of the people, this morning, September 10, 2018, CamControl Preah Vihear Branch led by Mr. Duong Mony, President of CamControl Provincial Branch in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and local authorities inspected the goods. Which are sold in various markets including Ban Jay Market and Angkar AIDS Market in Kantuot Commune, Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province.
Mr. Duong Mony said that as a result of the actual inspection, the branch team found outdated goods such as 16.69 kg of cakes, 67,715 liters of orange juice, 7.5 liters of cooking oil, fish sauce. 7.75 liters of syrup, 2.13 liters of fresh milk, 2.695 liters. At the same time, the branch team confiscated from the business owner to burn it.
Mr. Duong Mony also advised the traders to be aware of the import and sale at food safety, and he also emphasized that goods that are out of date are not required to be displayed for sale. To customers.
