Spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice: It is the discretion of the Investigating Judge on health grounds to decide on the provisional release of Kem Sokha, as well as the mandatory rules to be enforced.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Justice, on September 10, 2018, stated that the decision to temporarily release Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the Cambodia National Rescue Party, is at the discretion of Investigating judges on health grounds as well as mandatory rules to be followed.
Mr. Kim Santepheap said: “Both the family and the lawyer of the accused Kem Sokha mentioned the health reasons to apply for bail. "The decision on this request is within the jurisdiction of the investigating judge, as it sees fit in its discretion in the legal process."
"In the event that the investigating judge deems that health reasons are a necessary factor that requires the accused to be released on bail, the investigating judge must decide at that time. "The decision to grant bail sets out some of the obligatory rules that the accused must comply with, and the proceedings of this criminal case proceed normally in accordance with the criminal procedure in force."
It should be noted that Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the Cambodia National Rescue Party, was released on bail at dawn on September 10, 2018 due to his health problems after being detained in Trapeang Phlong Prison. 3) For more than 1 year.
