BERLIN: Germany could join air strikes with the United States, Britain and France if Syrian government forces resume use of chemical weapons against civilians in Idlib province. This is according to local media quoted by Sputnik on Monday afternoon, September 10, 2018.
According to the German newspaper Bild, the German Defense Ministry is currently considering options for retaliation in the event that Syrian government forces use chemical weapons against civilians again. There have also been the use of tornado fighter jets to attack government forces in Bashar al-Assad.
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of September 10, 2018, Mr. HIM Chhem, Senior Minister, Minister of Cults and Religions, presided over the celebration of National Literacy Day on September 08, 2018 at the Ministry of Cults and Religions organized by the General Department of Religious Affairs. Of the Ministry of Cults and Religions.
On that occasion, the Minister instructed the whole ceremony to implement the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the occasion of the National Literacy Day, September 08, 2018, eight recommendations, including:
First, the relevant ministries and institutions must develop the necessary policies, frameworks, standards, norms and mechanisms to lead, manage and implement effectively and quality to ensure access to lifelong learning for all people and in line with the new environment. Sustainable development goals.
Second, all ministries and institutions, educational institutions, and study centers and pagodas must develop lifelong learning programs in both literacy and vocational training to be more diverse and flexible to meet the needs of students to provide lifelong educational services. Non-formal and informal education services for all people.
Third, local authorities at all levels must pay more attention to support the development of learning centers, infrastructure and learning facilities, as well as encourage people who have not studied or dropped out of school to have the opportunity to learn. Again, in all forms of non-formal education programs, in particular, efforts must be made to make it easier for people with disabilities to have access to education.
Fourth: All media.
Sixth, pagodas and temples should be joined by the movement of monks, clergy, and nuns to promote the professional literacy program even more by educating people about the importance of learning about morality and promoting a culture of universal citizenship. Techo Hun Sen sends message to Swiss President on the death of Dr. Beat Richner
