Ministry of Social Affairs Holds Discussion with Partners to Strengthen Prevention and Care of HIV and AIDS Victims
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has held workshops with a number of relevant partner organizations to strengthen the protection and care of victims of HIV / AIDS and other important issues to understand the shortcomings and work. Improved service delivery to be more efficient.
A workshop to review the progress report for the first half of 2018 and the implementation direction of the Committee for Combating AIDS of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation was held on September 10, 2018 at the Ministry of Social Affairs. Mr. Chheang Bak, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Social Affairs, officials of the Ministry of Social Affairs, together with the chairpersons of other relevant organizations.
Speaking at the seminar, Mr. Chheang Bak, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs, thanked the National AIDS Authority and the Ministry of Social Affairs' HIV / AIDS Committee and partner organizations for including people living with HIV in vulnerable groups. Especially to get social protection and support good ideas that raise the need for strategic and systematic linkages.
Mr. Chheang Bak said that in today's workshop, the importance of responding to the stigma and human rights of people living with HIV and other affected people in the context of social protection and outreach was also highlighted. Let the committee members and partner organizations know about the 4th National Comprehensive Strategy to Fight AIDS, 2015-2020.
Mr. Chheang Bak added that in this workshop, they also raised the topic of learning, understanding the experience of partner organizations and understanding the shortcomings in order to improve in providing more efficient services. There is also the implementation of the resolution issued by the decision of the National Authority for Combating AIDS in the past.
The Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs said that this discussion will bring good ideas or inputs that can enable us to understand the positives and negatives of the past and make better improvements. Contributing to the fight against AIDS.
Mr. Chhour Sopanha added that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has paid special attention to the causes of victims of HIV, AIDS and other vulnerable people by designing and implementing guidelines. Many strategic policies focus on the prevention and care of victims of HIV and AIDS.
Dr. Hor Bunleng added that the National AIDS Authority will continue to strengthen cooperation with the Ministry of Social Affairs and other partner organizations to reduce the number of people affected by HIV and AIDS in Cambodia, regardless of Assist in human resources, materials and budget, as well as techniques.
Journalists from the four countries assessed the visit as having greatly enhanced ties and explored each other's cultures as countries with villages and fences. In addition, CLMV journalists thanked Air Asia for organizing the event and other sponsors and partners.
