WeFran Restaurant Owners Give Over $ 3,000 Gifts to Customers Celebrating 12 Years
(Phnom Penh): So far, WeFran Restaurant has been open for 12 years and has expanded its branches. To celebrate and give some special gifts to customers, the restaurant owner said that the restaurant has prepared special gifts worth more than $ 3,000 to customers.
According to Mr. Cheng Vanna, this is the 12th year that the restaurant has opened due to the support of the people, which has led the restaurant to expand its branch so far. And in terms of the 12th anniversary program, more than 100 male and female stars attended and many guests were present.
Mr. Cheng Vanna said that in order to celebrate the 12th anniversary and to give gifts to customers, he organized a raffle for customers with a total of more than $ 3,000. And when he is free from organizing this event, he and the artist plan to continue to do more charity work, because what he does is what he always does every year.
Driving must not violate the speed limit! 5 killed and 12 injured in traffic accidents nationwide on September 9 yesterday
(Phnom Penh): According to the report from the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police, on September 9, 2018, there were eight traffic accidents nationwide, resulting in five deaths. Three were slightly injured and nine were seriously injured.
According to the same source, in these 8 traffic accidents, 9 motorcycles, 2 trucks and 4 cars were damaged, and the causes of the accidents were: speeding, negligence Right, disrespecting vehicle rights and factors.
In the past nine days, there have been 65 traffic accidents, resulting in 30 deaths, 76 serious injuries and 31 minor injuries.
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen led the first delegation abroad after the formation of the Royal Government to participate in the 15th China-ASEAN Expo in Nanning, China.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at 8 am on September 10, 2018, will lead a high-level delegation to go abroad for the first time after the new Royal Government was formed only 4 days to attend the ceremony. 15th China-ASEAN Expo in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the 15th China-ASEAN Expo will be held under the theme "Building the 21st Century Maritime Silk Road and Innovating China-ASEAN Community" to Promote Private Sector Cooperation in Cambodia. In trade, business, investment and tourism for the better.
As the honorary chairman of the opening ceremony, the Prime Minister will deliver a keynote address at the 15th China-ASEAN Expo, aimed at boosting trade and investment between ASEAN and China, as well as attracting potential Chinese investors and tourists. Hold the ASEAN region.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Deputy Prime Minister Han Zheng will preside over the ribbon-cutting ceremony for the inauguration of the Cambodian National Pavilion, as well as visit the Cambodia Trade Fair Hall.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during his stay in China, the Prime Minister will hold separate talks with Chinese dignitaries and receive courtesy calls from Guangxi provincial leaders and key business leaders and executives. Of Chinese companies as well as giving interviews to Chinese media.
Notably, the China-ASEAN Expo is held annually with the aim of further deepening and expanding business and trade opportunities to achieve the goal of investing 1 trillion US dollars from China to ASEAN and $ 150 billion from ASEAN to China by 2020
The Prime Minister also stressed that the China-ASEAN Expo will not only provide opportunities for heads of state, government, leaders, Chinese entrepreneurs and all ASEAN member countries, but also exchange views to strengthen and expand trade and investment. Not only that, but it is also a forum that contributes to strengthening bilateral and multilateral cooperation and increasing trade opportunities between countries participating in exhibitions in all fields.
It should be noted that after completing the exhibition in China, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will lead a delegation to Hanoi, Vietnam to attend the World Economic Forum one day before flying back to Cambodia. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's trip abroad today is the first trip for Samdech and his delegation after the new Royal Government was formed, but not new for Samdech in 2018. Overall, in 2018, Samdech Techo has led the delegation to attend five important meetings abroad already.
Separately, at Kantha Bopha Hospital, a memorial service was held for him at the library in Kantha Bopha Hospital on the same day.
