No fishing during the spawning season! Central Fisheries Administration Officials Continue to Crack Down on Fishing Offenses and Break Over Illegal Mosquito Networks and Burn in Leuk Dek District
(Kandal): Mr. Vit Thearith, Director of Fisheries District, Kandal Province, on September 9, 2018, led a joint force to cross the multi-kilometer mosquito net that was smuggled by corrupt fishermen along the Vietnam-Cambodia border. On the surface of the water from one shore to the other during the off-season, the spawning grounds fall into the nets of the illegal fishermen.
Mr. Vit Thearith said that under the guidance of Dr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province, he led the force in cooperation with the Leuk Dek District Authority and the Armed Forces, and with the participation of the Sanda community, to crack down on illegal mosquito nets. In small lakes and large lakes.
As a result, the force dissected hundreds of mosquito nets and hundreds of meters of mosquito nets, removed thousands of poles, burned them and released hundreds of kilograms of fish. Illegal fishing must be turned back to legal fishing, otherwise when the force comes down, the message will be burned like now, because fishing with nets causes the most serious damage to natural resources.
