(Prey Veng): Not different from the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister always said, "Where there is suffering, there is always the face of the Cambodian People's Party" on September 9, 2018, the party working group Cambodian people in Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province, led by Mr. Steung Sokhom, the team leader, intervened to fertilize three canals and irrigate 554 hectares of rice that are suffering from drought.
According to the report of Smaong Tbong commune chief, the drought situation started during the election campaign and Kamchay Mear district has never experienced a drought, only this year suddenly there was a drought and lasted longer than any other year. All.
After listening to the report of the commune chief, Mr. Steung Sokhom led an urgent study team to find a source of water that could be used to draw water to help all the rice that is suffering from drought and the means to bring water to the fields. Also.
Due to the lack of canals in Smaong Tbong commune, which brings water from the main canal through, causing farmers to lack water sources for irrigating their fields, Mr. Steng Sokhom urged district and commune officials to rent excavators to dig three drainage canals. There is a mouth of 2 meters, a depth of 1 meter and a bottom of 1 meter, a length of 4,400 meters to draw water to the drought-stricken rice fields at a cost of more than 13 million riels, which is his own budget and his team.
Helping the farmers to bring water to save their rice has brought great happiness to many farmers' families in Kamchay Mear district. They also thanked and commended the team for their efforts to address their concerns.
On the same day, Mr. Steng Sokhom also inspected the canal that was digging to drain the water to the farmers' fields and urged the digging of this canal to be done as soon as possible.
The working group leader also met immediately with Kamchay Mear district and commune officials to check the drought situation in Kamchay Mear district. During the meeting, the President listened to the reports of each commune affected by the drought and provided emergency assistance to some communes, and he asked the district to make efforts to contact the provinces to request the intervention of water pumps. Save people's rice.
Mr. Steng Sokhom expressed his condolences to the people affected by the drought and promised to solve this problem in time.
In the afternoon of the same day, the team leader also continued to Seang Khwang commune, a commune affected by drought. Here, 867 hectares of paddy fields are affected and need urgent assistance to bring water to the rescue.
There, Mr. So Khon Rithykun, the head of the central working group to help Seang Khwang commune, said that he had intervened to restore a 2,000-meter-long canal from the main canal to farmers' fields and installed drainage. Along 4 roads to open the water.
