On behalf of the Commander of the Kampong Thom Military Operation Area, President of the Kampong Thom Cambodian Veterans Association, Major General Som Sun stated that this is a consideration for the honor and gratitude of the veterans for their valuable sacrifices. Cause of nation, motherland and people.
He added that the working group of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Kampong Thom province is determined to continue to go to the grassroots to serve the people twice as much, regardless of hardship, and would like to express our deep gratitude to Samdech Techo. Paying attention to the living standards and honor of the army, veterans, veterans, victims and families of the army.
It should be noted that the working group of Kampong Thom Veterans Association paid attention to the active activities of the Veterans Association in Kampong Thom province with high morale and high values by visiting the well-being of veterans and interviewing them. Satisfied and provided food, care, facilitation treatment.
In particular, the association has helped build houses for 95 needy veterans, which are the gifts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and the leaders of the Cambodian Veterans Association. As well as other philanthropists. General Mak Chito confirms the operation to crack down on drug crimes in nightclubs in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, received the drug work plan on September 08, 2018, came out to explain and confirm the operation to crack down on drug crimes at nightclubs in Phnom Penh.
Under the direct direction of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chief of Campaign, and Chief of General Staff Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, as Chief of the Secretariat of the Campaign, National Police Force, Military Police, Local Authorities The masses have been active in preventing and cracking down on illegal drugs.
In the three campaigns, law enforcement forces and the military police cracked down on 13,491 drug offenses, arrested 15,796 suspects and confiscated more than 668 kilograms of drugs. Authorities sent 4,717 drug addicts to temporary centers for treatment and rehabilitation.
"Dozens of drug traffickers, both Cambodian and foreign, have been arrested and jailed, and some are being sought by court orders and the International Police Red Cross," said General Mak Chito. "This is a huge success of the campaign, which has the support and active participation of both the national and international public."
Samdech Krala Hom still pays attention to the work of preventing and cracking down on drug crimes, especially the abuse of drugs in entertainment venues, especially entertainment clubs. Samdech has set out two measures to implement, including:
First: Preventive education measures:
* Strive to guide and explain to all site owners to understand the guilt of committing drug offenses and allow crimes to occur in their locations. Its location * The owner of the location must sign a contract with the authorities.
Second, if the owners of those locations continue to commit crimes or allow crimes to occur in their locations, the owners of the locations will face penalties:
* Revoke the license, stop the business, close the location * Send to court to punish according to law.
General Mak Chito confirmed that, in general, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, the campaign leader, intends to use educational measures as a priority by educating all site owners to wake up and eliminate drug offenses at their locations, and if not, That will have to use the rules of law enforcement, research, repression, this does not mean that not repression, but the repression in the big picture and at the same time.
