Samdech Techo Hun Sen Urges All Relevant Ministries and Institutions to Continue the Promotion of Literacy in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, called on all relevant ministries and institutions to continue to promote literacy in Cambodia. This is according to the message of Samdech Techo on the occasion of National Literacy Day, September 08, 2018.
First, the relevant ministries and institutions must develop the necessary policies, legal frameworks, standards and mechanisms to lead, manage and implement effectively and quality to ensure access to lifelong learning for all people and in line with the new goals. Sustainable development.
Second, all ministries, institutions, educational institutions, study centers, and pagodas must develop lifelong learning programs in both literacy and vocational training to be more diverse and flexible to meet the needs of students to provide lifelong learning services and services. Education in the non-formal and informal education system for all people.
Third, local authorities at all levels must pay more attention to support the development of learning centers, infrastructure and learning facilities, as well as encourage people who do not study or drop out of school to have the opportunity to learn. Again, in all forms of non-formal education programs, in particular, efforts must be made to make it easier for people with disabilities to have access to education.
Fourth, all media, including radio, television, newspapers, magazines, public and private newsletters, help spread the word about the importance of literacy so that our people can better understand literacy. Go to study for life.
Sixth, pagodas and temples should be joined by the movement of monks, clergy, and nuns to promote professional literacy programs by educating them about the importance of learning about morality and promoting a culture of universal citizenship.
Seventh, development partners and non-governmental organizations need to increase cooperation and strengthen partnerships to support programs, especially literacy programs linked to vocational education to run smoothly.
8th: The President of Factories, Enterprises and Private Companies, please cooperate and create conditions for opening literacy classes, combined with vocational training for workers, for their own benefit and for the benefit of factory owners. We all need to remember that "literacy, right thinking and decision making", "literacy leads to national economic growth", "literacy, harmony of individual and social life".
Samdech Techo stated that this year, the National Literacy Day on September 8 was celebrated under the theme "Literacy Towards Lifelong Learning" with the vision of developing all Cambodians to have lifelong learning opportunities anytime, anywhere. And all means of professionalism, skills, fitness, behavior, fitness and fitness to contribute to the economic and social well-being of individuals and society.
The concept of this topic is not only to learn literacy and numeracy, but also to consider the opportunity to gain knowledge, entrepreneurship, professional skills and innovation in all fields, especially literacy and technology, which is currently growing rapidly. The Cambodian Association of Higher Education Institutions presents a report on “Observing the 6th National Assembly Election”
