Minister of National Defense: The appointment of Hun Manet as Army Chief is most appropriate, because he is capable, not because of his father's influence (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Minister of National Defense, emphasized that the appointment of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Commander-in-Chief of the Army, is the most deserving, and this appointment is not because of his father's influence as Prime Minister, but because Hun Manet is competent enough to work in the army.
The confirmation of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh was made at the ceremony of promotion and change of position of three top commanders of Cambodia on the afternoon of September 7, 2018 at the Peace Palace. The defense chief claimed that all troops of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces were satisfied and supportive of the appointment of Hun Manet as commander of the army.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to change three top commanders, including: The Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces has been replaced by General Pol Saroeun, replaced by General Vong Pisen, and Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, replaced by General Kun Kim. Replaced by General Ith Sarath, the Army Commander was replaced by General Meas Sophea, replaced by Lt. Gen. Hun Manet.
Mr. Hun Manet is the eldest son of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and joined the army in 1995. Hun Manet was the first Cambodian to receive a scholarship to study at West Point Military Academy in the United States and graduated in 1999. In addition to graduating from the Military Academy, he also holds a Master's degree in Economics from the University of New York and a PhD from the University of the United Kingdom.
Mr. Hun Manet has extensive work experience in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. He was appointed Commander of the Counter-Terrorism Force in 2008 with high responsibility for building the capacity of the Counter-Terrorism Forces.
Mr. Hun Manet is a military officer who has been heavily involved in military work, both in terms of military capacity building as well as work related to the strengthening of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, which is an important institution in defending territorial integrity, independence and national sovereignty. Regarding Mars exploration, NASA is organizing a contest where candidates can win millions of dollars ...
