(Phnom Penh): Workers of "Jim Ly" factory located in Trapeang Toul village, Sangkat Kampol, Khan Por Senchey, more than 500 workers out of a total of 2,500 workers gathered this morning, September 7, 2018 on National Road No. Four Commanders-in-Chief of the Army to march to the National Assembly demanding help find a solution after the factory termination of the lease, the location will be relocated without payment of other benefits at the end of the year.
The protests of factory workers for almost a month and still do not end until the morning of September 7, workers gathered to march to the National Assembly.
According to the workers, the factory was renamed "Jim Lee" to "Gigi" but the company has not yet paid the workers' benefits, leaving 2,500 workers unhappy. Protest for money at the end of the year and other benefits.
