TOP NEWS: The King issued a Royal Decree ordering the appointment of a new cabinet after receiving a vote of confidence from the National Assembly
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on September 6, 2018, issued a Royal Decree appointing the composition of the Council of Ministers for a new term after receiving a vote of confidence from the National Assembly. And sworn in.
The new cabinet consists of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister, accompanied by 10 Deputy Prime Ministers, 17 Senior Ministers and 29 Ministers. The composition of the Royal Government of the 6th mandate does not have the Secretary of State like the 5th mandate. Three new Deputy Prime Ministers have been appointed, including Prak Sokhon, Aun Porn Moniroth and Chea Sophara. The number of senior ministers increased from 15 to 17.
In addition, participants can register to play a variety of games for free, such as: fruit eating contest, decorating cakes, making juice, smoothies, snacks and drinks to win a lot of prizes.
(Takeo): Many job opportunities for residents of Takeo province from the job forum program of Takeo Provincial Job Center on September 11, 2018, which is co-organized by Techo Sen Takeo Regional Polytechnic Institute and YAZAKI factory in Koh Kong special economic zone, which is in urgent need of recruiting workers.
Mr. Huy Lux, President of Takeo Provincial Job Center, stated that "the purpose of organizing this job forum to help the unemployed, especially for the people in Takeo can get job opportunities and a decent salary to support their families." Mr. Huy Lux also called on young people, especially those who are looking for work, to come and apply for a face-to-face interview with representatives from these factories.
Previously, the Takeo Provincial Job Center was part of the National Employment Agency of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which is responsible for finding jobs for people and recruiting for companies, factories and enterprises in Takeo.
It should be noted that the National Employment Agency (TEC) is an institution under the National Training Committee of the Office of the Council of Ministers. The NCCC was established by Sub-Decree No. 67 dated 27 April 2009 with the aim of promoting the provision of quality and effective labor market information services to provide employment opportunities for employers. And education and training providers have access to information from each other.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for September 6, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 2,387 vehicles and found 562 vehicles violating the law (81% motorcycles), 186 education vehicles and 376 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
