(Preah Vihear): The statue of Ta Suong or the Tbeng Mountain Shower was built at the roundabout in Kulen district to serve as a place of worship for the people. The construction is under the initiative of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and has been funded by many philanthropists.
According to Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province and the recipient of the construction of the statue of Ta Suong, said that the construction of the statue of Ta Suong or the wall of Phnom Tbeng is under The initiative of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, and the budget for this construction is part of the budget of the Governor and his family and his own budget, and also the participation of many philanthropists.
Mr. Samleang Try said that the construction of the statue of Grandpa Suong was started in April 2018 and is scheduled to be completed by the end of September 2018.
