Pailin Longan Community produces more than 5,000 tons of longan fruit per year, an increase of 30% every year
(Pailin): According to the 3rd General Assembly 2018 of Mien Pailin Agricultural Community, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Pursat, Mr. Sreng Sreang, President of Mien Pailin Association said on September 6, 2018 that Pailin longan farming community produced 5,590 tons in 2017 and the yield increased by more than 30% every year to supply both domestic and foreign markets.
Mr. Sok Sathim, Advisor of the Ministry of Commerce and Director of the Department of Commerce, said that currently the amount of longan in Pailin province is increasing every year, so the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the Ministry of Commerce itself is helping to facilitate and pave the way. Export Pailin lentils to sell directly to China without going through Thailand, such as signing an MOU between the two countries and enacting SPS phytosanitary standards.
