(Phnom Penh): A man was arrested by the police last week after beating his wife every day for the past four years, until she could not stand it and complained to the police to arrest him.
But later, because of the feelings between the couple for many years, she forgave him and only asked the police to help educate and make a contract to stop the violence and then released.
On the other hand, after his release, he did not give up even a little, but continued to beat his wife mercilessly, so his wife died and complained to the police for a second arrest and asked the police to take action. By law.
The husband was arrested on September 6, 2018 in Room 42 in Choam Chao 2 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the Chaom Chao 2 Police Station, the brutal husband, 23-year-old Chhay Chenda, is unemployed and lives in Room 42 in the above village and was born in Chamkar Leu Village, Svay Teap Commune, Chamkar Leu District, Kampong Cham Province. His wife, Bu Hong, 22, is a garment factory worker who lives in a rented house.
The suspect was arrested by the police after his wife filed a complaint on August 30, 2018, police said. She claimed that her husband had repeatedly beaten her for the past four years. However, after the arrest at the Chaom Chao police station, the wife only asked for education and made a contract to stop the violence and asked the police to release her husband without filing a complaint.
The source added that at that time, the police agreed and released him after educating and signing a contract. But so far, it has only been one week.
According to the authorities, the suspect did not change his ways, beat his wife and was arrested again by the police. And this time may not have the same fate as before, because his wife asked the police to deal with the law. Affect health! Tbong Khmum Cam Control Officer Continues to Inspect the Quality of Goods at Market
