WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US President Donald Trump on Wednesday warned against shutting down the federal government, in stark contrast to his previous stance on the idea of shutting down the federal government. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday afternoon, September 6, 2018.
"If it happens, it will happen and if it involves border security, I will not do anything," Donald Trump told reporters. Tram's remarks come ahead of a meeting with US congressional leaders on how to proceed with the congressional agenda for the coming months, including raising funds for the federal government, which expires on This September 30th.
The US Congress is currently working on approving the budget for the fiscal year, which begins on October 1. But Tram is expected to be forced to partially shut down the federal government in October if he opposes the budget.
