Police crack down on drug traffickers and send them to Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court
(Banteay Meanchey): Major General At Cam, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, led the police force of the Anti-Drug Bureau and the Police Force of the Office of Prevention and Intervention and the O'Chrov District Police Force to crack down on drug trafficking and use cases.
This operation took place at 9:10 AM on September 4, 2018 in Sala Krahorm Village (Yeang Thmey Village), Kob Commune, O'Chrov District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Ngeng Sochea, director of the Anti-Drug Police Office, said on September 5 that the suspect was Pet Sarom, a 27-year-old man living in Sala Krahorm village (Yeang Thmey village), Kob commune, O'Chrov district, Banteay Meanchey province. This person, along with the subject of consumption and trafficking, is also the subject of active fishing.
He said that the police searched the suspect's house and found two small bags of methamphetamine ICE weighing 11.10 grams, a plastic pistol, a mobile phone, a drug scale, a trigger. 2, 1 samurai sword and some other packaging materials and 2 banknotes to buy medicine.
According to the suspect's confession, the drugs were bought from a person in Thailand for 500,000 riel per bag. For money, they follow Wing and Trumani and sell the medicine in the village. This is the first time he has been arrested by the police.
The suspect was sent to the provincial court by the specialized police force to prepare the case file and proceed with the procedure.
