The following are the full oaths that all members of the National Assembly will be recited by the King Father:
We, the President, the Vice President and the Members of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, take the oath of office in the presence of the King, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach and Tevata Reaksa Svet Chhat.
In carrying out our duties and in fulfilling the mission entrusted to us by the people of Cambodia, we are committed to respecting the Constitution, serving both now and in the future for the benefit of the people. People, nation and motherland of Cambodia. We swear that we will not exploit the national interest for our own or for our family or for our party or for our own party.
We are determined to sacrifice our lives to protect both now and in the future the full independence of the motherland of Cambodia, the full national sovereignty, the legitimate territorial integrity in the land and sea borders that Cambodia once had. Generations from 1963 to 1969 were united and did not allow any division or separatism.
We are committed to maintaining neutrality and non-alignment for Cambodia, both now and in the future, and will not allow anyone who wants to interfere in the internal affairs of Cambodia or to give orders to Cambodia's national and international policy.
We do not serve foreign interests and do not harm the interests of the people, the nation and the motherland of Cambodia. In resolving national and international issues, we will completely eliminate all forms of violence. However, the Kingdom of Cambodia reserves the right to bear arms and fight against foreign aggression in order to defend its homeland.
We are committed to upholding, both now and in the future, a liberal, multi-party and multi-party democracy, as well as a strong respect for human rights, as enshrined in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.
We are determined to fight against all kinds of corruption, against social injustice, and to fight for national reconciliation, for national unity, for social peace and national peace, for the prosperity of the Cambodian people and for maintaining the glorious prosperity of the motherland of Cambodia. Respect, reverence and love of all of us.
(Kampong Cham): The police force of Kampong Cham Provincial Police on September 05, 2018 continued to crack down on illegal fishing in Koh Sotin district.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal said that the operation took place after he received information about illegal fishing and ordered Mr. Im Khoeun, Koh Sotin District Police Inspector, in cooperation with the police, the administration and the Special Intervention Force. Led by Mr. Lor Seang Huot, Deputy Inspector in Charge of Drugs, cracked down on illegal fishing at Prek Pong and behind Pong commune, Mohaleap commune, Koh Sotin district.
According to the General Commissioner, as a result, the specialized force confiscated 15 nets, 1,020 meters of barriers, 258 bamboo poles and released 215 kilograms of mixed fish into the natural lake.
The exhibits were burned on the spot with the approval of the Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court. For the mosquito net, it was transported and stored at Koh Sotin District Hall.
