Ministry of Economy, in collaboration with Asia-Europe University, organizes a workshop to disseminate the Law on Accounting and Auditing
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance and Asia Europe University on September 05, 2018 co-organized a seminar to disseminate the Law on Accounting and Auditing to the Management, Staff, Professors and Students at the Conference Hall of Lower Asia Europe University. Mr. Bou Tharin, Secretary General of the National Accounting Council, represented Mr. Ngy Tayi, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Accounting Council.
Dr. Chea Sopheap, Rector of Asia-Europe University, stated that the purpose of this workshop was to share important knowledge related to accounting and auditing law to the management, staff, faculty and students for the purpose of linking Theory to practice in working society.
Mr. Bou Tharin stated that the Law on "Accounting and Auditing" has many advantages and advantages, such as:
1) Increase the transparency and accuracy of accounting documents and financial statements of public institutions and enterprises, which can increase public trust in government institutions and enterprises, as well as the confidence of local and foreign investors.
2) Promote accountability and good governance of public institutions and enterprises
3) - Improve the quality and capacity of human resources as accountants and auditors and improve the accounting and auditing profession.
4) - Promote and sustain the sustainability of the capital market and create conditions for small and medium enterprises to be able to participate in the capital market
5) - Support the possibility of obtaining credit
6) -Improve the efficiency of tax collection for the state
7) -Create jobs for people.
The Secretary General of the National Accounting Council emphasized that at present, there is a shortage of accounting and auditing professionals in Cambodia for accounting, auditing for companies and auditing by units or businesses. All students must strive to excel and apply their accounting professional knowledge to meet the needs of the job market.
