(Phnom Penh): In the first session of the National Assembly in the new mandate held at the invitation of the King of Cambodia this morning, September 5, 2018, there were representatives of diplomats from 22 countries and representatives of 5 major international organizations. Most of them under the auspices of the United Nations were present at the invitation of the Cambodian side, while the other nine embassies did not attend.
Most of the participating diplomats in Asia, while some Western countries such as Australia, Sweden, Bulgaria, Europe, the United States, Canada, France, Germany and the United Kingdom did not attend and respond to the invitation.
Leng Penglong, secretary-general and spokesman for the National Assembly, confirmed to reporters that Cambodia had invited 31 embassies in Cambodia to attend the first session of parliament in the new term, but only 22 embassies attended. The other nine did not respond to the invitation.
The National Assembly spokesman did not know why the representatives of those countries did not attend yet, and expressed regret over the absence of the diplomats. "We regret that Cambodia wants good relations with all countries, and Cambodia has been trying to implement and develop democracy since 1993, but our efforts have had many difficulties and obstacles," he said. This road.
"The West does not properly assess the situation in Cambodia. If they want Cambodia to be like the West, it cannot be done immediately because Cambodia does not have the same traditions as the West," he said. "So, as much as we strive to practice democracy, we should celebrate."
As in previous mandates, in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the opening of the first session of the new legislature of the National Assembly on September 5 took place under the presidency of the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. In addition to the 125 members of the National Assembly, the opening of the first session was also attended by ambassadors and ambassadors of various countries to Cambodia.
The opening ceremony of the first session today begins at 8 am. After the opening ceremony of the first session, the opening session of the first session began its work under the chairmanship of Mr. Heng Samrin, Senator of the National Assembly, to decide on the validity of the mandate of each member and the approval of the internal regulations of the National Assembly for the sixth term.
