The Ministry of Labor instructs establishments that employ foreign employees for 2019 to apply for quotas from September 1 to November 30.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a notification instructing the owners or directors of enterprises and institutions that need to use foreign labor for 2019 to apply for a permit to use foreign labor (quota) from 1 month. September to November 30, 2018.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News on September 5, the Ministry of Labor has also ordered the owners or directors of enterprises and institutions that use foreign labor for 2019, as well as all foreigners doing business in Cambodia. Must complete the form to extend the validity of the card or work book of foreigners for 2019 from January 1 to March 31, 2019.
In addition to stating the cost of public services related to the use of foreign labor, the notice also states legal measures and penalties: In accordance with this announcement, the Ministry will take measures to implement the penalties in accordance with the provisions of Chapter 16 of the Labor Law.
The Ministry of Labor also called on the owners or directors of enterprises, establishments and all foreigners to implement this notice effectively.
