Mr. Bou Bun Chhean, Police Inspector of O'Raing District, confirmed that the accident occurred when a truck carrying pepper carrying more than 10 people traveling from Memot District arrived at the scene down the slope of the bridge and oversteered to hit the head. The bridge overturned and plunged into a deep ravine, killing two people on the spot and seriously injuring two others and slightly injuring 10 others.
