Stung Treng Provincial Armed Forces and Forestry Administration continue operation to crack down on forest crime on the Mekong River in Stung Treng City, confiscate some luxury wood
(Stung Treng): The Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie in cooperation with the Forestry Administration on the afternoon of September 4, 2018, cracked down on forest crime on the Mekong River at Wat Khok Suon, Hang Kho Suon Village, Samaki Village, Stung Treng City. .
Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie Commander Brigadier General Ieng Vandy told Fresh News that the operation was carried out in accordance with the order of General Sao Sokha, Acting Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie. The country should crack down on all illegal crimes in the territory it occupies.
According to the commander in the crackdown, special forces seized a boat loaded with 32 pieces of heavy rosewood (not yet measured), but the suspect escaped.
After the crackdown, all the exhibits were handed over to the Forestry Administration to be stored to build a case for legal action.
