Changlorfang Forest Park is located on Guangzhou Road, at the intersection of Sichuan and Fengtai Districts in Beijing, China. Unlike ordinary parks, this forest park has a variety of trees and flowers. The landscapes are also designed to international standards, with trees of different heights and shapes that make people walk in the park feel like they are walking in a small forest instead of Walking in the city.
The Guangzhou Road Office started clearing rubbish and managing construction for the area in late 2017 to turn the land into a forest park for its current decoration.
In addition, Chang Lofeng, Beijing, plans to establish a total of 21 forest parks by 2018. Beijing is trying to improve the quality of life of its people by providing more places to visit and improving the beauty of the city's environment. (China's CCTV)
The bridge connects Maldives, the capital of the Maldives, with the island of Hulhule, the Maldives' main international airport.
This 2 km long bridge allows locals and tourists to travel between the two islands in just 5 minutes.
Maldives President Abdul Layamin and a delegation from the Chinese government and head of the China Agency for International Development Cooperation Wang Xiaotao attended the opening ceremony.
President Yamin expressed his gratitude to the Chinese government for helping build the Maldives' first sea bridge, and said he believed the bridge would be more convenient for the people of the Maldives.
Artists from both countries also attended the opening ceremony.
