Draft Royal Decree on the Establishment of the "Supreme Advisory Council" was unanimously approved by all 16 parties
(Phnom Penh): On September 4, 2018, the draft Royal Decree on the Establishment of the "Supreme Advisory Council" was unanimously approved by all 16 parties at a discussion meeting at the Peace Palace. Led by Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin.
This draft Royal Decree has 7 chapters and 21 articles and will be sent to Samdech Prime Minister Hun Sen for consideration and decision to submit to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia for official signing.
The "Supreme Advisory Council" is another new mechanism to respond to the interests of the people as a whole, which is not in the interests of the Royal Government, and the presidents of all political parties participating in the consultation. Also announced full support for this initiative.
