According to Major General Pol Ratana, Deputy Director of the Criminal Police Department and the leader of the robbery force, according to the suspect's confession, the group had robbed more than 350 motorcycles. They stole and robbed more than 350 vehicles were cracked down on by the light criminal police.
The last time they robbed a motorbike just after midnight on August 30, 2018 in Veal Vong Sangkat, Khan 7 Makara. The active target of the robbery in Phnom Penh was Keo Sarin, a 28-year-old male (with drugs), along with nearly 10 other fugitives.
Lt. Gen. Pol Ratana said that their activities have three images: if you see a good opportunity, they steal motorcycles and sometimes use the image as a motorcycle riding in a crowd, causing conflict with the victims. The robbers chased each other to confuse the neighbors and then took the opportunity to run away from the motorcycle. They took the victim's motorcycle and fled. .
