According to the report of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, during the period when the sky continued to rain daily for almost 3 months, the roads in Ratanakkiri province were damaged, including:
National Road No. 76, a DBST paved road in Lumphat district, was severely damaged by rain for 3 months, 2.5 km long, but the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport repaired 2 km. And is undergoing ongoing repairs.
National Road No. 76, AC and DBST paved road in O'Yadao district, was severely damaged by rain for 3 months, 1.5 km long, but the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport has already repaired 1 Km and is undergoing ongoing repairs.
3. Provincial Road No. 3785, a red gravel road in Wensai district, was severely damaged by rain for 3 months, 8 km long, but the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport has already repaired 1 km and is Continue repairs.
4: Provincial Road No. 3RK1, a red gravel road in Ta Veng district, was severely damaged by rain for 3 months, 7 km long, but the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport repaired 2 km. And is continuing to repair.
Letter to readers: Fisheries officials in Kandeang district, Pursat province, and officials ordered the owners of fishing offenses to pay in return for not cracking down.
(Pursat): Recently, Mr. Lim Sokret, Chief of Kandeang Fisheries Administration Sangkat, and his colleagues went to crack down on fishing crimes at Srey Chak fishing community in Koh Kaek and Prek Trabek communes in Reang Til and Kanh commune, Kandieng district. Pursat Province.
