The opening ceremony of the technical skills training campaign was held under the leadership of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chair of the Capacity Building Working Group and Leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Ministries and Institutions, and was attended by Ms. Camilla Lombard. ) Deputy Chair of the European Union Cooperation Team in Cambodia and representatives of relevant development partners and a total of 450 participants.
The event is coordinated by the Institute of Economics and Finance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and the actual training process will take place at the Institute of Economics and Finance in the form of a technical curriculum lasting from 70-90 hours for Each course, which is a series of 21 courses from September 3, 2018 onwards.
At the same time, Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, emphasized that in the past 5 years, the Ministry has been successful in training and capacity building for the leadership and civil servants of the Ministry. Of the Royal Government on skills for public financial management, which are necessary for the implementation of public financial management reform.
At present, these human resources have been actively contributing to the implementation of roles and responsibilities in their respective units and have contributed to Cambodia to continue to maintain the credibility of the budget, which is essentially achieved in the phase. The first will be more successful in increasing financial accountability in the second phase of public financial management reform.
He said that the reform of public financial management is one of the key reform programs of the Royal Government under the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to ensure the success of the implementation of the national development policy agenda. Aims to improve the living standards of the people.
Currently, the reform of public financial management is in the third phase in order to increase the linkage of the budget to the priority policies of the Royal Government and to have more actors to implement, along with the transfer of ownership and responsibility. More and more to ministries and institutions in circumstances where human resource capacity is still limited, both knowledge, skills and willingness to participate.
This requires all ministries and institutions to pay more attention to strengthening the capacity, knowledge and awareness of "technical skills necessary for public financial management" for civil servants to ensure efficiency. Consistency and sustainability in the performance of roles and responsibilities, especially the implementation of program budgets and budget units, and the effective and sustainable implementation of information technology systems for public financial management.
