Meanwhile, Kim Sok, a political and social analyst in Cambodia who has just been released from prison, has fled to Thailand. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Director of the Counter-Terrorism and Transnational Crime Department of the National Police.
It should be noted that Mr. Kim Sok was released by the court on the morning of August 17, 2018, after completing his sentence, that is, he was imprisoned for about 18 months.
On August 10, 2017, Mr. Kim Sok was sentenced by the Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Ky Bithy, to 18 months imprisonment and fined 8 million Riel, plus 800 million Riel in compensation to the plaintiffs. Riel on charges of incitement to commit a crime.
The sentencing follows a lawsuit filed by the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) after Kim Sok incited and defamed the CPP as behind Kem Ley's assassination.
On August 29, 2018, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, strongly warned that he would sue social analyst Kim Sok and send him back to prison if he did not pay 800 million riel (approximately 20 million riel) in compensation. Ten thousand dollars to the Cambodian People's Party.
