(Kratie): The Anti-Drug Police Force of Tbong Khmum Province, in cooperation with the Anti-Drug Police Force of Snuol District, Kratie Province, launched an operation to crack down on drug trafficking and arrested a woman as the wife of the next suspect. From the husband escaped the shadows.
The operation was carried out on the evening of September 2, 2018 in Kronhung Sen Chey village, Kronhung Senchey commune, Snuol district, Kratie province.
According to the Snuol District Anti-Drug Police, the Tbong Khmum Provincial Anti-Drug Task Force has expanded its territory in cooperation with the Snuol District Anti-Drug Task Force of the Snuol District Police Inspectorate and under the direct command of Mr. Keo Socheat, Prosecutor. Kratie Provincial Court and Mr. Heang Sopheak, Prosecutor of Tbong Khmum Provincial Court.
When the two forces reached the suspect, Sron Khom, a 27-year-old Cambodian man, escaped, but the force arrested his wife, Khoeun Phatya, a 22-year-old Cambodian man.
Police searched the house and confiscated exhibits, including four large packages of suspected drugs, four drug scales, two swords, and a large number of drug paraphernalia.
Currently, the suspect and the exhibits were handed over by the Anti-Drug Force of Snuol District to the Anti-Drug Force of Tbong Khmum Province to proceed with the procedure.
