During the operation, the specialized force confiscated white gram powder, suspected drugs, 3 small packages, 5 motorcycles, 5 mobile phones and some drinking equipment. The suspects are currently being processed by the specialized police force for further investigation. Senior official of the Ministry of Interior: More than 110,000 foreign workers working in Cambodia, while those without a work permit were fined more than 1 million dollars
(Phnom Penh): As of the end of August 2018, more than 110,000 foreign workers working in Cambodia have paid more than $ 11 million in taxes and more than $ 1 million in fines. This is according to Mr. Chan Ean, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Interior.
During the ceremony of announcing the position and equipping the rank of Police Chief of the General Department of Immigration on the morning of September 3, 2018, Mr. Chan Ean said, "Until now, as of August 30, 2018, foreign workers have A total of 118,280 work permits (taxed $ 11,828,000) increased, exceeding expectations, with foreign workers found without work permits and fined more than $ 1 million. Also.
According to the senior official, before the establishment of the General Department of Immigration, only about 4,000 foreign workers had work permits and paid $ 400,000 in taxes, as foreign workers were not yet interested in respecting immigration and labor laws.
Mr. Chan Ean also pointed out that the work of managing immigrants has increased from 70,000 to nearly 200,000 and has been clearly divided into categories that are easy to ask for solutions.
According to Chan Ean, the most complicated category is foreigners holding irregular Cambodian administrative documents, however, so far the Ministry of Interior as well as the General Department of Immigration have confiscated about 80 percent of those documents. Chea Sophara Takes Nearly 4,000 Party Members in Tbong Khmum Province to Visit Angkor Wat Temple
(Siem Reap): Senior Minister Chea Sophara, First Deputy Chairman of the Central Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party, visited Tbong Khmum Province and Chairman of the Suong Municipality, Tbong Khmum District, Krouch Chhmar District and Memot District of Tbong Khmum Province. Nearly 4,000 CPP people visit Angkor Wat for 3 days.
The members of the Cambodian People's Party who were sponsored to participate in this big visit include: 1731 in Tbong Khmum district, 827 in Krouch Chhmar district, 1089 in Memot district, and 189 in Suong city, with a total of 3836 people and 91 buses.
The trip was made to thank the people as well as all members of the Cambodian People's Party for their efforts to bring victory to the party in the 2018 national election. The program was also held for 2 nights and 3 days, and the Senior Minister took party members in each district to visit Angkor, divided into 4 stages.
People are very happy because about 90% of all tourists have never visited Siem Reap, especially Angkor Wat. Under the guidance of Senior Minister Chea Sophara, they sang the national anthem and the Khmer chronicle in front of the Angkor Thom temple, which attracted a lot of national and international tourists and took photos.
