TOKYO (Reuters) - Major Japanese oil companies are reportedly preparing to suspend all crude oil imports from Iran in October amid fears of a warning from Washington to impose sanctions on those who dare. Continue to import Iranian crude oil. This is according to a quote from the Russian newspaper Sputnik on Monday afternoon, September 3, 2018.
The Tokyo government is reportedly seeking an exemption from Washington that would allow it to continue importing oil from Iran, but for now seems to be failing. Meanwhile, major Japanese oil companies are likely to find ways to increase oil imports from Iran.
According to a statement obtained by Fresh News on August 3, 2018, through the discussions of the members of the Labor Advisory Committee, which is composed of 16 government parties, 16 employers and The 16 union parties, the meeting achieved the following results:
1: Continue to use the mechanism of the tripartite technical working group consisting of 16 people from each party to discuss the minimum wage. The working group will start the discussion meeting from September 10, 2018.
2: Continue to use social criteria (family status, inflation rate and cost of living) and economic criteria (productivity, national competitiveness, labor market situation and sector profitability) as a study basis and recommendation to Labor Advisory Committee to review and decide.
Please be informed that the minimum wage of workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector in Cambodia has started to increase each year, and in 2018, the wages of workers in these sectors increased to 170 US dollars per month.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made it clear that there were no negotiations between Samdech and Sam Rainsy, and that Cambodia did not have a political crisis as Meas Ny analyzed.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's reaction came after Mr. Meas Ny, through an interview with a local newspaper, expressed his desire to see talks between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and prisoner Sam Rainsy to resolve issues in Cambodia while Samdech Travel to the US and Europe during this month or next.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed in a firm and serious statement that "There were no negotiations between me and Sam Rainsy during my visit abroad, both in the United States and in Europe. "I would like to say that Cambodia does not have a political crisis like the stupid analysis like Meas Ny, only politicians implement the law of Cambodia."
It should be noted that in recent times, the political situation in Cambodia has been seen to be improving after politicians, political activists and land activists were asked by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to apologize to the King of Cambodia. Next. The apology was made after the prisoners admitted their guilt and asked for forgiveness from Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
This apology is described as being in the spirit of national unity, as Samdech Techo Hun Sen did with Cambodians on all sides, especially with the Khmer Rouge 20 years ago, to bring Peace and harmony in Cambodian society is not the result of any foreign pressure.
However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has already stated that there will be no amnesty for Kem Sokha and Sam Rainsy, a politician with the nickname of a coward fleeing abroad.
