Catch all the overweight carriers! Another 11 vehicles seized from over 10 to 28 tons over 60 meters on Hanoi Road
(Phnom Penh): Despite the operation to seize the overweight truck led by Mr. Seng Chhuon, Undersecretary of State and Chairman of the Vehicle Technical Inspection Team, the overweight business is still occurring every day. Freight forwarders do not wake up to the road and continue to overweight, breaking the law to destroy the road.
On Sunday, September 2, 2018, Mr. Seng Chhuon continued to lead the raid to inspect the traffic on 60 meters and the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Road called Hanoi Road in Phnom Penh and intercepted 11 more vehicles. Overweight between 10 tons to 28 tons.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has often called on all drivers to respect the law and not to drive overweight, as overloading can seriously damage roads. The senior minister also stated that he did not want to be fined for overweight because it could not be offset by the amount of road damage.
