* Continue to eat clean food - well cooked, drink and use clean water as well as personal hygiene and diligently wash hands with soap every time before cooking and after defecation.
Sleep under mosquito nets to prevent dengue fever, malaria and other mosquito-borne diseases.
* Inspect the house for any possible damage, beware of snakes or other venomous animals that can bite or bite.
Avoid touching fallen wires and be careful that there may be pieces of glass or sharp metal in the premises that could lead to cuts or injuries.
If you have a health problem, go to a health center or hospital near your home for treatment.
At the same time, the Ministry of Health encourages the general public to follow the above simple advice to protect you and your family from various diseases.
