The opening ceremony of this training course was held on the afternoon of September 2, 2018 at High Sky Hotel (Kien Khleang) in the presence of Major General Chea Bunthol, Deputy Director of the Central Department of Judicial Police, Dr. Nget Van Thuok, Director of Private Services of the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department. And Dr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Investors and President of the Cambodian Pharmaceutical Sellers Association.
On that occasion, Mr. Ley Sopheap raised a number of issues related to the health business, both illegally, such as the sale of pharmaceutical products and cosmetics online, he stated that if the sale of products in accordance with the Ministry. Health is not a problem, but on the contrary, if the advertisement is false, exaggerated, deceptive, it will cause a lot of problems.
That is why the Cambodian Pharmacists Association, the Federation of Cambodian Medicines, Pharmacists and Dentists, in collaboration with the National Police Commissioner and the Phnom Penh Health Department, organized this training so that pharmacy owners and clinic owners can better understand the relevant laws to avoid misconduct. Unconsciously in daily business.
He said that the first step is to explain the law first so that they can better understand and implement it properly, and then the relevant institutions will cooperate to inspect and take legal action against any health business establishments. Violating the law or deliberately deceiving people who go to health services in those places.
He said that in this training, there is a lot of knowledge related to laws, procedures, regulations, as well as explain the application for registration and renewal of business at the OWSO (available in all districts. And districts across the country) which has provided a lot of convenience to traders who want to open a business in the health sector as well as other sectors.
