Therefore, the Legal Awareness Program of FRESH NEWS, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation this week, brings up the topic of "Divorce Procedures" as follows:
There are two types of divorce proceedings for legal marriage: (1) Divorce with consent and (2) Divorce for reasons as stated in the Civil Code, according to Articles 978 and 979 of the Civil Code. 2007 of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Therefore, one of the parties (spouse) of the marriage can file for divorce to the Capital / Provincial Court, and if the court finds that there are reasons and clear evidence that both parties can not live together as husband. / The other wife, then the court must decide the divorce party through the power of "verdict" according to the law on the procedure related to individual status.
Even if the parties' divorce petition has the reasons mentioned above, but if the court finds that the divorce is causing the support of the spouse or children poor or unbearable pain or because That claim is contrary to good faith, the court may reject the divorce claim by considering the actual situation or by discretion.
Prepared by: Ms. Savy Lida, Member of the Working Group on the Preparation and Dissemination of Legal Articles and Mr. Sok Ponleu, Assistant Lawyer and Member of the Working Group on the Preparation and Dissemination of the Legal Articles of the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation
