The horrific incident of a Thai car hitting a Cambodian car happened at 8:20 pm on August 31, 2018, along the national road in Pong Nam Ron district, Chan Borei province, Thailand.
The dead wife, Kheang Thearaphon, 41, deputy director of the Pailin Provincial Hall, and her husband, Siek Rattanak, 50, were seriously injured and were being treated at the Chan Borei Provincial Hospital. An unknown silver CRV with no license plate was also completely damaged. The driver of the car, who is an unidentified Thai party, opened the car door and escaped.
Prior to the incident, the two victims were seen driving a silver CRV in an east-west direction, crossing the Pailin provincial border to Chan Borei, Thailand. While traveling on the road, a white Thai Mitsubishi car overtook each other and hit the victim's car, causing serious injuries and death.
Both vehicles were badly damaged and were towed off the road by Thai authorities to be stored for storage.
Currently, the body of the victim was contacted by relatives to the Thai side to be transported back to Pailin province and prepare for the traditional ceremony, while Mr. Seak Rattanak is still in the emergency room in Thailand.
