A deputy governor of Prek Pnov district and his wife are accused of making a contract to sell a house worth nearly half a million dollars after receiving the deposit and the first installment, but ran to sue to cancel
(Phnom Penh): A deputy governor of Prek Pnov district, Mr. Touch Salin, and his wife, Sam Lalin, are accused of entering into a contract to sell two flats in Bayap village, Phnom Penh Thmey commune, Sen Sok district, worth nearly half a million dollars. The first phase of the deposit and payment from the buyer more than $ 180,000, but ran to the court to terminate the contract to buy and sell the house, the purpose is to break the deposit and the first payment from the buyer.
The charges against the deputy governor of Phnom Penh's Prek Pnov district were made by Chan Sovannara, a representative of Sen Sok Sovann Development Company, and another Chinese woman.
In the contract, which is recognized and heard by the lawyer Bun Keo Lim stated that the buyer's representative must pay in three stages: the first stage: a deposit of 20,000 dollars, the second stage: to pay the purchase price. $ 165,000 on March 30, 2018 and Phase 3: The buyer must pay a $ 300,000 down payment when the seller completes the transfer of title to the buyer.
However, after the buyer made a deposit of $ 20,000 and paid an additional $ 165,000, Mr. Touch Salin and his wife refused to transfer the name to the buyer and ran to the court to terminate the contract. Intended to deduct deposits and surcharges totaling nearly $ 200,000.
Seeing the actions of the deputy governor of Prek Pnov district and his wife, the buyer ran to sue the president of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in early August to request an order to protect the two flats.
The buyer made two appeals: First, he asked Mr. Touch Salin and his wife, who is the seller of the house, to abide by the contract of sale of the house with the correct thumbprint and recognition from the lawyer, and secondly: The Ministry of Interior as well as Phnom Penh Capital Hall to temporarily suspend the work of the Deputy Governor to allow the court to deal with legal procedures.
