International Analysis: Four key points behind US aid to the Egyptian government, despite its alleged dictatorship!
1: If the United States does not provide assistance, Egypt may turn to Russia, while the peaceful relations between Egypt and Israel may be in danger.
In terms of the peace treaty between Egypt and Israel, the United States no longer seems to be useful to Egypt, and Egypt no longer needs US intervention or mediation. Why Egypt is no longer interested in confronting Israel. Instead, Israel could become one of Cairo's most important regional partners.
2: Putting pressure on Egypt is not as effective as providing aid
The recent suspension of US aid prompted the Egyptian government to reconsider the case in 2013 and to establish good relations with North Korea. Putting pressure on suspending aid to change the attitude of Egyptian leaders is a waste of time. Therefore, instead of imposing unprofitable sanctions, the United States decided to use the Cold War by providing aid instead.
Third, the United States provides assistance to Egypt to obtain key rights such as crossing the Suez Canal and the right to fly over Egyptian airspace.
Fourth, Egypt needs $ 1.3 billion in aid for anti-terror operations in Sinai
Such a strategy is not only unsuccessful, but also detrimental to the Sinai people. And victory against the Islamic State is impossible. That is why Egypt still needs a lot of money to fight the rebels. These are the reasons why the United States provides assistance to the Egyptian government, which it accuses of being dictatorial, even though Egypt does not meet the conditions set by the United States.
