Mr. Sun Chanthol vowed to redouble his efforts to serve the people in return for his overwhelming trust in the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Kandal): On Saturday, September 1, 2018, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of the Standing Committee of Koh Thom District Local Strengthening Committee, Kandal Province, Riding a bicycle to visit and thank the people in Chroy Takeo and Kampong Kong communes who voted for the Cambodian People's Party on July 29, 2018.
During the ceremony, the Senior Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the people in Koh Thom district who loved and fully supported the Cambodian People's Party, especially supporting Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister to continue to lead and develop the country. Progress continues.
In front of the people of Koh Thom district, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol pledged that he and his team will continue to work harder to serve the people as a civil servant in accordance with the high recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to continue to develop. Villages, communes in Koh Thom district for further development, such as the construction of concrete roads, clean water, canals, and street lighting.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also instructed the people to provide information to the team in case they encounter difficulties in daily life, and he and his team will try to solve it as effectively as possible.
Please note that for the 6th legislative election of the National Assembly on July 29, 2018, the people went to the polls in large numbers up to more than 83%. The CPP received nearly 5 million votes to control the seats in the National Assembly 100%, that is, 125 seats in the National Assembly 125 seats are controlled by the CPP alone.
Mr. Veng Sakhon requested people all over Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province to make efforts to restore agricultural production after the flood
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Chairman of the National Task Force for Kampong Siem District on September 1, 2018, requested the people to make efforts to restore agricultural production after the flood and the General Department of Agriculture as well as the Department of Agriculture and Forestry. And provincial fisheries must find all means to solve problems for the people in a timely, efficient and effective manner.
This request was made on the occasion that Mr. Veng Sakhon, together with Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, visited and brought more than 100 tons of rice and food donated by philanthropists to distribute to more than 5 flood victims. Thousands of families in Koh Roka commune, Kokor commune, Koh Tonem commune, Ro Ang commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province this morning, September 1, 2018.
On this occasion, the Governor also thanked Mr. Veng Sakhon and members of the working group for taking into account the well-being of the local people, this is a good humanitarian gesture of members of the Royal Government who adhere to the culture. Share in all circumstances to alleviate the suffering of the people.
Mr. Veng Sakhon stated that on behalf of the Royal Government, the leadership of the Ministry and the working group to help Kampong Siem district, he expressed his deep regret for this flood and would like to share all the hardships that people throughout the commune. Roka Island is facing.
Through Mr. Veng Sakhon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen sent his condolences to visit and share the suffering of the flood victims throughout Kampong Siem district and Wish everything goes back to normal soon.
On this occasion, Mr. Veng Sakhon mentioned some of the main reasons that caused floods and droughts are due to climate change. All of these phenomena inevitably destroy the lives of people, animals, crops, homes, and physical infrastructure. In fact, this year, Cambodia is experiencing floods and drought in 16 provinces, including Kampong Cham.
He said that he understands the difficulties and problems that the people are facing. The Royal Government, with Samdech Techo as the Prime Minister, has ordered all the authorities of the Armed Forces to solve the problems for the people in a timely and effective manner to help. Alleviate the hardships of citizens everywhere and all families without letting any people die of lack of food.
Through today's donation, he would like to thank all the philanthropists who have donated their personal wealth, materials and budget to share the people's livelihood today and call on philanthropists to continue to support. More humanitarian activities as possible. On this occasion, he donated some materials and money to the pagoda's chief and commune authorities.
Once again, Mr. Veng Sakhon thanked all members of the working group and all the voters who voted for the CPP. This result clearly shows the will of the people who want peace, freedom, stability and development with Samdech Techo as Prime Minister.
In order to contribute to the maintenance, protection and development of the country, Mr. Veng Sakhon advised all professional officers and relevant authorities at all levels to:
1: Increase attention to implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen better. 2: To strengthen the efficiency of providing public services to the people, especially to continue to implement policy K3 to be sustainable and effective. Hunting and fishing and local authorities must monitor the flood situation and be ready to help people after the water recedes in a timely and efficient manner.
