Phnom Penh Governor Leads Officials to Inspect Poor Roads in Po Sen Chey District
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 1, 2018, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, led the authorities and professional officers to inspect the condition of Street 123CC in Thmor Koul II Village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Sen Chey. This line has been damaged, making it difficult for people to travel.
To determine the road to be rebuilt, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will build a concrete road with a length of 970 meters and a width of 6 meters. In addition, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will also make arrangements for the sewerage network.
In connection with the opening of the road and sewer system, the Governor of Phnom Penh requested the Public Works Department to install the bulldozer as soon as possible and also ask for the people's understanding on the impact and disturbance when the construction begins. Process.
After inspecting the condition of Street 123CC, Mr. Khuong Sreng also continued to visit and inspect the distribution of clean water to the people in Tuol Key village, Sangkat Pleung Cheh Roret, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Mr. Khuong Sreng on that occasion confirmed that the visit and inspection of clean water distribution to the people, he wanted to know and see the living conditions, shortages and desires of the people. Obviously. When we know what the people want, and on behalf of the Phnom Penh administration, which is the mother and father of the people, we will provide it to the people.
In fact, in Tuol Key village, Sangkat Pleung Cheh Roret, Khan Por Sen Chey, the people in this village do not have a clean water system to use, so the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has set up a water truck to transport people to the back of the house with the state price.
