Help in times of need! Five widows receive gifts from Lt. Gen. Thong Thavarin, Deputy Commander of the Army, to pay off bank debt and build a house
(Kratie): Lieutenant Colonel Sos Hussein, Deputy Chief of Army Inspection, brought a donation of Lt. Gen. Thong Thavarin, Deputy Commander of the Army and Lieutenant General Sim Tai, Chief of Army Inspection, 2 million Riels. To 5 widows and children living in poverty after the death of their husbands, leaving them to live in a hut in Prey Ko village, Damrey Phong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province, to pay off bank debts and build a house.
Sous Hussein said the widow, 35-year-old Kreung Sreyvit, suffered from chronic illness and sold cattle, pigs, chickens, ducks, farms and houses to treat her husband. He did not recover and died for more than a year.
Seeing this difficult situation and after receiving the information, the general also assigned the team to take 2 million riels to help pay off the bank debt and build a house.
Mondulkiri province is changing more and more! Provincial Governor vows to develop and calls for more investors in the border province
Speaking at a meeting on development projects in Mondulkiri, Mondulkiri Governor Svay Sam Eang said that although our province has developed differently in the past, we work together. Contemplate this notion as you interact with your neighbors and your loved ones.
But we are talking about now, the transition from the province used to be quiet to rejoice due to the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen working hard to restore and develop rapidly between the capital city and this remote province closer. Close to each other, there is a luxurious road and bridge communication system for better traffic.
Not only that, the province has also mobilized many development investment partners in agriculture, agro-industry and many partners in the tourism sector to invest. Infrastructure development, both public and private, has grown significantly, population growth has increased.
The province has also been working to further improve the city's aesthetics to attract more local and foreign tourists. Construction on the private sector is also growing, such as guesthouses, hotels, tourism are being invested and developed to meet the needs of tourists.
The Ministry of Environment considers the publication of an article under the title "Minister of the Environment requesting Mr. Hun Sen to logging companies in economic land concessions" of VOD on August 30, 2018 as inciting and slandering. True, malicious intent pollutes society, destroys public trust in the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Through this clarification letter, the Ministry of Environment confirmed some of the reasons requested by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to allow the company to clear the economic land concession as well. The reasons are:
1. According to the legal procedure, companies that receive ELCs need to clear and clear the location of their ELC investment projects that have received investment rights from the Royal Government to implement their projects in accordance with the master plan. The transportation of non-timber forest products from clearing, clearing and clearing of ELC investment projects is done with proper legal permission.
In this letter, the Ministry of Environment reiterated that since 2012, the Royal Government has completely stopped granting new economic land concessions to private companies. The Ministry of Environment also affirmed that it will continue to make more efforts to serve the nation and the people of Cambodia in the cause of protecting natural resources, biodiversity conservation to preserve natural resources for future generations.
Good news for Cambodian students! University of Arizona USA accepts students to study in Phnom Penh
