(Kampong Cham): Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, on August 31, 2018, ordered the specialized police force of the Provincial Police Commission to increase the prevention and suppression of drug offenses at the local level. Rural areas are threatened by drugs.
The regulation was made during a meeting to review the results of the first half of the fight against drugs and set the direction for the second half of 2018, as well as to strengthen the skills and implementation of the plan on the third campaign against illegal drugs. Of the Royal Government at the Provincial Police Commission.
Speaking on that occasion, Major General Em Kosal reminded and stressed that the officials in this plan must pay high attention to their skills, the implementation of procedures on professional work. In particular, the administrative police officers need to pay more attention and crack down, which in some rural areas now seems to be spreading and threatening by the drug problem.
In order to carry out this work more effectively, the General Commissioner instructed the police force on five main plans to prevent and suppress drug crimes at the local level, including:
First, outreach work as a priority in remote areas to educate people and youth to better understand the dangers of drugs.
Second: Implement outreach plans to target vulnerable people, especially young people in this remote area, who are easily deceived by drug traffickers. Use administrative measures to promote targeted management updates by detecting drug-testing targets in order to take measures to keep victims away from drugs.
Third: Continue the actual crackdown on drug trafficking
Fourth: Promote measures to rehabilitate drug-addicted youths to health centers in communes and districts
Fifth, strengthen cooperation with civil society organizations, associations and local communities to mobilize support for these activities.
Please be informed that this morning, the General Commissioner also chaired a meeting to review the situation of the results of the social security operations for the first nine months of 2018 and the implementation of the work of the police and the community in August and the direction of the tasks for September 2018 in accordance with Instruction of the General Commission of National Police. Daily Summary of National and International Special News on August 31, 2018
