Japan's Defense Ministry on Friday proposed a military budget of up to $ 48 billion, up 2.1 percent for 2019, starting April 1. On the other hand, if the package is approved, it would mean a seven-fold increase in the military budget as Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe is strengthening Japan's military capability to respond to the North Korean missile threat. Increasing Chinese military influence in the region.
