Samdech Techo Hun Sen Invites Singaporean PM to Visit Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has invited Singaporean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong to pay an official visit to Cambodia in the near future. Better friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Singapore. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs released on August 31.
During a three-day visit to the Republic of Singapore from August 29-31, Senior Minister Prak Sokhon paid a courtesy call on Singaporean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong and introduced him. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's greetings and thanks to Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong for sending a congratulatory message on Cambodia's general election victory.
According to the press release, Senior Minister Prak Sokhon also extended an invitation to Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong to pay an official visit to Cambodia at an appropriate time from Samdech Techo Prime Minister. Upon hearing this, Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong gladly accepted the invitation.
In addition, Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong praised the long-standing relationship between Cambodia and Singapore and expressed his deep appreciation for the strength of peace and continued development in Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Lee Hsien Loong encouraged to further promote the good cooperation between the two countries, Cambodia - Singapore to serve each other as well as strengthen the ASEAN Center and the building of the ASEAN Community.
In a press release on the outcome of Senior Minister Prak Sokhon's official visit to the Republic of Singapore released on August 31, 2018, it was stated that during the bilateral meeting, Senior Minister Prak Sokhon and Mr. Vivian Balak Krishnan noted We are very pleased with the progress of the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and Singapore, especially in the areas of investment, trade and tourism, which are growing.
The two sides reaffirmed their commitment to work closely together to build a stronger leadership-to-leadership relationship, between business and people-to-people and people-to-people exchanges, and to enhance economic exchanges. And cooperation in various fields, including aviation, telecommunications, energy, employment and human resource development.
"Vivian Balakrishnan congratulated Cambodia on its general election victory and pledged further support for Cambodia's vibrant progress and modernization process," the statement said.
The Cambodian diplomat thanked Singapore for sending election observers to Cambodia and reaffirmed Cambodia's full support for Singapore's success in its ASEAN chairmanship.
This was confirmed in a press release on the results of Senior Minister Prak Sokhon's official visit to the Republic of Singapore from 29-31 August at the invitation of Mr. Vivian Balakkrishnan, released on 31 August This 2018.
"The Senior Minister also expressed the hope that Singapore would increase imports of rice and other agricultural products from Cambodia and would consider a bilateral framework agreement on labor cooperation," the statement said.
At the same time, Senior Minister Prak Sokhon thanked Singapore for its continued support for Cambodia's socio-economic development, especially human resource development, covering the development of digital capabilities.
