The 8th largest job event in Cambodia is organized to:
* Create a convenient one-stop meeting platform for employers, educators, and job seekers to exchange and share labor market information, as well as raise awareness and cultivate productivity ideas.
* Employers can advertise current and future recruitment needs to attract competent job seekers.
* Job seekers can apply for jobs on the spot as well as receive information on current and future job opportunities and skills development opportunities.
* Training providers can advertise all kinds of curricula, courses and skills development programs.
* Introduce ideas, skills and technologies to enhance productivity and efficiency in business by demonstrating the success of outstanding employees and sharing experiences, knowledge and skills of famous national and international experts.
* Provide a platform for building human resource communication networks.
Outcome of the Consultation of ASEAN Economic Ministers and ASEAN Partners during the 50th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings in Singapore
(Phnom Penh): On Thursday, August 30, 2018, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and ASEAN Economic Minister for Cambodia, led a delegation to the ASEAN Economic Ministers 'Meeting and Partners during the 50th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting. And related meetings chaired by Mr. CHAN CHUN SING, Minister of Commerce and Industry of the Republic of Singapore.
The meeting was also attended by the Ministers of Economy and Delegation of ASEAN Member States, Ministers and Delegates of Partner Countries, the ASEAN Secretary-General and representatives of the ASEAN Secretariat, with the following key outcomes:
1. The 10th Mekong-Japan Economic Ministers' Meeting: The Mekong Economic Ministers (Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Vietnam, Thailand) and Japan highly valued the cooperation under the Mekong-Japan framework, especially on the implementation of the Mekong-Japan Industrial Development Project and Vision. Deepening within the framework of the Mekong subregion.
In addition, the Royal Government of Cambodia considers the digital economy as a priority sector, while Cambodia has been shifting from the use of labor to the use of technology, especially the importance of the participation of the private sector, including small and medium enterprises. An important catalyst in driving the digital economy.
The Japanese side has expressed support for the connection of software and hardware infrastructure and human resource development, especially in the digital economy, including e-commerce.
The Minister expressed his support for Cambodia and thanked the Chinese side for inviting Cambodia to be the host country at the 15th ASEAN-China Expo to be held on September 12-15, 2018 in Nanning, People's Republic of China. China with the high presence of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
3. The 24th ASEAN-Japan Economic Ministers' Consultation: The consultation welcomed the dialogue between the Japan Chamber of Commerce and the ASEAN Industry on initiatives aimed at promoting innovation, strengthening business and industrial development.
The consultations noted the projects under the Economic and Industrial Cooperation Committee of the ASEAN Economic Ministers - Ministry of Commerce and Industry of Japan (AMEICC), especially in relation to the development of business, industry, cooperation related to small and medium enterprises. Promote the development and deepening of ASEAN-Japan relations.
In addition, the consultations also discussed the progress of the implementation of the ASEAN-Japan Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, urging all stakeholders to expedite the completion of the First Protocol on the Amendment of the ASEAN-Japan Agreement to be able to sign Signing at the 21st ASEAN-Japan Summit during November 2018.
4. The 15th ASEAN-Korea Economic Ministers' Consultation: The Consultation noted the cooperation activities of the ASEAN-Korea Business Council, focusing on the ASEAN-Korea Business Forum in sharing experiences as well as economic and trade cooperation. Promote cooperation between small and medium enterprises in ASEAN and Korea and the TASK program, which has been consulting and training enterprises in Cambodia, Myanmar and Vietnam.
The consultations also reviewed and discussed the progress of the ratification of the third protocol on the amendment of the ASEAN-Korea Trade in Goods Agreement and urged the parties to the agreement to accelerate further liberalization under the framework of the Commodity Trade Agreement. ASEAN-Korea.
5. 21st ASEAN Plus Three Economic Ministers' Consultation: The Consultations welcomed and appreciated the reports and recommendations of the East Asia Business Council, especially on the facilitation of digital economy development in East Asia and its exploitation. From the Free Trade Agreement in accordance with the principles of the World Trade Organization (WTO).
The consultations also approved the ASEAN Plus Three Economic Cooperation Action Plan 2019-2020, which includes key activities such as joint research activities, small and medium enterprise development, trade facilitation, public-private dialogue and The development of the digital economy as well.
6. 6th Ministerial Meeting of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement: This meeting discussed some of the remaining issues that need to be decided and guided by the Ministerial level, focusing on the four major areas, including trade in goods. Trade, services, investment and intellectual property.
The Ministers of the 16 countries expressed their soft stance and high commitment to conclude the agreement negotiations in 2018, as mandated by the heads of government of the 16 countries, urging all negotiating parties to make more efforts and respond positively. Both bilateral and multilateral.
The meeting also reaffirmed the provision of special flexibility to all least developed countries to reap maximum benefits after the entry into force of this agreement. NABA Theater offers a new colorful show!
