(Battambang): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province, Mr. Vong Piseth, Project Director, and Mr. Ouk Nida, Representative of the Asian Development Bank (ADB), on August 30, 2018, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the night market. Battambang city in Battambang province under a grant from the Government of Japan.
The construction of the Battambang New Night Market in the Greater Mekong Subregion is a corridor development project to improve the livelihoods of the people along the Mekong River - Battambang Province, which is funded by a grant from the Japanese Fund to Reduce Poverty.
The new night market is located in Svay Por commune and in the center of Battambang city, between the provincial hall and the Sangke river. The project was approved on May 21, 2013, with a construction period from August 2017 to April 2018.
The night market was built at a cost of more than 300,000 US dollars on an area of 3,064 square meters. There are 152 poor market vendors, 137 of whom are women, which is organized into a market traders association governed by the night market management committee. The 152 market members also received training and funding for their businesses supported by the project.
