Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Khim Bunsong expressed his great pleasure and warm welcome to the presence of Ms. Sushma Swaraj, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of India and the accompanying delegation who spent valuable time visiting Siem Reap Province in order to strengthen and expand bilateral cooperation between the people and the two governments (Cambodia-India).
In addition, Mr. Khim Bunsong would like to express his sincere congratulations on the glorious success of the Indian Foreign Minister's three-day official visit, which the two governments (Cambodia-India) discussed on cooperation. Further operations include the renovation of the Temple of Preah Vihear on Ta Prohm in Siem Reap, a project renovated by the Indian government.
Mr. Khim Bunsong also congratulated the signing of the visit on two documents: Agreement between the Government of India and Cambodia on the Restoration of the Temple of Preah Vihear in Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province and the Memorandum of Understanding between the National Institute of Diplomacy and Relations International of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia and the Foreign Service Institute of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of India.
At the same time, the Governor of Siem Reap thanked the Government of India for supporting the democratic elections in Cambodia for the sixth mandate, which was successfully completed on July 29, 2018 recently.
(Tbong Khmum): Finally! The Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Ky Bithy, on August 30, 2018, decided to continue detaining Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the National Rescue Party in Trapeang Phlong Prison, Tbong Khmum Province for another 6 months according to the procedure. Bail is not allowed.
The trial in Trapeang Phlong prison in Tbong Khmum province was chaired by Investigating Judge Ky Bithy and represented by Deputy Prosecutor Sieng Sok of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. The four lawyers representing Kem Sokha were also present at the prison hearing.
Kem Sokha's arrest follows the release of a video of him confessing to a systematic conspiracy with foreigners to overthrow Cambodia's legitimate government, following in the footsteps of Serbia and Yugoslavia. It is an act of treason. Hurry up! Borey Monorom, Prek Taten, housing for low and middle income people officially opened for sale!
Kandal Province CamControl Finds Defective Canned Drinks and Butter for Sale at Prek Anchanh Market and Roka Kong Market
(Kandal): In order to protect food safety as well as people's health, on August 30, 2018, Mr. Ou Manorin, President of CamControl Kandal Branch, cooperated with the Department of Commerce and local authorities to inspect and disseminate food quality and safety at the market. Prek Anchanh and Roka Kong Market are located in Muk Kampoul District, Kandal Province.
Mr. Ou Manorin said that during the inspection of the two markets, the team tested some foods such as vegetables, fruits, meatballs, noodles, seafood, such as squid, shrimp, but the results of the preliminary tests were obtained. Good results. At the same time, the team confiscated more than 10 cans of rusty and expired cans and 2 cans of spoiled butter and burned them.
According to the branch president, the team distributed posters and disseminated information to traders, vendors and consumers to understand the consequences of eating out of date and adding banned chemicals to food.
