(Phnom Penh): Mr. Try Tay Hy, Managing Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX), has announced that the CSX will provide professional officers to hold seminars for universities across Cambodia if the university wishes to provide stock market knowledge to its students.
The CSX Management Officer stated, “The Cambodia Securities Exchange is pleased to partner with universities across Cambodia to provide securities-related knowledge to students. The Cambodia Securities Exchange can provide professional officers to conduct workshops or open classes to interested universities.
"In addition, the Cambodia Securities Exchange is pleased to sign a memorandum of understanding with the university to improve human resource development in the securities sector," he said.
According to Mr. Try Tai Hee, the reason why CSX decided to do this is in order to increase knowledge in the field of securities and spread this awareness to educational institutions, especially universities, so that students have more knowledge in this field.
Speaking at the event, the Deputy Director General of CSX said that the Cambodia Securities Exchange is working hard to attract securities issuers and potential investors in order to develop the Cambodia Securities Exchange more trading activities.
HA Jong Weon added that today's program will make a significant contribution to raising the awareness of the securities sector to all the professors present here and strongly hope that knowledge related to this new field will be Disseminated to the public and especially students at various universities.
Samdech Sangkha Non Nget and Mrs. Men Sam An Invite to Dissolve the Body of Brahma Panha Veng Wutty
(Kampong Speu): Samdech Preah Mohasometheathipady, Honorary Doctor Dr. Non Nget and Mrs. Kittisangha Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, summoned and presided over the cremation of the body of Brahma Panha Veng Vuthy Preah Akka Moha Sangkha Rajathipati Tep Vong, Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach III of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Advisor to the Provincial Council of Kampong Speu and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Techea Phnom Srong.
The body of Brahma Panha Veng Wutty is far away from all of us, but all that remains can not be extinguished: the construction of pagodas, goodness, goodness, honor, dignity, activism, perseverance, perseverance in work. It will always be in our hearts and we will never forget his noble ideals, national conscience, and noble example of heroism.
History of Brahma Veng Wutty Since becoming a priest, he has strived to practice the Dharma of Preah Samma Samput. Strive to build Wat Srak Phnom Srong in Srong commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province to become a place of worship for Buddhists of all walks of life.
Wat Sdech Phnom Srong is a new pagoda under the wise leadership and Bin Prasop, making this pagoda a great and famous pagoda and under the direct support of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. The King of Cambodia.
The court will announce the decision to extend or continue the detention of Kem Sokha at 2:00 pm
(Tbong Khmum): After the hearing in Trapeang Phlong Prison, Tbong Khmum Province, the judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court will announce his decision to postpone or continue the detention of Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the National Rescue Party at 2 o'clock: 00 pm on August 30, 2018. This is according to the claim of the defense lawyer for Mr. Kem Sokha.
The trial in Tbong Khmum's Trapeang Phlong prison was presided over by Judge Ky Bithy and represented by Deputy Prosecutor Sieng Sok of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. The four lawyers representing Kem Sokha were also present at the prison hearing.
Expert doctors: People with frequent headaches should be careful about the four diseases that lead to the most dangerous
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Bui Chauwi from Vietnam confirmed that there are four of the most serious and dangerous diseases and occur in people of all ages, both men and women who often have headaches.
Dr. Bui Chau Tvei, Head Specialist from Cho Ray Hospital, Vietnam, made the remarks on the morning of August 30, 2018 at the free monthly check-up and treatment program at Cho Ray Hospital in Phnom Penh in collaboration with the company. DHG Pharma.
He added that headaches are divided into two main groups, including headaches inside the brain and headaches outside the brain, all of which are worrisome if not. Treated for that time.
At the same time, Dr. Bui Zhou Tvi also called on all people who suffer from headaches should reduce their thoughts, reduce stress and get enough sleep, and should consult a doctor. When this happens, avoid buying over-the-counter medications without a proper prescription.
Police Inspect 3 Entertainment Clubs in Poipet and Serei Sophorn City, Find 2 Suspicious Hides and Detain Some Khmer-Chinese Suspects for Questioning
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Force, led by Major General Ace Cam, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, conducted an operation to inspect three different entertainment venues (clubs) and found two entertainment venues suspected of stealing, trafficking and using drugs. Illegal drugs in Serei Sophorn and Poipet, Banteay Meanchey province.
Currently, the authorities are detaining some suspects who are being interrogated by specialized forces and taking urine tests, while the owner of the location, the prosecutor, has made a contract to stop using drugs. Phnom Penh Department of Public Works and Transport: The section of road that collapsed by the Tonle Sap River in Russey Keo district is 100% completed
(Phnom Penh): A section of road that collapsed into the Tonle Sap River in Group 2, Prek Ta Kong Village, Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Chroy Changva has been completed and is open to people to cross.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, said that the team of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh has poured large stones and sandbags to fill the bank of the Tonle Sap River. The construction was completed 100 percent by mid-August so that people could return to normal travel.
It should be reminded that the Governor of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, on the morning of August 4, 2018, that is, while he led the local authorities and officials under his supervision to check the actual situation of the river bank collapse. He immediately ordered the relevant professional officers to rebuild one of the damaged roads immediately.
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng on the day of the inspection, the construction of the collapsed riverbank road was done temporarily to prevent further landslides and to enable people to travel. Temporarily, because the people in this area communicate only this one way.
The then Governor of Phnom Penh also confirmed that in the coming low water season, he will send professional officers to study the technique thoroughly and the Capital Administration will be able to hit the road to make this road strong and consistent.
Chip Montreal lays foundation to build giant supermarket in The Landmark 271
This amazing shopping mall project started the foundation on the morning of August 30, 2018 under the chairmanship of Senior Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, accompanied by government officials and officials. Many business investment partners.
It should also be noted that in addition to the construction of such a large shopping mall, The Landmark 271 project will have high-end hotels, commercial buildings, modern condominiums, theme parks, gymnasiums, Western-style, especially the five entrances with architectural design. Perfect. For living, The Landmark 271 offers 3 types of villas: Villa Queen, Queen A and Twin Villa.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, this morning, August 30, 2018, received three newly appointed Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Cambodia to pay a courtesy call and receive pre-departure recommendations. To complete diplomatic missions in the Republic of the Philippines, Japan and Belgium.
During a courtesy call at the Senate, the three new ambassadors received a number of recommendations from the President of the Senate.
The three new ambassadors are: Mr. Ing Rachana, Cambodian Ambassador to Japan, Mr. Leng Chanvirak, Cambodian Ambassador to the Republic of the Philippines, and Mr. Noum Piseth, Cambodian Ambassador to Belgium.
