(Phnom Penh): The body of the former owner of Chhay Hong Hotel, who had just bought a jet ski and rode along the Mekong River and then fell into the river for 4 nights and 5 days, was found around the missing location. At 6:30 am on August 30, 2018, along the Mekong River, Lvea Village, Sangkat Koh Dach, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
The body of the drowning victim was Hok Bun Huy, alias Ta Huy, a 48-year-old man, a former owner of the Chhay Hong Hotel and now the owner of a noodle shop with the Phnom Penh Sanitation brand in Prek Leap Village, Prek Leap Sangkat, Chroy Changva District.
On the morning of August 30, 2018, at 6:30 AM, the relatives of a Cambodian Muslim fisherman who was hired by the victim's family to find the body found the body of the former owner of the Chhay Hong Hotel in Lvea Village. Koh Dach Sangkat, Chroy Changvar District, about 500 meters from the old port, also reported to the Chief of Lvea Village Defenders to inform the authorities of Koh Dach Sangkat to the scene and contact the relatives of the victims.
Later, Koh Dach commune authorities ordered the fishermen to transport the body of the former owner of the hotel, Chhay Hong, to the Bak Kheng pagoda to wait for relatives to receive and take to the traditional ceremony. Minister of Agriculture Holds National Consultation Meeting on "Draft Strategic Plan for Effective Forest Management"
The workshop was co-organized by the Forestry Administration in collaboration with UNDP and was attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, representatives of UNDP, ladies and gentlemen, and many other development partners. These include:
First, monitor the progress of the preparation of the strategic plan for effective forest management in 2018-2032, and second: seek input from all stakeholders, including knowledge, experience and good recommendations, and include in this draft, useful for editing. To be even better, both legally and technically, and then submit to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for review and approval.
On this occasion, the Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the leadership of the Forestry Administration, UNDP and all relevant officials who have made every effort to facilitate and support all possible and good cooperation to make the workshop. Importantly, do well today.
Mr. Veng Sakhon also highlighted the key points of the forestry sector to brief the workshop that the forest plays an important role in protecting the environment, reducing climate change, contributing to economic development. Nation and reduce poverty.
Recognizing the benefits of invaluable national forest resources, the Royal Government is firmly committed to continuing to carry out in-depth reforms in the forestry sector through the introduction of a series of policies and regulations for the following main purposes:
First, sustainable management of forest resources through control of forest exploitation, conservation of forests reserved for domestic use, and conservation of wetlands as a fish sanctuary. Second: Protection of biological resources. Diversity and endangered species of plants and wildlife
Third, develop community forestry in a transparent and sustainable manner through on-site development by local communities in accordance with the potential in each geography.
In particular, the development of ecotourism communities to create jobs, increase incomes, reduce total dependence on forest products and by-products, encroachment on forest land, plantations and reduce poverty and migration. And are facing many big problems such as:
Starting from these issues, the Royal Government, headed by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, has launched a forest sector reform program, which includes several key action plans, including:
* Strengthening the implementation of forest laws * Establishing and strengthening community forests * Implementing strict measures to control and prevent forest crime * Strengthening the management of forest reserves * Establishing forest areas for the conservation of plant and wildlife genetic resources And erecting permanent forest boundary posts * Planting seedlings at outreach stations * Planting seedlings in reforestation areas and other locations
In particular, the "Tree Day" ceremony every year to inspire all masses to participate in planting trees, protecting forests and biodiversity, which is a valuable heritage for all mankind. Indeed, the achievement is the success of the implementation of policies and strategies of the Royal Government with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
In particular, the draft strategic plan for productive forest management that we are currently preparing is for the following purposes:
* Increase and strengthen the capacity to manage the forest to provide sustainable results in the future to contribute
Poverty reduction
* Increase the living standard of the community, maintain the economic growth and ecology of the productive forest
* Expand the forest products business based on legal principles, both national and international
* Strengthen forest governance, develop institutional and human resource capacity, encourage community participation, support sustainable forest management
* Strengthen national and international cooperation, development partners, local authorities and the armed forces at all levels.
The Minister urged all members of the workshop to use their wisdom, knowledge and experience to thoroughly and in-depth review of key inputs mentioned in the Fifth Draft Strategic Plan for Forest Management. This provides, in particular, the most important points to consider and give the most comprehensive and in-depth advice:
First, compliance with the national forest policy and regulations of the Royal Government of Cambodia; Second, the establishment of strategic goals and activities, including financing projects, to address barriers to productive forest management.
Third, the capacity and resources of the institution to implement the strategic plan in accordance with the procedures and fourth: the challenges that may be obstacles in the implementation of this strategic plan.
