(Siem Reap): On August 30, 2018, the National Association of Capital-Provincial Council announced the opening of a two-day training course in Siem Reap on two lessons for 30 trainers to have the ability to continue training for Capital and Provincial Council members across the country.
After completing the course, a group of 30 trainers, consisting of chairpersons and members of the 25 provincial capital councils, will organize further training for members in the 25 provincial capitals.
Currently, there are 393 Capital and Provincial Councilors nationwide, including 384 from the Cambodian People's Party and 9 from FUNCINPEC.
The National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils was established in 2013 with the aim of enhancing the capacity development of the Capital and Provincial Councils and protecting the legitimate interests of its members in order to strengthen the rule of law and promote democracy in Cambodia.
