After Inspection, the Minister of Rural Development announced the rehabilitation of a road in Chey Sen District, Preah Vihear Province.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, on the afternoon of August 29, 2018, announced the renovation of a 4 km road in Chey Sen district, Preah Vihear province, after inspecting that this road was almost damaged. Completely due to flooding.
Accompanying the Minister of Rural Development on that occasion was the presence of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as well as the Deputy Governor, government officials and the Armed Forces.
Mr. Ouk Rabun said that this road will be rehabilitated in the near future so that people can pass through safely as well as transport agricultural products easily and quickly.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on August 29, 2018 issued an official press release on the results of the official visit of the Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of India, Ms. Susma Swaraj.
Ms. Susma Swaraj led a delegation to pay an official visit to Cambodia from 28-30 August 2018 with the aim of enhancing friendly relations and further strengthening cooperation between the two countries.
During the visit, Ms. Susma Swaraj paid a courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and held a bilateral meeting with Senior Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs. The two sides recalled the results of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's fruitful official visit to India in January this year.
