(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for August 29, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 1,082 vehicles and found 103 vehicles violating the law (76% motorcycles), 34 education vehicles and 69 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 551 helmets and goggles were inspected on August 29, 37 education helmets were inspected and 43 helmets were fined.
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on August 29, 2018 issued a notification on the reminder of the payment of property tax 2018, which will close on September 30. This.
The warning comes after the General Department of Taxation observed that some property owners have not yet fulfilled their tax declaration duties.
The General Department of Taxation stressed that "In order to promote the payment of property tax for 2018, it is possible to be highly effective and avoid congestion, to rush to declare tax on the due date, which may lead to inactivity." For any reason, the General Department of Taxation would like to remind all property owners who have not yet fulfilled their tax payment duties, please hurry to declare your tax payment on September 30, 2018.
The tax also states that for failing to submit the required documents on time, the property owner will be penalized.
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Commissioner, Major General Chuon Narin, on August 29, 2018, responded to Facebook users who accused him of stealing his stall many times and there was no evidence, but the police did not That work is untrue, with the intention of completely destroying the reputation of the Sihanoukville police force.
The General Commissioner confirmed that regarding the burglary of Ms. Chamroeun Chanlyda 3 times, the police conducted two raids, the first time arresting 2 children and the second time arresting 5 children. The case was sent to the provincial court, but the juveniles were convicted. At that time, the prosecutor's office of the provincial court educated and released them.
In fact, on the afternoon of August 29, 2018, Lieutenant Colonel Sam Prak, Police Chief of Sangkat 4 Administration Post, led a group of journalists to inspect the location of the pharmacy directly south of the two lions roundabout. The pharmacy is still open as a small market, a small mart selling medicine and other items, but the owner has built another stall in the west corner, shaped like a container, tucked into the wrong side of the public road.
The Sangkat 4 Administrative Police Chief confirmed that the municipal / provincial authorities had previously instructed him to dismantle the stall, but he did not listen, and the people in the shop would not want to speak to the authorities. Since instructing him to dismantle the stall, he has been unhappy with the authorities.
According to the post chief, Chamroeun Chanlida's pharmacy has a lot of valuables, but at night it is locked and there are no guards or security guards on the sidewalk. The opportunity for the wicked or street children to sneak up to sleep on the roof of the stall at night, take the opportunity to dig the roof to get the material.
Regarding the information that Ms. Chamroeun Chanlida posted a message insulting the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police, ignoring her complaint, it is not true. Therefore, Major General Chuon Narin, Sihanoukville Provincial Police Commissioner, would like to completely reject.
Please be informed that today, the Sihanoukville Provincial Police Force in all fields under the leadership of Major General Chuon Narin has been doing the most diligent work that the general people in the province have seen and supported.
The Khmer Literature Festival will be held again in Battambang in the middle of next month!
(Phnom Penh): A group of Khmer poets and a committee of the organizing committee of the Khmer Literature Festival met to inaugurate an informal festival at the ST 63 Bassac restaurant recently. This unofficial opening ceremony was held to give a short presentation about the second Khmer Literature Festival, the detailed program in the whole festival and the conditions for attending and announcing the opening of the festival.
The Khmer Literature Festival will be back again after the success of the first Khmer Literature Festival in Siem Reap last year. The second festival will be held in Battambang, a province rich in culture and civilization since ancient times. The whole program will start from 21 to 23 September 2018 at various locations in Battambang.
Under the theme "Past, Present and Future of Khmer Literature", the second edition of the Khmer Literature Festival has three main objectives: 1: To cultivate a love of national literature in Cambodia, 2: To promote the honor and values of Khmer writers in Cambodia. In the society and 3: increase the opportunity to communicate and expand the scope of the market for writers.
Sophina, Founder of the Khmer Literature Festival, said: “We believe that when poets, writers, students, publishing houses, literary agencies, artists and the entire community come together to discuss literary issues, new ideas Will run towards the pen.
Ms. Sophina added that the new collaboration will create a wide range of literary activities. All of these activities will lead us to excellence and the belief that we can make progress for the culture of literature.
Meanwhile, Suong Mak, who is also the author and director of the festival's organizing committee, said: "We need the unity of the same writers to raise the value of the writers by the writers themselves."
Mr. Suong Mak continued, "We believe that if we know how to value ourselves, others will value us." That is why we together created this literary festival to reflect the solidarity of the writers in raising the value of the writers and promoting the reading habits in Cambodia.
As for Suon Sotheara, another writer and organizer, he said excitedly: "I am very happy that this year's festival is held in Battambang, because it is a province rich in artists, history and art. Culture. I hope that the people in Battambang will participate in large numbers.
Please be informed that the 2nd Khmer Literature Festival will bring many special programs such as: Literature Discussion Forum, Creative Writing Workshop, Local Reading Program, Book and Book Sale, Short Story and Poetry Contest, Bicycle and Poetry Program The play tells the story of "Kolap Pailin", cultural visits, as well as many other performing arts performances. The festival is open to the public.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Visits and Brings Donations from Prince Real Estate Charitable Foundation to 700 Flood Victims in Batheay District
(Kampong Cham): About 700 flood-affected families living in Batheay District, Kampong Cham Province were visited by Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and brought food donations from Prince Real Estate Charitable Foundation. Prince Real Estate (Cambodia) Group Mr. Lee Min distributed the gifts to the people.
During the meeting and visiting people living in Tuol Chan village, Chbar Ampov commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, this morning, August 29, 2018, the Governor of Kampong Cham province said that a total of more than 30,000 people were affected by the floods. To this day, the water level continues to rise above the emergency level. According to the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, the water will continue to rise for the next three days before receding.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun added that in order to alleviate the hardships of the people, the provincial authorities and the Prince Real Estate Charitable Foundation brought a generous gift to distribute to the people, each family received 1 bag of rice, 1 bag of fish, 1 bag of fish and 1 box of noodles. The total amount of charitable donations distributed to the victims was $ 20,000.
Please be informed that Kampong Cham province has suffered from floods since July 30 so far, causing about 32,000 people to face problems. About 16 people were killed and 54 others were seriously injured and a large number of crops and livestock were damaged. Chinese emperor denies plans to set up military base in Afghanistan
