Bomb blast in western Iraq "kills 8, injures 16"
A car bomb had exploded at an Iraqi police recruiting center at Kisak, west of Anbar province, killing at least eight people and wounding 16 others. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday afternoon, August 29, 2018.
According to Iraqi authorities, one of the assailants drove an explosive device into the checkpoint, which was controlled by Iranian military forces and pro-Baghdad militants, while the dead included militants. Five people were killed and three others were injured, and the death toll is expected to rise as some of the injured are in critical condition.
