The Indian Foreign Minister praised the idea of establishing a "Supreme Advisory Council" during a courtesy call on Senior Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. This morning, August 29, 2018.
According to Ket Sophan, a spokeswoman for the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during this morning's meeting, Shusma Swaraj praised the election process in Cambodia, which went well and many people went out. Vote. She considered the overwhelming turnout as a decision to maintain peace in Cambodia.
The Indian Foreign Minister also congratulated the successful election process in Cambodia and congratulated Samdech Techo Hun Sen on his success in leading the new government.
"It is a great initiative for national reconciliation for non-elected political parties to participate in the decision-making process," Ket Sophan was quoted as saying by the Indian Foreign Minister. Other things of the new government.
In this morning's meeting, Senior Minister Prak Sokhon also highlighted the favorable political environment in Cambodia in recent times by the release of convicted politicians, demonstrating Samdech Techo's spirit of national reconciliation. Hun Sen too.
It should be noted that the opening of another new page of history for the benefit of the whole nation of Cambodia, on August 21, yesterday, the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, decided to establish the "Supreme Advisory Council". Agree from the political parties that participated in the election of 15 members of the 6th legislature.
The "Supreme Advisory Council" is composed of parties that participated in the sixth mandate election with the approval of the Prime Minister. Each party has two representatives, who are delegates and appointed by Royal Decree proposed by the Prime Minister (with the same rank as Senior Minister and Minister).
The President of the Supreme Council shall follow the principle of rotating once a month according to the number of the voter list. The "Supreme Advisory Council" has a secretariat, with officials from the Council of Ministers and an official from each party. The secretariat and meeting place are in the Peace Palace.
The "Supreme Advisory Council" shall meet once a month, convened by the chairperson, and meet with the Prime Minister every six months, or as required by the Prime Minister, in the meantime, as convened by the director. Minister.
This "Supreme Advisory Council" will be completed in accordance with the mandate of the Royal Government of the sixth legislature. Products for two well-known brands from abroad are now available in the Cambodian market
