(Preah Sihanouk): After the preliminary investigation was completed, the Chinese and Cambodian police forces jointly enforced the law to arrest 18 Chinese nationals involved in crimes in Sihanoukville on August 24, 2018. Go recently.
According to Chinese-language newspapers, China has sent troops to cooperate with the Chinese embassy. They joined the Cambodian police force to focus on the arrest of Chinese people involved in illegal activities in Sihanoukville.
Earlier, Chinese and Cambodian police also launched a number of joint operations to crack down on telecommunications fraud and illegal gambling. Joint enforcement of laws against certain areas of crime remains a rarity, highlighting the seriousness of Sihanoukville's problems. And show the respect and punishment of the Chinese side for the abuse of the Chinese people in Sihanoukville.
China pays close attention to crime in Sihanoukville In recent years, with the rapid development of Sihanoukville economy, many Chinese and Chinese companies have invested and lived there. Most of them obey the law, but there are some who are involved in industries such as pornography and drugs that Cambodia has banned. Therefore, the Chinese side is very interested in this issue.
Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Xin Po has spoken publicly on several occasions, calling on all foreigners to abide by the laws of the state in the region, fully respecting the traditions and customs of the people and living appropriately. With local people.
However, some people are not of high quality and even engage in illegal activities abroad. Some people engage in illegal gambling, some drink and disturb public order, some ignore traffic laws and cause injuries.
"Compared to the millions of Chinese tourists, these people are very small, but they have seriously damaged the image of the Chinese people," the ambassador stressed. "For these people, the attitude of the Chinese side is clear, and we support the relevant departments of the Cambodian government to deal with the law."
Enforcement of the two countries' common law is expected to continue. A Chinese man who has been in Cambodia for many years says that because of the small number of Chinese in Sihanoukville, the whole image of the Chinese is being destroyed in Cambodia. The implementation of this joint law is a presumption of compliance between the two governments by public opinion.
(Preah Vihear): National Road No. 94, a type of red gravel road that was badly damaged in two places, has now been repaired 100% and allowed people to travel as usual. From August 28, 2018.
This section of National Road No. 94 connecting from Chhep district town to Kampong Sralou commune, Chhep district, Preah Vihear province was badly damaged in two places, PK54-55, 150 meters long, due to rain for a whole month. Past
Mr. Samleang Try, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, told the news agency this morning, August 29, 2018 that under the direct guidance of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, National Road No. 94. PK54-55 is now 100% repaired and put back into operation, but the director of the department has also assigned a regular maintenance staff.
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of August 28, at the Ministry of National Assembly-National Assembly Relations and Inspection, Ms. Kittisang Dr. Men Sam An, Minister, received a working delegation from the Vietnam-Cambodia Friendship Association led by Mr. Vo Mao, President of the Association.
