Join to protect health! CamControl Battambang Provides Food Safety Education at Schools in Samlot District
(Battambang): Camcontrol Officer, Battambang Branch, on August 28, 2018, in collaboration with Samlot District Hall and Giz under the EU DAR project, presented a program on education, promotion, food safety and control of food and beverage sales in schools. Study in Samlot district, Battambang province.
Mr. Hak Sokrin, President of CamControl Branch, said that in collaboration with Giz under the EU DAR project, there will be coordination and preparation from Samlot District Hall and to provide knowledge to the general public, especially teachers, students in all schools. Where professional officers participate in presentations on food safety education programs and monitor food and beverage sales at schools.
Mr. President stated that in this program, professional officers visited the schools in the following programs: in the morning at Spong Chrov Krom Primary School in O'Sramil Krom village, O'Samrel commune, Samlot district, and in the afternoon at O'Chrab Primary School in the village. Chhor Kar, Samlot commune, Samlot district.
The program was led by Mr. Pich Chenda, Head of CamControl at Port 400 in Samlot District, with the participation of representatives of district governors, district health officials, commune councils, school principals, teachers, students, and more than 100 school vendors.
He added that the outreach program will continue in other places as per the practice so that people can better understand the health effects of food sold on the market or other places, especially in schools in urban and rural areas. .
On the morning of August 29, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Mr. Kem Sokha is still a convict and has not yet become a prisoner. No, so there is no request for release.
