Kun Nhem Meets Experts in Africa to Test Containers to Control Illegal Goods
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, met with professional officials from various countries in Africa to exchange and learn from each other's experiences. Inspect containers to prevent illegal goods such as drugs.
This is the first meeting of the General Department of Customs and Excise with law enforcement officials from countries in Africa within the framework of the container inspection program. The meeting aims to exchange work experience, share confidential information with relevant law enforcement officials in order to further strengthen regional and international cooperation.
The Container Control Program is a joint project organized by the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) and the World Customs Organization (WCO) and aims to prevent and suppress drug trafficking, wildlife and transnational crime. Other. Currently, nearly 50 countries are participating in this program.
For the future and to improve work efficiency in this context, Mr. Kun Nhim also supported and asked the law enforcement officers of the countries participating in this program to communicate and cooperate more closely under this program to control the container using the relevant mechanisms. Others of the United Nations and the World Customs Organization.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Javier Montano also thanked Dr. Kun Nhim for his support and warm welcome to the delegation to visit and share experiences at the Customs and Excise Department of the International Airport (Phnom Penh International Airport and Siem Reap International Airport). ) And Sihanoukville International Port Customs and Excise Branch.
