Cambodian Representations in China, Malaysia, Indonesia and the Cambodian Consulate General in Shanghai Intervene to Help 26 Cambodians Return Home
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on August 28, 2018 issued a press release stating that the Cambodian Embassy in China, Malaysia, Indonesia and the Cambodian Consulate General in Shanghai, China has continued to intervene to rescue 26 Cambodians back home.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs:
1: The Cambodian Embassy in China cooperated with the Chinese authorities to intervene, rescue and organize the repatriation of seven Cambodian women who were tricked into marrying Chinese men illegally. In China, they returned to Cambodia on August 9 and 23, 2018.
2: The Embassy of Cambodia in Malaysia cooperated with the competent authorities of Malaysia to organize the repatriation of 7 Cambodian workers (1 female) from Kratie, Kandal, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum and Battambang provinces. Working illegally in Malaysia and intending to return to Cambodia. The seven workers returned to Cambodia between August 4 and 15, 2018.
3: The Cambodian Embassy in Indonesia facilitated the repatriation of two Cambodian fishermen, 28 years old and 36 years old, from Kampong Thom Province, who were detained by the Indonesian authorities after their fishing boat entered. In Indonesian waters. The two workers returned to Cambodia on the evening of August 15, 2018.
