(Stung Treng): A poor woman living in Chhwang village, Sam Ang commune, Thala Borivat district, Stung Treng province, had a miscarriage but had no way to go to the hospital this morning, August 27, 2018.
Seeing this situation and receiving information immediately, Brigadier General Ieng Vandy, Commander of the Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie, sent a car to transport the woman to the hospital to give birth.
This humanitarian act was underlined by Brigadier General Commander under the direction and order of General Sao Sokha, Acting Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, without overlooking any citizen. Do not allow any citizen to suffer, all must be taken care of.
