(Phnom Penh): Prudential Cambodia, one of the leading life insurance companies in Cambodia, recently sold its 150,000th insurance policy, a significant achievement in the field of life insurance in Cambodia and reflecting the public's confidence. For the company as well as the company's products.
Since launching its business in 2013, Prudential Cambodia has been urging people to focus on planning for the future. Therefore, the achievement of this brilliant achievement in five years shows the company's efforts to raise awareness of the Cambodian people about life insurance services and the need for long-term financial planning. .
David Nutman, CEO of Prudential Cambodia, thanked the company's customers for giving them the confidence to support them toward their financial goals.
"We truly thank you for your support of Prudential Cambodia, which has helped us become a leader in the life insurance industry in Cambodia," he said. With the trust and confidence of all of you, we have been able to achieve the achievement of issuing 150,000 insurance policies since 2013. This is a significant increase compared to the same period last year when we issued 100,000 insurance policies.
"This achievement would not have been possible without the hard work and dedication of our staff, agencies and partner banks across Cambodia," he said. "We remain committed to providing world-class life insurance products that are tailored to the specific needs of the Cambodian people and to promote Cambodia's long-term economic growth."
