PEC Kampong Thom: 80% of Kampong Thom voters go to the polls without coercion
(Kampong Thom): The meeting to review the work of the 6th National Assembly election on August 26, 2018 confirmed that in the last National Assembly election, 80% of the people in Kampong Thom province among those who have Names on the voter list went to the polls voluntarily without coercion.
The review meeting was chaired by Mr. Sok Hay, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Mr. Preng Savuth, Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Election Committee (PEC) with the participation of representatives of local authorities, representatives of political parties, representatives of NGOs, the Armed Forces. And more than 500 relevant officials.
Mr. Loung Sony, Vice President of PEC, Kampong Thom Province, confirmed that the election process has a step-by-step process according to the calendar, especially the 14-day election campaign process, including the preparation of the voter list, the reception of election observers, the distribution. Election leaflets, election campaigns, polls and vote counting.
After the intervention of the Armed Forces, as well as the participation of municipal, district, commune and sangkat administrations from political parties, non-governmental organizations related to the parliamentary election process.
Mr. Preng Savuth, Chairman of the Provincial Election Commission, said that overall, the parliamentary election was free and fair, non-violent and non-threatening, and had a better atmosphere than the previous election. In the past, 80% of the people on the voter list went to the polls to vote for their political party at their own discretion and without coercion.
Mr. Sok Hay praised and appreciated the leadership, staff and officials at all levels of the Provincial Election Commission, Municipal Administration, Municipalities, Armed Forces and all stakeholders who work hard to ensure security and order. The work of the 6th parliamentary election went smoothly.
He thanked the representatives of political parties, national observers, non-governmental organizations and other stakeholders for their joint implementation and implementation of laws, regulations, procedures, and ethics, despite minor problems and irregularities. In general, the process of the 6th National Assembly election in Kampong Thom province was highly valued and considered to be successful.
