National Bank of Cambodia and State Bank of Vietnam hold bilateral meeting to strengthen cooperation and friendly relations between the two central banks
The bilateral meeting is held annually with the aim of strengthening cooperation and friendly relations between the two central banks to contribute to the development of the banking sector as well as the economy in both Cambodia and Vietnam.
The meeting was successful and fruitful, with the two central bank leaders discussing the economic and banking situation of the two countries and praising the progress of cooperation over the past year.
Under the MoU, which was updated in February 2017, the cooperation of the two central banks has expanded to enhance the exchange of experiences and mutual information, strengthen cooperation on joint work, such as oversight of existing banks. Cross-border operations in both countries and the development of payment system connectivity as well as human resource development.
Currently, the Cambodian banking system has five Vietnamese bank branches operating and contributing to the investment of the Cambodian economy. In addition, the meeting also set priorities for strengthening and expanding traditional cooperation in a number of areas, especially with regard to the continued exchange of experiences on core work, including:
1. Management of monetary policy and promoting the use of the national currency. 2: Development and management of financial technology. 3: Improving the financial environment and contributing to poverty reduction 4: Strengthening bank controls.
In addition, the State Bank of Vietnam will continue to increase scholarships for National Bank of Cambodia officials for master's and doctoral studies in Vietnam. Tycoon Ly Hour: Cambodia still has the most extensive investment opportunities in the real estate sector between ASEAN countries!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Oknha Ly Hour, President of the Cambodian Association of Housing Developers, highlighted the positive signs that Cambodia is hosting the 2018 ASEAN Real Estate Conference and Exhibition, which shows the cooperation of investors in the ASEAN region and in the world.
This statement was made by Mr. Oknha Ly Hour on August 24, 2018 on the occasion of his participation in the 2018 ASEAN Real Estate Conference and Exhibition, which was also presided over by Mr. Mey Van, Royal Delegate. The government is in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Financial Industry of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Dr. Kim Heang, President of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Appraisers, as well as many national and international guests.
Mr. Oknha Ly Hour stated that "The organization of the 2018 ASEAN Real Estate Conference and Exhibition, Cambodia is hosting this event in order to show the cooperation of investors in the ASEAN region and other countries as trading partners and To show the progress of the real estate sector and to disseminate the scope of the real estate sector in Cambodia to investors in the country as well as in ASEAN as a whole.
Tycoon Ly Hour briefed national and international participants on the progress and development of Cambodia today. He said that Cambodia is now a peaceful country, developed, free market, especially the continuous development of the real estate sector, with high-rise buildings, housing, schools and other infrastructure.
He added that in addition, the real estate sector is a sector that is prominent and has grown significantly, and national and international investors are very interested in this sector. Compared to countries in the ASEAN region, Cambodia still has opportunities. In extensive investment in real estate and infrastructure.
He said that the factors that claim that Cambodia is a developing country and a country with the right vision and a country that provides a warm confidence in investment is focused on factors such as:
1. Macroeconomic stability is 7% annually. 2. Government supports business. 3. Investment is competitive. 4. Investment promotion agencies provide one-stop-shop services. Local and international markets. 6. Investment protection. 7. Adequate infrastructure and strategic location. 8. Economic sector support. 9. Adequate labor resources and favorable geographical location.
He called on investors, both domestic and foreign, to look and consider investing in Cambodia, a country with a strategic location as well as the right vision for investment, especially in the real estate sector. Infrastructure to grow and prioritize benefits for long-term investors.
Mr. Mey Van also stated that the positive aspects of this program (ASEAN Real Estate Conference and Exhibition 2018) have helped to promote the development and economic growth of Cambodia to the 10 ASEAN countries, including the world. See Cambodia's economic growth with this decade.
He added that the program will attract investors from many countries to invest in Cambodia in addition to the five countries currently investing.
Dr. Kim Heang said that the ASEAN Real Estate Agents Association's Conference and Expo program promotes Cambodia's economic development to ASEAN and will help share experiences between investors from different countries. Come to build relationships and make it easier to buy real estate in other countries.
According to a report by the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, in December 2017, there were 3,052 real estate investments in 11 million square meters, with an estimated investment value of $ 6 billion. America. In the first half of 2018, there were a total of 1,643 projects on an area of more than 5 million square meters, worth an estimated 2 billion US dollars.
Asia Europe University Basic Year Students Visit Royal School of Administration
(Phnom Penh): About 130 students of all special subjects of the basic year of Asia-Europe University led by Mr. Sous Sophea, Head of the Department of Basic Education of Asia-Europe University, on the afternoon of August 24, visited the Royal School. Administration in Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The purpose of this study tour is for students to learn about the history, mission, structure, role, duties, process, legislation, as well as many other important points that this institution has fulfilled in the past to the present.
Mr. Sous Sophea said that every year, Asia-Europe University always leads students to study in various ministries and institutions in order to link the study to practice in order to gain more new experiences and knowledge for students. .
He also said that the Royal School of Administration has completed the mission of training and developing human resources and specialists with high skills and professional conscience to help implement the mission of good governance, improve the quality, transparency and service to the people. High efficiency.
The Royal School of Administration was established for the first time in the history of Cambodia in 1914 by Royal Kram No. 85-NS dated March 29, 1956, on the initiative of His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King Father of National Independence. Yes, Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King of Cambodia. However, when it was first established, it was not called the Royal School of Administration, it was called a court that trained civil servants.
From 1995 to 2013, the Royal School of Administration was under the Office of the Council of Ministers, and from 2013 to the present under the Ministry of Public Function.
Mr. Tep Kosal, Director of the First Training Department of the Royal School of Administration, also gave a presentation on the selection criteria for civil servants, the process of selecting civil servants, the preparation for the civil service examination, and explained the questions raised by students in detail. Well.
