(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, together with Mr. Sok Puthivuth, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, Deputy Governor and colleagues on August 25, 2018, inspected the rice fields affected by Drought in Ta Vong village, Punley commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province to check the actual situation and discuss to find a solution.
According to a report by the Banteay Meanchey Department of Agriculture, 5,469 hectares of paddy fields, including early-season rice, medium-season paddy and heavy paddy, were affected by the drought and more than 8,000 hectares were affected by floods. According to the report, it is currently raining, which could save a large amount of rice. In particular, the flood has receded back to normal.
