(Phnom Penh): On August 25, Cambodians of Chinese descent held a ceremony to offer water offerings or Chinese Pchum Festival to pray for happiness, prosperity and a prosperous business for their families.
But some families sacrifice again in the evening according to their faith and resources. After the cremation, they still burn sacrificial paper, money, gold, silver, clothes and other paper offerings such as passports, visas, plane tickets, cars, houses and so on.
The arrangement of the offerings in this water offering ceremony is not different from the New Year offering ceremony moving into the New Year. Through previous studies, we see that this ceremony is organized in four main concepts:
First, the dedication of Kosal to the ancestors and Pret
Second, thanks to the river or sea, which has always helped to improve livelihoods through fisheries, agriculture and trade.
Third, reunion after the New Year for the past 6 months to share wisdom and experiences in daily life and continue the vision for the future.
Fourthly, declare an emergency or provide emergency information to those who live near the waterfront that the water is starting to rise.
