(Phnom Penh): The case of a former military officer and a former commune official who swindled people's money and falsified land purchase documents in Kampot province will be heard by the Court of Appeal this weekend.
The hearing on the afternoon of 22 August was chaired by Mr. Plang Samnang, President of the Trial Chamber, Mr. Nuon Ratana and Ms. Kim Dany as Advisory Judges, and Ms. Yin Sokuntheary as Representative of the Prosecutor General.
However, during the hearing, the court heard only the appeals of the accused and the plaintiffs in relation to compensation and mental illness, while the appeals of the two prosecutors were not raised. Debate for the court to know clearly, just to remind the prosecutor's appeal, a case will be decided, but the appeal of the parties until the end of the trial.
It was observed that the President of the Council tried to question only the civil compensation, which was the appeal of the parties, while the appeal of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court Prosecutor did not seem to be ignored.
At the conclusion, Ms. Yin Sokuntheary, the Deputy Prosecutor of the Trial Chamber, requested the Council to consider the appeal of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court Prosecutor as well, as the Phnom Penh Municipal Prosecutor's appeal considered the sentence to imprisonment. The accused were too light-hearted and did not deserve to be punished for their crimes against the people.
During the hearing, the defendants replied that they did not act as charged, but they did not have any witnesses and exculpatory evidence, only to name the fine people who died in the accident. In order for me to stand up and take responsibility before the law instead of them who are living.
The lawyers representing the victims said that they had submitted strong evidence to the court, including a forged letter used by the defendants to defraud them, as well as a forensic certificate from the National Police. The authorities' stamp is a fake letter.
In addition, the victim also has documents confirming that the accused actually received their money through several checks.
Victims' lawyers hope that the Court of Appeal will be able to provide justice to their clients without following the example of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
After the hearing, the court postponed the announcement of the verdict in the case to the morning of August 28, 2018.
It should be reminded that Mr. Koy Sao, Trial Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued Criminal Judgment No. 1194 "M" dated 27 April 2018 and Criminal Judgment No. 1195 dated 27 April 2018 convicted the accused. The first name is Sun Seang, male, 48 years old, occupation is a military officer and the second name is Heng San, male, 45 years old, a former member of Trapeang Phleang Commune Council, Chhouk District, Kampot Province.
Case 1: The two defendants were sentenced to six months in prison, with all sentences suspended and no longer required to serve their sentences in prison for fraud and requiring the defendants to jointly reimburse the plaintiffs. $ 50,000 and $ 5,000 compensation were paid during 2013 in Phnom Penh in accordance with Articles 377 and 378 of the Penal Code.
Case 2: Conviction of 3 defendants sentenced to 1 year and 6 months imprisonment, but only 6 months imprisonment in the first prison for fingerprint fraud Citizens' signatures and seals of the authorities in Kampot province, secondly for using fake letters and thirdly for fraud committed during 2013 in Phnom Penh according to Article 626, Article 627, Article 628, Article 377 and Article 378 of the Penal Code.
