(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Economy and Finance on August 24, 2018 issued a joint statement calling on all microfinance institutions to favor interest rates, defer repayments. And not to confiscate the property of the people affected by the floods, that is, to alleviate the financial risks that may arise from the floods.
The issuance of the statement between the two institutions was made in response to the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who called on the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Economy and Finance to work with financial institutions to ease the repayment period or rate. Interest on flood victims.
According to a statement from the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Economy and Finance, banking and microfinance institutions are encouraged to:
1: Continue to provide credit carefully and have a soft settlement mechanism for customers affected by the actual flood to maintain the stability and strength of the financial sector.
2. Continue to examine and evaluate the repayment ability of farmers affected by the flood accident as a basis for reducing the repayment period, lowering the interest rate or not taking interest for any period and not confiscating the property of farmers. As well as provide appropriate solutions.
3. Continue to monitor the situation and the impact of the flood on the people and provide the necessary support in accordance with the actual circumstances.
Please note that the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on August 23, said, "I also take this opportunity to call on the National Bank, the Ministry of Economy and Finance to work with microfinance institutions to favor the people who face "Will flood by reducing the repayment period or reduce interest-free within a certain period."
Samdech Techo further stated that these mechanisms to help reduce difficulties because now the rice he grows his crops are damaged. Therefore, the possibility of him repaying on time is not possible, please do not confiscate his property, instead be tolerant of him, delay repayment and do not charge interest. China and India have agreed to expand military ties amid trade disputes With the United States
