APSARA Authority calls on people from all walks of life to plant trees in Angkor Park
(Siem Reap): The restoration of forest cover in Angkor resort is one of the priority tasks in the conservation and sustainable development of Angkor resort. At the same time, APSARA Authority calls on people from all walks of life to plant trees in Angkor Park Forest as well.
In fact, 1,000 hybrid saplings were replanted on August 23, 2018 in the forest area south of Banteay Kdei, and such large-scale saplings were planted as part of the daily work of the Department of Forestry Management. Cultural and environmental landscape of APSARA Authority.
Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, Mr. Hang Pov, who led the tree planting program with the participation of APSARA Authority staff, heritage police and park rangers, said that this replanting is very important because the land in Angkor Part Mostly sandy and the foundation of the temple also needs groundwater moisture to keep the foundation of the temple stable.
In addition, the forest has made the cultural landscape in the Angkor area more attractive, and many tourists are satisfied with this beautiful green landscape. Nowadays, some tourists are interested in cycling in the forest, which is an important part of tourism.
In order for people from all walks of life to have the opportunity to participate in planting saplings in the Angkor Park forest, as well as to encourage forest conservation, Mr. Hang Pov stated that in principle, APSARA Authority wants the participation of all circles to participate in restoring forest cover. Again, especially in the Angkor resort area, because this is not the exclusive duty of the APSARA Authority, but the shared responsibility of all citizens.
Therefore, all people in or outside of Siem Reap can request the seedlings or seedlings from the APSARA Authority to plant at home, village, institution or company. In addition, they can also plant saplings in the forest of Angkor Park by simply contacting the forestry officer to arrange the planting site.
It should be noted that the area where the seedlings are planted is the land that the APSARA Authority has resolved the policy with the people to replant the seedlings. Court orders release of military officer who hit the head of a fried meatball seller with a gun in Sen Sok district
(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Municipal Prison (PJ) officials said that four and a half military officers who used a pistol to hit the head of a fried meatball seller in Sen Sok district were released by Investigating Judge Ros Piseth of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. Out of jail temporarily.
Judge Ros Piseth ordered the release of Nuon Po, 49, a four-and-a-half-year-old military officer with the title of Deputy Chief of Training Office of the Deception Unit, ID number 059051, on 20 August. 2018.
It should be reminded that the police force of Sen Sok district arrested the suspect on the night of August 2, 2018 after the suspect took a P08 handgun No. 5854 and hit the victim's head. The cause of the violence started from a traffic accident when a friend of the suspect drove a Camry Whale under the influence of alcohol and hit the victim's meatball tuk tuk, which occurred in front of Wat Samrong Andet floating on the concrete road, Factory Village 1, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok.
The suspect then drove a Pros car to intervene, and the victim threw stones at the car window, causing violence to the victim.
Tep Vanny, a Boeung Kak Lake land activist who has just been released from prison, along with three other Boeung Kak Lake activists out of six defendants, re-entered the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the morning of August 24, 2018 to confront The trial of another case involving them in connection with the "insult and death threat" case filed by former Boeung Kak Lake woman Ly Mom.
The six Boeung Kak Lake women accused in this case include Tep Vanny, Heng Mom, Nget Khun, Chheng Leap, Kong Chantha and Tol Srey Pov, who were sued by Ly Mom. Accused of public insult and death threats in 2012.
During the trial, the trial judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court decided to drop the charges of public defamation, but sentenced the six defendants to six months in prison each for "threatening to kill." But the sentence was suspended in prison.
However, Tep Vanny, one of the six defendants, did not agree with the Phnom Penh Municipal Court's decision. She told reporters after the hearing that she would appeal to the Court of Appeal in the near future.
Following the Royal Decree and the release order, Boeung Kak Lake community land activist Tep Vanny was released from "M2" prison at around 9 pm on August 20, 2018. Nearly 30,000 Families in Prey Veng Province Affected by Floods, Senior Minister Nhim Vanda Tells Authorities to Monitor Regularly to Help Victims
(Prey Veng): Prey Veng, a province along the Mekong River, is prone to floods every year, causing damage to people's homes, property and crops, as well as public infrastructure, which requires a response. Immediate response to the disaster, including post-flood rehabilitation.
On the morning of August 24, 2018, Senior Minister Nhim Vanda, Permanent Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, presided over the 7-month disaster review meeting and the direction of Prey Veng province.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Duch Kunthea, Deputy Governor of Prey Veng Province, said that as of August 23, the maximum water level was 6.84 meters, while the emergency level was 7.50 meters higher than in 2017, which was higher than 1. 24 meters. As for the rain situation, all cities, districts, communes and sangkats in the province were affected by the rain, but some communes also experienced drought.
The deputy governor confirmed that the water level above affected 11 districts in 13 communes, with 29,225 families evacuated to 370 families and drowning. 6 water floods and flooding of houses, rice crops, mixed crops, health centers, roads, wells, dams, canals, etc. To be rehabilitated after the flood.
At the same time, Senior Minister Nhim Vanda said that not only Cambodia but also many other countries have been suffering from natural disasters such as floods, hurricanes, etc., which have caused serious disasters to the people. India, for example, is experiencing floods in Hawaii, the United States is experiencing hurricanes, typhoons, etc.
The senior minister added that the world is experiencing alarming climate change, which is causing more and more dangers that are difficult to cope with. Senior Minister Nhim Vanda instructed the Prey Veng Provincial Disaster Management Committee to regularly monitor the situation of natural disasters and take measures to respond immediately to this disaster.
