Beware of health! Camcontrol officers found more than 400 kilograms of pig blood containing chemicals in Chbar Ampov market and Chbar Ampov vegetable market
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bun Chamroeun, Head of Camcontrol Branch of Phnom Penh International Port, at dawn on August 24, 2018, led his forces in cooperation with Chbar Ampov Market and Chbar Ampov Vegetable Market Commission to inspect and confiscate pig blood found. Contains banned chemicals (Borax).
Mr. Bun Chamroeun said that during the operation, CamControl officers confiscated 420.8 kilograms of pig's blood from six pork stalls after a preliminary test by CamControl officers found the presence of banned chemicals in the blood. The pigs will have the owners of the six stalls make a guarantee contract to stop using this chemical. If they refuse to resign, they will continue to sell products containing chemicals and will be punished according to the law in force.
After signing a contract with the CamControl officer, the owners of the six stalls agreed to the request of the CamControl officer to stop mixing banned chemicals into the pig's blood.
The branch manager also explained to all pig slaughtering traders to pay high attention to food safety, please do not take chemicals mixed in the pig's blood, because if we eat it, it will damage our health "Please traders do not sell "Prohibited chemicals, we need money, but buyers need them to be healthy."
Please also note that this inspection was carried out on 10 stalls selling pig blood in the two markets above.
