(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, wrote an interesting article on his official Facebook page! Fresh News Unit would like to publish to the full readers as follows:
Editorial: Things get stuck and fall
Better than what the ruling party has done in the past and plans to continue to gain the support of the electorate. The exam for the sixth term of the Royal Government was already held on July 29. More than 83% of registered voters have exercised their political rights to elect a leader for the next five years.
The Cambodian People's Party is the party that passed the exam. With a landslide victory, he won all 125 seats in the National Assembly. Because the majority of the people believe in the party's ability to maintain peace, stability and promote the development of the country in the past and beyond. It means that the people voted for peace, stability and development. The people voted for sustainability.
The people have decided to use the ballot instead of following the call of some extremist politicians who want to block the democratic process through boycotts of elections, violence, separatism and attempts to take over the fate of another country.
Students who pass this year will receive a degree recognizing their abilities and paving the way for higher education, which is higher, more difficult, and requires more effort to succeed. Exams from college in the next few years.
The CPP is no different. Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen was appointed by the King of Cambodia as the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia on Friday, August 17. Samdech will have to match the composition of the Royal Government of the sixth mandate to lead the implementation of the political program with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 as the core.
There is no doubt that the new government will redouble its efforts to meet the aspirations and expectations as well as the overwhelming trust of the electorate. Many world leaders have congratulated and wished the new government success in fulfilling its mandate.
But just like wishing the students who are taking the exam today, one blessing is not enough. Self-effort to achieve new achievements for the nation and the people is important if the CPP wants to maintain the honor of continuing to serve the people as the ruling party for the next term.
