General Nem Sovath Leads a Working Group to Hold a Meeting on Building Achievements in the Win-Win Monument
(Phnom Penh): General Nem Sovath, Director General of the General Department of Politics and Foreign Affairs and Chairman of the Working Group on Research and Construction of the Win-Win Monument, this morning, August 23, 2018, led the working group to open a meeting related to the construction. Achievement area in the win-win monument at the meeting hall of the Ministry of National Defense.
The meeting was also attended by representatives of the Cambodian Red Cross, representatives from the SIMAC unit and several win-win monument construction teams.
Lt. Gen. Nem Sovathdey also outlined key projects to organize an exhibition of the process of implementing a win-win policy and other projects to be inaugurated on the day of the official inauguration of the Victory Monument, which will be held. Up on December 29, 2018.
Speaking on that occasion, General Nem Sovath also revealed many other important projects in the construction of a win-win monument and presented various important plans to organize an exhibition and present as Various achievements of win-win politics under the wise and correct leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
After the meeting related to the construction of the achievement area in the Victory Monument, General Nem Sovath also led the team and stakeholders from other institutions to inspect the construction process at the Victory Monument.
CamControl officers continue to inspect petrol stations / depots in Meanchey district, found 2 petrol stations selling less than liters of fuel
(Phnom Penh): On August 23, 2018, CamControl officers continued to inspect 6 gas stations and depots in Meanchey district. Of the six stations and depots, four complied with the quality and measurement standards, while two depots did not have the right amount of fuel to meet the measurement standards.
The inspection at the gas station and depot was led by Mr. Nguon Somlyvong, Deputy Director of the Department in collaboration with the professional officers of the laboratory. These inspections are aimed at protecting the economic interests of consumers, protecting the machinery of all types of vehicles and protecting the environment arising from improper fuel consumption, and in particular to prevent fraud.
According to Mr. Nguon Somlyvong, the quality and quantity control is based on on-site monitoring equipment, such as a caliper tank with a specific size for measuring the amount of oil fired from the counter in different sizes, with a capacity of 5 liters 10 liters and 20 liters. The octane and cetan indexes are used in mobile laboratory vehicles.
Mr. Nguon Somlyvong claimed that for depots that sell oil that does not meet the measurement standards, the inspection officials have asked the station owners and depots to make a contract to adjust the vending machine according to the correct prediction through the competent authorities. .
Mr. Somlyvong also called on all vehicle users to consider in choosing a gas station / depot. That is, choose a reliable company to use new equipment that sells regular gasoline or soup and diesel with good quality and all liters.
