(Mondulkiri): Husband and wife committed suicide bombing on the afternoon of August 21, 2018 in Pu Tong village, Chong Plas commune, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province, leaving 4 orphans helpless and Shelter.
On the morning of August 22, 2018, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, assigned the Provincial Working Group to bring some of his own budget, along with some food and equipment of government officials to support the families of the bodies and children. 4 orphans, 3 males and 1 female, to manage their livelihood.
A 50-year-old woman named Ma Chanthou, the grandmother of the four orphans, expressed her gratitude to the provincial governor and his team for all the valuable support provided to her family during her ordeal. Now.
It should be noted that on the afternoon of August 21, 2018, yesterday, there was a case that surprised the neighbors and the police by finding a couple lying dead in their house due to the suicide bombing. In Pu Tong village, Chong Plas commune, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province.
Major General Lor Sokha, Mondulkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, said that the story of the suicide has not yet been confirmed, but is waiting for the commissioner's professional officers to cooperate with local officials on this case. The provincial commissioner said that the story of the suicide bombing of the couple has not been confirmed by any competent authorities and the identities of the two victims are not yet known.
Chong Plas commune police chief confirmed that the above case is indeed a suicide. After the inspection, the police and local police handed over the bodies of the couple to their relatives for a ceremony at Wat Prey Meas.
According to the locals, the couple often quarreled and did not save the day. And the husband and wife above, the husband has many wives and wives, which is the element that makes the wife jealous of the husband and makes the wife always create conflicts.
Residents who knew the couple's story said that the husband had been rescued three times by the locals: the first time he drank acid, the second time he took rat poison, the third time he could not hang himself. Died because the locals rescued in time. The third time, the man committed suicide, as the husband tied a bomb to his wife, and no villager dared to come to the rescue.
The sound of the bomb exploded like lightning, startling the neighbors, but not the lightning. The villagers there are so sympathetic to the four children in their care that, to this day, they do not know what they expect to live on.
