On the one-year anniversary of the workers' visit tomorrow, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to visit nearly 20,000 workers in Kandal province
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, August 23, 2018, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will continue to meet with 17 workers. 503 people from 12 factories in Kandal province. The meeting will take place in Prek Treng 2 village, Samrong Thom commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province.
Tomorrow's meeting is to celebrate the one-year anniversary of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to workers. During this year, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with workers 54 times and a total of more than 750,000 workers met directly with Samdech Techo.
According to Minister Ith Sam Heng, there are currently 464 factories, enterprises and establishments in Kandal province with 155,138 workers with a total wage of $ 372 million. There are 170 garment and footwear factories with 137,664 workers, earning more than $ 330 million a year. The minister also said that in June, two new factories opened, employing 3,341 people.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen started to open a forum to talk with workers from factories, enterprises and establishments since Sunday, August 2017. This is the 54th meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and workers tomorrow. The 54 meetings were attended by a total of 751,540 workers.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the visit to meet with the workers in order to understand the hardships of workers and solve their challenges. In particular, to promote better industrial policy 2015-2025.
