The statement of the Deputy Foreign Minister of the United Kingdom was made during a meeting with Senior Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on the evening of August 22, 2018.
The United Kingdom is a major recipient of Cambodian goods in Europe, especially clothing and footwear. The removal of tariffs on Cambodian goods from European countries is a hot topic in Cambodia in response to the political situation. The leaders of the former opposition party, the former National Rescue Party, have always hoped that the preferential treatment would be a pressure for the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Contrary to the wishes of former opposition leaders, Britain, another new country in Europe, has announced tariff preferences for Cambodian goods.
Foreign Ministry spokesman Keth Sophan confirmed to reporters after the aid that "Britain is committed to continuing to provide trade concessions even after leaving the European Union."
In response to the continuation of tariff preferences for Cambodian goods, Senior Minister Prak Sokhon also thanked the United Kingdom.
Please note that the trade volume between Cambodia and the United Kingdom has increased steadily. A report by the Ministry of Commerce has shown that the trade volume between Cambodia and the United Kingdom increased from more than $ 800 million in 2015 to more than $ 900 million in 2016 and to more than $ 1.02 billion, equivalent to more than $ 1 billion. In 2017.
Cambodian goods exported to the UK include clothing, footwear, as well as some processed agricultural products such as rice and pepper.
(Phnom Penh): The United Kingdom, through the Deputy Minister for Foreign Affairs for Asia and the Pacific, Mark Field, has announced his support for the establishment of the "Supreme Advisory Council" by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen. He considered the establishment of the "Supreme Advisory Council" as a spirit of reconciliation in Cambodia.
The Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of the United Kingdom emphasized this during a meeting with Senior Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on the evening of August 22, 2018.
Cambodian Foreign Ministry spokesman Ket Sophan told reporters after the meeting that during the meeting, McPhil said Cambodia had a bitter history from the Vietnam War, the transition to the Pol Pot regime and other civil wars. With this bitterness, Britain has always announced its support for Cambodia in all it can do so that Cambodia has a bright future.
Speaking on the history of Cambodia's division in the past, the Deputy Foreign Minister of the United Kingdom also expressed support for the establishment of the Supreme Advisory Council of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. This is according to Mr. Ket Sophan.
Mr. Ket Sophan quoted the content of the meeting as follows: "He (Mr. McFill) also supported the spirit of national reconciliation established by Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Supreme Advisory Council, which includes all "All parties to exchange views, and he hopes that this process is a positive process and the spirit of national unity will continue."
This "Supreme Advisory Council" will be completed in accordance with the mandate of the Royal Government of the sixth legislature.
