It should be noted that on the morning of August 22, 2018, the Supreme Court continued to hear the second bail application of Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the National Rescue Party.
According to the merits, this hearing was held because Mr. Kem Sokha's lawyer did not agree with the decision of the Supreme Court on March 9, 2018, upholding the judgment of the Court of Appeal and requiring Mr. Kem Sokha to continue his detention. Sokha remains in prison for questioning and to prevent new crimes from occurring.
The decision of the Supreme Court is also based on the fact that Kem Sokha's case is a criminal offense that needs to be detained for a thorough investigation.
In connection with this request, the presiding judge, Mr. Khim Ponn, announced in the original quote, citing: "Mr. Kem Sokha committed a crime of peace with foreigners from 1993 to 2017. "This is a crime, so the investigation must be thorough."
It should be reminded that Mr. Kem Sokha was arrested from the house in the middle of the night in early September 2017 on charges of "treason" and sent to the prison in Trapeang Phlong prison in Tbong Khmum province. Kem Sokha was charged with conspiracy with a foreigner under Article 443 of the Penal Code.
According to the Cambodian Penal Code, peace with a foreigner is an act of collusion with a foreign state or foreign agency to create hostility or aggression against the Kingdom of Cambodia. This offense is punishable by 15 to 30 years in prison.
