(Koh Kong): The Koh Kong Provincial Administration has issued a notice informing people who are illegally occupying or using land that is not in the list of plots of land in the Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary area to hurry to hand over their title deeds. All lands shall be returned to the Koh Kong Provincial Administration and any encroachment on forest land in this area must be stopped.
Pursuant to the announcement of Koh Kong Provincial Administration on the revocation of land use rights and encroachment on forest land in Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary, which was received by Fresh News on the evening of August 21, 2018 This confirms that the Koh Kong Provincial Administration has set out the following measures:
1. All titles of land tenure in the Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary that are illegal or not in the title deed shall be returned to the Koh Kong Provincial Administration for annulment or demolition in accordance with the procedures.
2. Occupation, encroachment on forest land, clearing, burning of forest land, construction of houses, stalls or sheds to take ownership of land in the Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary area are illegal and must be dealt with according to the legal procedures in force.
Please note that the Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary is a large natural area established by Royal Decree since 1993.
