Mr. Chan Yutha confirmed that "the water started to rise from 1 past midnight. As of 11 a.m., the water had risen to its full height, overflowing from the Jan 7 diversion, at a height of 0.73 meters (similar to the flood last July) and was continuing to rise more slowly. "But we can completely control the flood situation without any problems and there are leaks in three delta dams, but we have already repaired them."
