(China): Robots for a variety of industries and services surprised visitors at the 2018 World Robotics Conference held in Beijing last week.
Chinese and international companies that make more than 160 robots showcased their latest generation of robots at the five-day event.
Skilled robots can be seen everywhere in this convention. These include miniature robots at the industrial robot hall that can skillfully turn on the lights as well as pick fruits precisely.
According to the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, China's robotics sector grew at an average annual rate of nearly 30 percent over the past five years, to $ 7 billion in 2017. The number of industrial robots used in China in 2017 was more than 130,000, up 68.1 percent from 2016.
Other robots can also make coffee and write letters.
