This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with 16 party leaders to participate in the election and consult on national construction and development.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, won the election in the new term this morning, August 21, 2018, met with the leaders of 16 political parties who participated in the election to consult on construction and Develop the nation for the better. This consultation took place at the Royal Government Palace.
The leaders of the 16 political parties participating in the consultation include:
1: Khmer United National Party 2: New Light Party 3: Cambodian Nationality Party 4: Khmer Rising Party 5: Beehive Social Democratic Party 6: Democratic Republican Party 7: Khmer Republican Party 8: Raksmey Khemara Party 9: FUNCINPEC Party 10: Party Khmer Economic Development 11: Cambodian Youth Party 12: Theosophical Party 13: Khmer Will Party 14: Indigenous Democratic Party of Cambodia 15: One Khmer Party 16: Cambodian People's Party
Separately, four other political parties did not participate, including: 1: Our Motherland Party, 2: Local Democratic Party, 3: Coalition Party for Democracy and 4: Khmer Anti-Poverty Party
This consultation meeting between the head of the Royal Government and the leaders of the political parties is considered as a new development in Cambodian politics and a rare event in the history of Cambodia. This development is considered a good thing for Cambodian society as well as the democratic process in Cambodia. In particular, it is a political development that brings benefits for the country and the people of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that this consultation meeting is a demonstration of true national unity along the path of democracy in Cambodia and leading to the establishment of the Supreme Advisory Council between the Royal Government and political parties.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that the establishment of this consultation to listen to the opinions of leaders of political parties that do not win the election as an element in leading and developing the Cambodian nation to grow even more.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the consultation was also to provide an opportunity for political parties that contested the election and did not win seats to participate in improving policies and provide good ideas for the Royal Government to lead. And national development.
