(Phnom Penh): Boeung Kak Lake Community Land Activist Tep Vanny, who was imprisoned by a court in 2016, was pardoned by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni on August 20, 2018. This is at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. This is according to the Royal Decree that Fresh News received a little earlier on the night of August 20, 2018.
In a royal decree, in addition to pardoning, Tep Vanny also ordered the pardon of three other Boeung Kak Lake community land activists, including Heng Mom, Bo Chhorvy and Kong Chantha.
(Phnom Penh): Rainfall in Phnom Sruoch and Oral districts of Kampong Speu province, about 200 mm, flows into small streams, streams into Stung Prek Tnaot and then continues to flow below in Phnom Penh and Kandal province before flowing into the Bassac River. This was confirmed by Mr. Chan Yutha, spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, told Fresh News on the night of August 20, 2018.
The spokesman confirmed that the flood of Stung Prek Tnaot will arrive in Phnom Penh at around 2 am this morning, but the Ministry has been intervening.
Mr. Chan Yutha stated, "But before flowing into the Bassac River, floods often pose a threat to the Stung Prek Tnaot delta dam in Phnom Penh as well as in Kandal province." In the face of this problem, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, is ready to deal with this flood situation.
According to the spokesman, since August 19, more than 20 heavy machinery, along with technical officers, as well as other equipment such as shells, soil, have been sent to the site to be deployed at the dam. Delta to prepare for intervention.
Mr. Chan Yutha added briefly, "We have been ready here since yesterday, we are not so worried because we have prepared enough machinery, technical staff and other means. For one intervention, our dam body just received a major overhaul last month.
