(Pursat): The first pile of wood, about 20 cubic meters, which was found at the south balcony of National Road 55, about 300 meters in Stung Thmey village, Bramoy commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province, was destroyed by the Armed Forces. To crack down.
The crackdown took place after relatives and friends of journalists reported and published on August 14-15, 2018.
In fact, on August 19, 2018, the joint police force led by Colonel O Sophara, Colonel Buk Bun Chhoeun, Veal Veng District Gendarmerie, cooperated with many environmental officials to crack down on illegal timber traders. A total of 280 pieces of sokrom, kokki and koko wood, which the traders hid at the above location, are planned to be shipped to Phnom Penh for sale.
The timber was handed over to environmental officials to be stored at the Phnom Samkos Wildlife Protection Office to build a case for procedural action.
