A speeding container truck hits the railing of the Weiko Bridge and falls into the river, a fisherman and a hairless passenger.
(Svay Rieng): A container truck swerved, hit the railing of the bridge and fell into the Waiko River, but fortunately did not cause any harm to passengers.
Although not dangerous, it did endanger the lives of travelers and anglers alike. This case happened at 4:25 on August 20, 2018 on National Road No. 1 at the end of the East Highway Bridge in Bak Ronas Village, Sangkat Sangkor, Svay Rieng City, Svay Rieng Province. The accident also caused a motorcycle to fall into the river.
According to a 15-year-old boy who owns a motorbike, Samantha Rachana, who was fishing near the scene, said that before the incident, he and a friend were fishing under the highway bridge, while the motorbike was parked on the side of the road. A container truck was speeding from east to west.
Arriving at the commune where the incident took place, he swerved to the left and hit the railing of the bridge more than 20 meters below the ground and continued to hit a motorbike that was left standing and dragged into the Waiko River.
