Ministry of Economy and Finance Conducts Orientation Training for 372 New Civil Servants from 25 Capital-Provincial Departments of Economy and Finance and Related Units at Local Level
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on August 20, 2018 organized an orientation training course for 372 new civil servants from the 25 Capital-Provincial Departments of Economy and Finance and relevant organizations under the supervision of The basis for participating in the implementation of financial management reform in the third phase to achieve effective and effective.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Mr. Pich Sambath, Under Secretary of State, on behalf of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and in collaboration with the Institute of Economics and Finance and the General Secretariat of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Target trainees who are new civil servants.
The event was held to enable the target trainees, who are new civil servants, to understand and expand the basic knowledge related to economic and financial management, including:
* Public financial management reform * Structure and functioning of the Ministry of Economy and Finance * Relations between public financial management reform and public service * Public administration affairs and key aspects of the Law on the General Statute of Officials The Civil Service of the Kingdom of Cambodia as a basis for the effective performance of the duties and responsibilities of those officials.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Pich Sambath emphasized that the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia has always given priority to building and developing human resources to support socio-economic development. .
He added that it has contributed to Cambodia achieving a high economic growth rate of about 7% in the past three terms and has contributed to help Cambodia become a low-middle-income country and is striving to become. High middle income country by 2030 and high income country by 2050.
Mr. Pich Sambath also emphasized that orientation training is very important for new officers and stakeholders in both the public and private sectors in strengthening and expanding knowledge and equipping the work spirit and as a bridge for further professional development. Better to promote productivity and sustainable efficiency in each unit.
At the same time, the Undersecretary of State stressed that the Ministry of Economy and Finance has always paid attention to building and developing skills for public financial management for the leadership and civil servants of all ministries and institutions.
In response to the need to implement public financial management reform in the first and second phases, the Ministry of Economy and Finance officially launched in 2007 the first strategic capacity building and development plan prepared by Institute of Economics and Finance with the assistance of the Technical Advisor of the World Bank.
This strategic plan has been actively and lively implemented and has achieved proud results that have contributed to the successful implementation of public financial management reforms to build the "credibility of the budget" at the stage. The first in 2008 and "Financial Accountability" in the second phase in 2015.
The Undersecretary of State also stressed that these achievements are a solid foundation for the continued implementation of the third phase of public financial management reform, which began in March 2016 with the goal of "increasing budget integration. And priority policies ”in socio-economic development.
In addition, the above achievements also contribute to help Cambodia get out of chronic cash debt and have a cash surplus to increase public investment spending in key sectors such as education and health, and even to gradually increase the salaries of civil servants. Armed forces of all kinds and more retirees.
(Phnom Penh): 2018 is the last year of Hang Chuon Naron as Minister of Education, Youth and Sports in the fifth mandate of the Royal Government of Cambodia. As the Minister of Education since 2014, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron has received much praise and admiration from the people for the work of reforming the education system in Cambodia, especially the restriction of high school exams or so called.
With the introduction of Hang Chuon Naron's slogan "You know, you pass", the Baccalaureate exam is extremely strict, not allowing all candidates to bring copies of documents and calculators into the examination room. . In addition, there will be severe fines to the point of suspension, suspension or other penalties if the candidate violates the rules of the exam, such as having to take the exam instead.
Education reform, especially the five-year Baccalaureate exam, has changed the attitude of Baccalaureate candidates by turning their attention to study, increase their knowledge, and prepare for the exam. Breaking the subject or stealing copies of documents during the exam like never before.
In fact, in the 2018 Baccalaureate event, which took place on the morning of August 20, 2018, at the examination center in Preah Sisowath High School, the candidates did not find a single copy of the documents. Hang Chuon Naron once claimed that he slept only three hours to reform the education system.
During the final session of the fifth mandate at Preah Sisowath High School this morning, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron considered the education reform to be more successful than expected. The success of this reform has not only enabled Cambodia to refine its knowledge resources, but also honored its teachers.
"After cooperation, the results from year to year have exceeded expectations," he said. "So I do not expect this reform to be so successful. Not only can it change attitudes and create a supportive movement, even more honorable."
Minister Hang Chuon Naron considered the success of the reform of the Baccalaureate due to the clear policy of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on education, especially with the cooperation of the Anti-Crime Unit. Corruption and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron's reforms also made the students and parents very satisfied, because these reforms have all awakened the students to learn.
However, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron has not yet revealed the shortcomings or remnants of his reforms, waiting for the formation of a new government and waiting for a new education policy launched by Samdech. Techo Hun Sen first.
The Minister further stated that after Samdech Techo Hun Sen issued an education policy for the new mandate, and if he continues to gain the confidence of the Royal Government to continue as Minister of Education, he will look at the points. Continue to improve the education sector. Many illegal fishing gears were destroyed after the police cracked down in Kandieng district
