(Kampong Thom): Sandan District Authority, in collaboration with Kampong Thom Provincial Health Department and Adra Organization, on August 20, 2018, celebrated World Breastfeeding Week in Sandan Village, Commune, Sandan District to disseminate to the people. Understand the importance of breastfeeding under the theme "Breastfeeding is a solid foundation of life."
The event was held in the presence of Ms. Sim Sidaroth, Deputy District Governor, with the support of Adra Cambodia Hug Project, with the participation of the Armed Forces, village authorities, communes, residents and more than 300 students.
Mr. Ken Chamroeun, Vice President of Adra Hug Project in Sandan District, said that the organization of the World Breastfeeding Week aims to raise awareness among mothers, including:
First, the mother must start breastfeeding immediately during the first hour after delivery, which will provide the first useful milk. Second: Give only breast milk to the baby. During the first six months of their life: Third, continue to breastfeed until the child is at least 2 years old and provide appropriate supplementation.
Ms. Sim Sidarot stated that according to the 2014 Demographic and Health Survey report showing the results in Cambodia, the practice of complete breastfeeding is the only way to breastfeed. Decreased from 73.5% in 2010 to 64.6% in 2014.
Breastfeeding started immediately in the first hour after delivery and continued breastfeeding until the age of 12 months was found to decrease from 65.3% to 62.6% and decreased. Down from 83% to 80%. In addition, the provision of pre-determined age supplements increased significantly in both urban and rural areas between 2010 and 2014.
At the same time, she advised all mothers to pay attention to breastfeeding to help children get the best start in life and can help reduce the disease. Special! For low price and good quality phones, do not forget "Siv Eng Shop" with all models of phones
