(Phnom Penh): In response to the suggestion that the Ministry of Education is restricting only the high school exam, or Bakdup, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, claimed that the reform of the education system in Cambodia. Do it from kindergarten to high school, not just during the Baccalaureate exam.
According to Hang Chuon Naron, the Ministry of Education has reviewed the curriculum at all levels from grade 1 to grade 12, and the ministry has also reviewed textbooks, revised teaching methods, and the reform is relevant. And teacher training. In addition, there is training in pedagogical schools, refresher training, teacher training, improving school management, which is a priority for the past year as well as for the next 5 years.
In addition to the curriculum review, the Ministry of Education also conducts school inspections, focusing on four main components: Leadership and management of principals, II. Learning and teaching, III. Improving student learning outcomes; and Involvement of parents and the community in school management.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron also said that the third major point of the Ministry of Education's reform is to assess students 'learning values, which focus on students' knowledge of Khmer literature and mathematics as well as science. Review the curriculum to make Cambodia a curriculum similar to other countries in the region. To implement this work, the Ministry has also decided to adopt the same curriculum as Singapore.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron added that the Ministry wants to teach students according to Singaporean standards, not only for students to memorize, but also for students to think critically, solve problems, work in a team and for students to contribute to knowledge. Like skills, and then higher reform.
"Thus, we see that although we have a comprehensive reform, but the public does not know that reform, he only knows the exam."
