(China): An official report on the state of China's cyber security shows that mobile Internet networks face higher security risks.
China Cyber Security Report 2017 summarizes the cyber security situation in China in 2017. The report was released on Wednesday at the 2018 National Cyber Emergency Center Conference.
Experts say the security risks of virtual and non-virtual operating systems have greatly affected the main interests of the Chinese people.
"The number of cyber security vulnerabilities in the Internet-enabled smart devices in 2017 more than doubled in 2016," said Yan Hanping, director of operations at the National Cyber Emergency Center. And this number will continue to increase in 2018. "It shows that new devices connected to the Internet are very risky."
Many people's personal data, including home address, identity and bank accounts, are stored on mobile phones where the risk of infection is highest.
"Between January and July, the number of newly formed foreign-invested companies increased by 99.1 percent year on year," said Zhu Ping, deputy director of the Foreign Investment Administration Department of the Ministry of Commerce. The same as last year, there were 35,239 companies. "Foreign direct investment was actually nearly 72 billion US dollars, up 2.3 percent from the same period last year."
Investment in the modern industry rose 7.5 percent, accounting for 21.5 percent of total foreign direct investment. Foreign direct investment in modern manufacturing increased by 31 percent.
Zhou Ping, deputy director of the Foreign Investment Administration Department of the Ministry of Commerce, said: "In the first seven months of this year, the modern manufacturing sector continued to grow rapidly with more efficient industrial structure. "Foreign direct investment in China's manufacturing sector was about 22 billion US dollars, up 8.8 percent from the same period last year."
China's 11 pilot free trade zones saw a 30 percent increase in foreign direct investment, with $ 9.5 billion in investment, and 5,186 newly formed foreign-invested companies.
Investment from countries participating in China's One Belt One Road project has increased by nearly 30 percent, while other major countries investing in China have also seen good growth. According to data from the Chinese Ministry of Commerce.
China has put in place a number of measures to open up China's market since the beginning of 2018, the 40th anniversary of the implementation of China's market opening policy reform.
