This morning, the high school diploma exam (Bakdup) has started, 16 important prohibitions that candidates should not take the exam
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 20, 2018, the high school diploma exam will start at 7 am today until August 21. Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, opened the message at Preah Sisowath High School in Phnom Penh.
This is the fifth time that the Ministry of Education has reformed the high school exam, with observers participating in all activities of the candidates. The reform of the last four exams has been a great success.
There are 25 examination centers in Phnom Penh, with 913 examination rooms with 22,778 candidates.
During the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination Session on August 20-21, 2018, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has deployed law enforcement forces in all 25 examination centers and 10 revision centers in Phnom Penh to better protect security and order for more than 20,000 candidates. People.
For the convenience of candidates who are preparing for the Baccalaureate exam, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has issued 16 key prohibitions for candidates to avoid. This August 20-21.
The 16 prohibitions include:
1: Do not arrive at the examination center after the second bell.
2: Do not wear armed forces uniforms into the examination center.
3: Do not bring books and copies of all documents into the examination center.
4: Do not bring explosive weapons, mobile phones, electronic devices of all kinds, notebooks, documents, calculators, watches with calculators, bags, handbags, bags, other packages and white water.
5: Do not enter the exam room before the supervisor calls the name.
6. Do not use inappropriate words or behavior in the examination center or cause conflicts in the examination center or in the examination room by threatening other candidates.
7. Do not refuse to retaliate or provoke verbally or physically in response to the inspection of the competent person or the person in charge of the examination, search, search for documents and other materials that are prohibited from being taken into the examination center.
8: Do not answer the test on any worksheet without the signature of the guardian.
9: Do not copy the subject in other papers and do not throw the subject out of the exam room.
10: Do not stand up, turn left - right, crawl forward, turn back or walk out of the seat without permission from the caretaker. Do not write assignments and read aloud to your neighbors or drag other people's worksheets in front of or under your own worksheets.
11. Do not exchange worksheets or draft papers or verify answers or copy each other and do not place worksheets far in front of you, causing others to see or drag.
12: Do not make a mark on the worksheet to make its citation known, such as writing different letters from all the letters in the work to make different signs or irregular lines or erase with white water or write across the line.
13. Do not hide or tear your worksheet and do not tear or hide other people's worksheets.
14: Do not destroy or damage the equipment in the exam room, such as removing doors, windows, opening walls, boards, broken tables, chairs or blackboards.
15: Never let others take the exam instead or fill in their worksheets.
16. Do not use words and behaviors that disrupt the order of the exam or affect the reputation of the speaker.
Please also note that for candidates who do not comply with the prohibitions of these 16 points, candidates are set to fall automatically.
