This morning, the Minister of Education cut the final exam of the 5th mandate at Preah Sisowath High School (Phnom Penh): This morning, Monday, August 20, 2018, this is the final exam for high school students called Bakdup. Finally, for Mr. Hang Chuon Naron as Minister of Education, Youth and Sports in the fifth mandate of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron was entrusted by the Royal Government of Cambodia to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to take charge of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in 2014, which is also the first year of the Baccalaureate exam. 2014 was the first year of the reform of the bankruptcy exam under the direction of Hang Chuon Naron "You know is successful", which caused many students to fail that year less than 50 percent. Forcing the Ministry to organize the second exam.
Coming to save the education sector in Cambodia, which was seen as very bad, especially the bankruptcy exam, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron once stated that he spent only 3 hours a night sleeping.
Under the beginning of the reform, based on a clear vision to extract a real knowledge resource, all students, especially those who are preparing for the Baccalaureate exam, have awakened to their studies to increase their ability to prepare for the exam by Do not wait to copy or spy on documents or buy a leaked version of the course or find a way to bribe the teacher to revise the course.
The reform of this exam has made both students and parents show great satisfaction with this reform because the new important mechanism reminds their grandchildren to turn to study hard not to spend time walking. Play more in the competition year.
Hang Chuon Naron's reforms also reduced the number of A-level students as he did before he came to power. In 2014, the year of the first reform exam, there were only 11 A-level students. But the number also increased after the students woke up. In 2015, there were 108 A-level students, in 2016, there were 405 A-level students and in 2017, there were 424 A-level students.
The 2018 Bankruptcy Exam is the last year of the 5th term of the Royal Government and also the last year of the rule of Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, while the new term of the Royal Government will be established on September 6. It is not yet known whether the Royal Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen will continue to give confidence to Mr. Hang Chuon Naron to continue as Minister of Education, Youth and Sports or not?
(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert, Mr. Rath Sandab, expressed his interest in some opinions that are often raised in a political sense, especially recently, claiming that the 6th National Assembly election is a fake election. Or anyway.
At this point, Mr. Rath Sandab also said that the election of the sixth mandate is not different from the previous mandate because there are observers from all political parties, especially national and international observers from Countries participated as witnesses at all polling stations across the country.
In other words, if we talk about the opinion that accuses this election of being a fake or not, then the opinion that is raised is just an opinion that can only be said out loud as an excuse. In order to oppose or not recognize the election results, not unlike the previous mandate.
As for the allegations in this election, whether they are fake or not, as an excuse, at this point, Mr. Rath Sandab noted:
First, in terms of elections, this mandate is not different from the previous mandate. Because those who raised this opinion have already clearly lost in this election, with their group calling for people not to go to the polls. In contrast, 83.2% of the population went to the polls, the highest turnout in the previous election.
Finally, Mr. Rath Sandab also confirmed that the election system is not different from the previous mandate. This means that the election is based on a multi-party liberal democracy, but in terms of the people's choice, it is one-party. In other words, the people decided to vote for the Cambodian People's Party, especially for Samdech Te Hun Sen to lead the country one hundred percent, equal to 125 seats in the National Assembly.
As for the reason why the people turned to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen more than the previous mandate, because the people have seen the actions of the opposition always want to push the country into a color revolution, especially people are afraid the country will fall into War like the 1970s again.
Therefore, in terms of multi-party liberal democratic elections and the people deciding to choose a one-party leader, this is not a new thing or a strange thing in the political history of our Cambodian society. During the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era, under the royal leadership of His Majesty the King-Father, our highest deity, the people voted in the same way.
