Police in Kampot province have arrested a taxi driver who threatened him with a knife.
Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Mao Chanthurith told Fresh News that the suspect was arrested by his police force at 11 am on August 19, 2018 in Andong Khmer commune, Kampot city. Kampot.
According to the General Commissioner, the taxi driver threatened to kill people in this public place since the beginning of July 2018, but only the video recorded from the security camera in the other passenger car was shared when Recently. He said that after seeing the video, he ordered the specialized police force to launch a search immediately until he was arrested today.
Major General Mao Chanthurith confirmed the story that the suspect, who was the taxi driver, did not pull out a knife to threaten the traffic police who were facilitating traffic in front of Samaki Market, saying that the suspect had a dispute with another taxi driver who was driving. The car in the back then pulled out a knife and threatened, but then the traffic police and other residents nearby facilitated their return.
The Kampot provincial commissioner also said that after the arrest, the specialized police force confiscated the knife that the suspect threatened in the car. After the arrest, the suspect was taken for questioning before building a case to proceed with the procedure.
