The above is a traditional activity that Cambodians often celebrate, but if we look at the meaning and legal aspects, what are the conditions?
There are many situations that lead to the failure of the purpose of the pledge, which leads to the dissolution of the pledge, such as the death of the other party, serious misconduct by the other party or by mutual consent. These are all reasons for breaking the promise.
What are the issues related to this pledge, in case the pledge is dissolved, can the parties demand a refund? And which party is responsible for the payment?
On the other hand, if the agreement is dissolved by agreement, the parties can determine their respective responsibilities and the parties must abide by that agreement. For example, the man and the woman agree to dissolve the contract without demanding anything from each other, the man does not demand a gift and the woman does not demand a commitment fee. How can a party claim compensation or damages due to the termination of an agreement?
Prepared by Lawyer Lan Sinit and Mr. Rath Chanthy, Assistant Lawyer and a member of the Working Group on the Preparation and Dissemination of Legal Articles of the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation
Ghana announces full week of mourning after death of former UN Secretary-General Kofi Annan
According to Akufu-Addo, the mourning period will begin tomorrow, with the flag of Kanaaga being flown at half-mast across the country and at all Ghanaian diplomatic missions around the world. The Ghanaian leader said he was "deeply saddened" by the news of Annan's death. At the same time, world leaders also expressed their condolences over the sad news.
Kofi Annan, who had three children and was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 2001 for his work for world peace, has died in Switzerland. Annan served as Secretary-General of the United Nations from early 1997 until the end of 2006, and was the first black man to lead this top international body.
