(Kampong Cham): Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal ordered the Provincial Criminal Police Force, in cooperation with local forces, on August 18, 2018, to crack down on an illegal gambling place in Chamkar Leu District, arresting him. Two suspects on the orders of Kampong Cham Provincial Prosecutor Huot Wutty.
The General Commissioner confirmed that before the crackdown, he received information from the people and ordered the Criminal Police Planning Task Force led by Colonel Thanh Sok Vun, Director of the Office in cooperation with the Svay Teap Administrative Police Station to crack down on gambling sites. Illegal settlement (cockfighting) at a rubber plantation in Taing Krang village, Svay Teap commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province.
According to Major General Em Kosal, as a result, the specialized forces cracked down on two players: First: Leng Bunlong, male, 40 years old, and second: Soy Khouch, male, 36 years old, residing in Taing Krang village. Svay Teap commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province. The confiscated exhibits include: 2 chickens, 1 chicken scale, 1 chicken mirror, 3 motorcycles.
Currently, the suspect and the above exhibits were brought to the Kampong Cham Provincial Police under the order of Mr. Huot Wutty, Prosecutor of the Kampong Cham Provincial Court, for questioning and to file a case according to the procedure.
