BEIJING (Reuters) - The Chinese government will continue its cooperation and relations with Iran despite US President Donald Trump's warning to impose sanctions on companies or countries that continue to trade with Tehran. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Saturday, August 18, 2018.
China has close trade ties with Iran, especially in the energy sector. But Donald Trump, after announcing the withdrawal of the United States from the Iran nuclear deal, announced that he would impose sanctions on companies and countries that continue to trade with Iran, while the other signatories are China, Russia, Britain, France and Germany. With the withdrawal of Washington.
