(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, and Ms. Hang Lina, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the National Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning, jointly explained in detail the benefits of compiling statistics to the public.
A detailed explanation of the importance of compiling this statistic was made on August 17, 2018 with the participation of Ms. Neav Chanthana, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and other relevant officials.
Ms. Chea Serey stated that the main purpose of organizing this workshop was to disseminate the importance of statistics, as you can see, that Cambodia is moving fast, so there are a lot of external and internal risks. More than ever. If we have enough data and information to be able to analyze it in a timely manner, it will be possible to reduce these risks.
She added that today's publication between the National Bank of Cambodia and the National Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning is to disseminate to all relevant institutions, including businesses and the education sector, so that they understand the importance and contribute to the provision of data. .
Ms. Chea Serey added that compiling statistics is important because when doing something, it is necessary to have data to analyze, if there is no data, it is clear that it is not possible to analyze or do something clearly.
Ms. Hang Lina said that the need for statistics is important, but there are still some difficulties that have arisen, such as budget problems, however, the Institute continues to work hard to strengthen the compilation. This statistic is better because without statistics, doing something will be more difficult.
Ms. Neav Chanthana also said that this is not the first time that the Institute and the National Bank have jointly organized a workshop on the importance of compiling statistics, so far the National Bank has worked together.
She added that the importance of compiling these statistics is to widely disseminate the benefits of compiling and using economic statistical data in the formulation of macroeconomic policies, development plans and strategies, and research related to the economy and the economy. Finance.
