Asia Europe University awarded certificates of appreciation to 317 undergraduate students
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of August 17, 2018, Asia Europe University (AEU) organized a certificate awarding ceremony for 317 graduates of the Faculty of Business and Tourism Management and the Faculty of Social Sciences and Economics, 167 females.
The award ceremony was attended by Dr. Chea Sopheap, Rector of AEU, and the winners were: Management, Marketing, Accounting, Hotel and Tourism Management and Banking and Finance. Graduated and defended the research dissertation in the 2016-2017 academic year.
Saing Chanthou, Associate Dean of the Faculty of Business and Tourism Management, said that every year, graduating from the University requires students to do internships at companies and organizations, both public and private, to link theory to practice through Research on the operational processes of companies and organizations related to students' skills.
He added that the requirement for this internship is for the purpose of collecting and compiling documents, as well as reviewing the actual work of the company or unit, to write and compile for the most strict review and evaluation committee and make recommendations on the dissertation. From the committee to review and evaluate the dissertation to be more effective.
He also expressed his appreciation for the successful results of the efforts of students in all disciplines. Mr. Saing Chanthou stated that from generation to generation, students have a broader understanding of research work, which makes every student gain the ability, knowledge, skills to respond to the job market.
Dr. Chea Sopheap stated that AEU University has clearly defined its vision, mission and objectives, especially the establishment of mechanisms as well as policies to promote research to students at all levels. Facilitate staff, professors and students in research.
He also encouraged all 17th generation thesis students to continue to participate in the research process more actively and effectively for the purpose of strengthening their skills in order to develop themselves and society.
