(Phnom Penh): On August 17, 2018, 7 Cambodian children with congenital heart disease received free surgery through a charity project to treat heart disease in Cambodia under the "Bumrong Rath" hospital and Bumrungrad International Hospital, Thailand, together with the Thai Embassy in Cambodia.
In fact, today, the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA), Calmette Hospital and Thai AirAsia held a press conference on the Charity Project for Cardiology in Cambodia, a project designed to use specialized skills and Bumrungrad Hospital's own resources to provide free congenital heart surgery to children in neighboring countries.
The representative of the Bumrungrad Hospital Foundation said that this is why the Bumrungrad Hospital Foundation was established to ensure that children are treated in a timely manner, reducing complications and mortality, while improving children's health. The Bumrungrad Hospital Foundation and Bumrungrad Hospital have been running a series of projects to help children since 2003.
To date, 775 children with congenital heart disease in Thailand have undergone heart surgery through this program. During the past five years, after the project was well established in Thailand, aid has been extended to neighboring countries such as Myanmar and Vietnam. And this year, on the occasion of the 38th anniversary of the establishment of Bumrungrad Hospital, we are committed to continuing to provide our solutions to improve public health.
To show the warm relationship between Thailand and Cambodia through the Public Health Program, we are pleased to offer heart surgery to seven Cambodian children with congenital heart disease for surgery at Bumrungrad Hospital in Thailand. . The surgery will be provided free of charge, which can alleviate the difficult situation of hospitals in Cambodia. This is the additional emphasis of Ms. Napas Paorohitaya.
This heart-healing charity project is a clear demonstration of the "heart to heart", confirming Thailand's commitment to Cambodia. "We are honored to be a part of this great project and to support children in need of heart surgery," said Thai AirAsia.
In the future, AirAsia will assist selected patients and their families with free air travel to Thailand for heart surgery. This is a meaningful role for us and we are very proud to contribute to helping those in need.
Professor Chheang Ra, Director General of Calmette Hospital, stated, "As a Cambodian, I would like to express my deepest gratitude to all the donors and partners of the Foundation."
"I would also like to join the celebration with this child with congenital heart disease who received free surgery at Bumrungrad International Hospital in Thailand, which is a great help for the people," he said. Cambodians. ”
The Director General of Calmette Hospital claims that this is the beginning of the contribution of Cambodian children to the Phnom Penh Heart Center, which has helped many Cambodian children with surgery and treatment, and the project still needs long-term partners for the future. " C Investment does not offer 100% scholarships for Cambodian women entrepreneurs who want to develop their business.
