(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hun Manet, Chairman of the Board of the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA) on August 17, 2018, claimed that many years ago, Cambodia has become a sad land. Full of problems and crises to become a rich land with prosperity and potential in all fields.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. HUN Manet's participation in the presentation and press conference on "Charity Project for Cardiology in Cambodia" under the auspices of Bumrungrad Hospital and Bumrungrad International Hospital in collaboration with the Thai Embassy. Cambodia Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA), Kalmet Hospital and AirAsia.
Speaking on the occasion, Dr. Hun Manet stated, "Over the years, Cambodia has transformed from a land of misery, full of problems and crises into a land of prosperity and prosperity. "Potential in all areas under the influence of peace, which has enabled the Royal Government to achieve many great achievements."
Mr. Hun Manet stated that a large part of the health sector is through achieving the goal of reducing the mortality rate, which is the actual result, the mortality rate of children from 124 per 1,000 live births in 2000 to 45. In 2010, the maternal mortality rate dropped from 450 per 1 million births in 2000 to 206 in 2010 and has been steadily declining.
He added that in 2016, the number of people receiving health services (examination and treatment) at the state's public health facilities was more than 10 million, and the mortality rate was low or 0.85%, which shows From the increase in the use of state health services and the improvement from year to year. In addition, the prevalence of all other forms of infection has been significantly reduced.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Manet emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia has also set out a number of policies to increase consideration and attention to the well-being of people across the country and to encourage the participation of the private sector. Associations through various humanitarian programs and activities to provide a wider range of health care services and free medical check-ups for poor people across the country.
Mr. HUN Manet also mentioned that the charity project to treat heart disease in Cambodia through the Foundation of Bumrungrad Hospital and Bumrungrad International Hospital is a big contribution, even though we are in different countries, but our common goal Is to help people in need.
It is this similarity that has drawn us both (Cambodia-Thailand) and from all sides: 1: Bumrong Rath Hospital Foundation and Bumrong Rath International Hospital, 2: Samdech Techo Cambodian Youth Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA), 3: Calmette Volunteer Hospital and all stakeholders, as well as our team of doctors, work together to help humanity and our society.
At the same time, I hope that the Bumrungrad Hospital Foundation and Bumrungrad International Hospital will continue to help more Cambodians in the future. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Hun Manet. Prosecutors end interrogation of Lexus 570 owner with state license plate
