Japanese investors are rushing into the Cambodian stock market
(Phnom Penh): Japanese investors have been entering the stock market the most among all foreign investors. This is according to the press release of the momentum of foreign investment in stocks in the first half of 2018, which Fresh News received on August 17, 2018.
"From January to June 2018, the trading volume of foreign investors in the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) was approximately 5.16 billion Riels, or 67.38% of the total trading volume," the statement said. Although the number of trading accounts of foreign investors is less than the number of trading accounts of Cambodian investors.
According to the press release, the large and active participation of foreign investors in the trading of shares on the CSX shows their positive expectations for the future of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, as well as some of the benefits that they will benefit from. Investments in this stock exchange also include:
1. Cambodia is considered one of the countries with the strongest economic growth in the world, about 7% in the last 10 years. Therefore, investing in the Cambodia Securities Exchange is an opportunity to reap the benefits of this booming economy.
2. Foreign investors can hold shares of listed companies indefinitely and receive tax incentives such as income tax and stamp duty.
