General Department of Taxation Introduces the Implementation of withholding tax to avoid double taxation and prevent income tax evasion
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation has issued guidelines on the implementation of withholding tax within the framework of the agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax.
According to the instruction received by Fresh News on August 17, 2018, to facilitate the implementation of withholding tax within the framework of the agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and prevention. Tax evasion related to income tax must follow the instructions below:
First, Cambodian resident taxpayers shall apply the accounting method in accordance with the International Accounting Standards of Cambodia on all payment of dividends, interest, royalties and technical fees to the resident taxpayer of the other Party of the Agreement. The above income payment is considered to be paid if it is recorded in the accounting book of the Cambodian resident taxpayer who is the withholding agent.
Thirdly, the payment of dividends, interest, royalties and technical fees shall be taxed in accordance with the new Article 26 (a) of the Tax Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia, but not to exceed the rate specified in the DTA as stated. In Instruction No. 4084, dated March 26, 2018, on the rules and procedures for the implementation of the agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax.
The General Department of Taxation hopes that the Cambodian Resident Taxpayer and the Resident Taxpayer of the other State Party, state institutions and organizations under the scope of this Agreement will pay attention to the implementation of the contents of this instruction. Highly effective. Ministry of Industry Organizes the Second Training Workshop on "Efficiency of Clean Production Resources and Environmental Management System" in Industry and Handicraft
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts, in collaboration with the Cambodian Climate Change Alliance of the National Council for Sustainable Development of the Ministry of Environment, organized the second training workshop on "Efficiency of Clean Production Resources and Environmental Management System" in the field of industry and handicrafts.
Today's training workshop has three objectives to provide participants with:
1: Knowledge and experience on efficient use of resources and clean production by making savings, reducing costs and good housing by increasing productivity.
2: Understand the basics of environmental management systems in factories and handicrafts.
3. Increase the capacity of professional officers and stakeholders.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of this important training seminar, Mr. Sat Samy said that under the wise leadership of Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, the Ministry has been implementing action plans to respond to climate change with its overall vision and mission. Such as:
1. Efficient use of resources and clean production will enable factories or handicrafts to benefit from lower production costs, increase productivity, and contribute to minimizing emissions and wastes. Greenhouses into the environment as well.
Taking this great opportunity, Mr. Sat Samy also thanked Mr. Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, who always encouraged and fully supported the implementation of the above project.
