According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, told the media that during the meeting, the British Ambassador and Samdech Techo Hun Sen did not mention the issue of strengthening trade relations and other areas between the two countries. For other issues as well as the election in Cambodia.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth emphasized, "In this meeting, she informed Samdech Techo that during her six-week diplomatic mission in the Kingdom of Cambodia, she was warmly welcomed. Most. And in this ongoing mission in Cambodia, she will do everything to strengthen bilateral relations between Cambodia and the United Kingdom.
In addition to demonstrating her commitment to strengthening diplomatic ties, the new British Ambassador also highlighted a number of key areas and priorities that she will focus on, including Technology issues, demining issues, trade, women's rights and education.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the United Kingdom as well as the British people for their assistance to Cambodia. Especially in the field of education, help train human resources, which is an important factor of Cambodia, and also thank the United Kingdom for helping Cambodia in the field of demining.
Samdech Techo said that Cambodia has a large-scale ASEAN Demining Center to assist countries in the region and also contributes to the work of the United Nations. In this regard, Samdech Techo expects the UK should consider strengthening cooperation with the ASEAN Demining Center located in Cambodia.
Regarding the promotion of women's rights, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia has placed the role of women in the Royal Government from the district level to the army, police as well as other institutions. In addition, the Royal Government has taken care to build schools where women can go and also to build shelters for women.
This rainy season causes a lot of rain and floods everywhere, which is why tiger mosquitoes are a transmitting agent of dengue fever. During this period, dengue fever has continued to increase significantly, especially in densely populated areas, including Phnom Penh, Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum, according to the Ministry of Health. Strong.
"We also intervened, we saw an increase because it is normal to rain, but there is no emergency like in 2012," he said. We only do areas where there is an increase in mosquitoes, we start distributing abattoirs and spraying mosquito repellent. "So because we have this series of actions, we have been able to prevent and control it."
Mr. Ly Sovann called on people to help clean themselves, clean the environment around the house not to put water. He said that where there is water, there must be cover, fish to eat worms, and contact the health center or village volunteers when needed to help solve the problem, as well as measures to prevent dengue fever.
According to the spokesperson, if a child is suspected of having a fever or other symptoms of dengue fever, do not leave him or her at home and send him or her to the nearest health center or hospital. He strictly forbade village injections at any clinic provided by non-doctors accredited by the Ministry of Health.
(Phnom Penh): The Higher Secondary Diploma Examination Session on August 20-21, 2018, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will deploy law enforcement forces in all 25 examination centers and 10 revision centers in Phnom Penh to ensure good security and order. More than 20,000 candidates.
During the meeting on organizing security and order on the day of the bankruptcy exam on August 17, 2018 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall, Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, affirmed that "Phnom Penh Municipal Authority has prepared sufficient police forces to protect security, order and safety. To candidates for the high school diploma exam on August 20 and 21 early next week.
Regarding the exact number of security forces, the Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh did not want to give the number because it is the national social security.
Mr. Nuon Pharath said that on the 20th and 21st, Phnom Penh Capital Hall will deploy traffic police forces on all major roads, especially the access roads to the 25 examination centers in Phnom Penh from 5 am onwards. Because there are more than 20,000 candidates in Phnom Penh.
Chea Cheat, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, said that this is the fifth time that the Ministry of Education has reformed the high school exam, with observers participating in all activities of the candidates. The reform of the last four exams has been a great success.
According to the Undersecretary of State, there are 25 examination centers in Phnom Penh, with 913 examination rooms with 22,778 candidates.
At the same time, he requested all relevant institutions and authorities to continue to cooperate and support to coordinate candidates during this year's high school diploma exam to get better.
However, Mr. Kheang Seng, Deputy Chief of the Anti-Corruption Unit, requested the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority to provide 24-hour security at all examination centers and security at all 10 centers in Phnom Penh until the 29th of this month. August 2018.
As for the observers for the examination centers in Phnom Penh, Mr. Kheang Seng mentioned that the organization placed 1,114 volunteer observers in 25 examination centers. He added that all candidates and stakeholders are guilty of criminal misconduct, and if there is a misdemeanor, the Anti-Corruption Unit will investigate and arrest the perpetrators.
Confidentiality of Exam Subjects The ACU and the Ministry of Education often urge candidates, observers, moderators, supervisors, and other stakeholders to refrain from recording disciplines and to maintain the confidentiality of disciplines that even personal recordings do not allow. Also, if the photographer is caught, he will be punished as well.
