(Phnom Penh): On 16 August 2018, the Co-Investigating Judges issued two separate Closing Orders in the case against O'An, according to the differing record of whether O'An is within the jurisdiction of the Chamber. Is the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) a senior leader or one of the highest authorities? This is according to the announcement of the Khmer Rouge tribunal today.
The National Co-Investigating Judge considered that O'An was not under both jurisdictions of the ECCC and decided to drop the charges against O'An for that reason. In order to do so, the National Co-Investigating Judge considered O'An's involvement and the seriousness of the offense, as well as other factors such as the content of the ECCC Agreement and the law and the intent of the parties. Establish this agreement and law.
The two Co-Investigating Judges have filed a Closing Order in their respective languages and will issue a follow-up translation as soon as possible. However, the Co-Judges will provide a summary of their arguments in two languages to ensure that the public is adequately informed of the results until the full translation is complete.
