(Phnom Penh): The University of Cambodia (UC) has decided to announce 3,050 scholarships for students who lack the ability to afford to continue their higher education at their university. This is according to Mr. Y Ratana, Deputy Rector of the University of Cambodia in charge of Human Resources in a press conference on the afternoon of August 16, 2018.
He said that seeing many students who are short and do not have enough money to pay for education at the best higher education institutions in the country due to high tuition fees and daily expenses, so they want scholarships. To alleviate the burden of their family expenses and enable them to focus, study hard and become Cambodia's outstanding human resources.
Mr. Y Ratana said: "Therefore, in the strategy of recruiting young people to pursue higher education and to celebrate the 15th anniversary, the University of Cambodia has decided to provide a total of 3,050 scholarships for the 2018-2019 academic year. "
