(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Isan, spokesman for the Cambodian People's Party, said that the Cambodian People's Party has no policy to share seats in the National Assembly to the party that did not win the election.
Mr. Sok Isan confirmed this in the press conference on the election results held at the Phukitra Hotel this morning, August 16, 2018.
Mr. Sok Isan stated, "We do not abandon the will of the people and we do not insult the will of the people. The CPP is a party that always respects the will of the people, we can not take the will of the people to other parties that the people did not vote for. "Do not compare the will of the people with economic and social land concessions, because the will of the people is not an economic and social land concession."
