(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, the sixth mandate, led by the Cambodian People's Party, after winning control of all seats in the National Assembly, did not care or fear the threat of tax cuts from some countries.
The spokesman of the Cambodian People's Party, Mr. Sous Yara, said in a press conference on the results of the 6th National Assembly election on the morning of August 16, 2018 that the threat to terminate the preferential tax is just an unfortunate propaganda of Only a few politicians.
According to Mr. Sous Yara, if the preferential tariffs are cut, not only Cambodia, but also the United States or Europe will lose because Americans do not buy cheap goods from Cambodia to use in their country. They.
"The threat of sanctions or tax cuts is something that some Western politicians are campaigning for," said a ruling party spokesman. The simple thing that is easy to hear is that trade is a scale, a trade scale is profitable, profitable "Cheap stuff, so do not panic."
On the other hand, the cut in tariffs is due to the fact that Cambodia has moved from the poverty line to the low-middle-income countries, so whether or not you want tariffs for Cambodia will no longer exist. This is an additional emphasis of Mr. Sous Yara.
Mr. Sous Yara stated, "Cambodia has crossed the poverty line, so entering the middle-low-income country stage means that Cambodia has to go through a period of preferential tariffs, and this is Cambodia's progress. "They use the term preferential tax as just a movement to propagate misfortune."
