Ratanakkiri Governor Inspects Sesan River Flood Situation and Impact in Vern Sai District
(Rattanakiri): The Governor of Rattanakiri Province, Mr. Thong Savun, on August 16, 2018, accompanied by the Deputy Governor and Deputy Director of the Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, inspected the flood situation and the impact of the people. Affected by the flooding of the Sesan River in Vern Sai district.
Speaking on that occasion, the provincial governor instructed the district, village and commune authorities to intervene in a timely manner and pay attention to the temporary living conditions of the people who were evacuated to safety.
The provincial governor distributed donations from the provincial branch of the Cambodian Red Cross to distribute to 50 families evacuated to safety in Team Krom village, Kachon commune, Vern Sai district, including noodles, rubber, tents and some medicine.
According to the provisional report from the district authority, due to the continuous rain situation, the Sesan River flood affected 3 districts, including Vern Sai district, Ta Veng district and Andong Meas district, affecting 1,274 families, evacuating 403 families to safety. . In this situation, the provincial authorities and local authorities have taken great care to evacuate people to safety.
