Sihanoukville Police Launch Large-Scale Drug Operation at Skyline Club, Detain 53 People, 29 Chinese, Indonesian and Korean
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police under the direct command of Major General Chuon Narin launched a large-scale drug crackdown operation at the Skyline Entertainment Club, arresting 53 suspects, including 24 Cambodians. 10 Chinese, 17 Indonesians and 2 Koreans.
Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin told Fresh News that the crackdown took place from 1:45 am to 5:00 am on August 16, 2018, with the coordination of the Prosecutor's Office. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court.
According to the General Commissioner, a large-scale operation to crack down on drug cases in the Skyline bar arrested 53 people, 7 females, 10 Chinese, 17 Indonesians, 2 Koreans, most of them were employees of the Golden Ginseng and Tongfang Mingju casinos, as well as citizens. Twenty-four Cambodians confiscated 26 packs of ketamine and ecstasy, four bottles of drugs to mix with water. After the test, all of them contained drugs.
Police who went to the scene said that during the raid, they were actually using it, and one of the 53 men reported to the police that the drugs were bought in the bar.
