According to a letter from Chbar Morn City Hall, the owner of the motorcycle depot was told to stop arranging motorcycles, sending money on public roads and charging more than the limit in the charge book.
In that, Chbar Morn Municipality would like to inform the owners of 4 locations:
* First: Mr. Nop Sanin, the owner of the motorcycle depot north of Kampong Speu Market * Second: Sao Van, the owner of the motorcycle depot north of Kampong Speu Market * Third: Tho Thea, the owner of the motorcycle depot north of Kampong Speu Market * Ty 4: The name of Chon Srey Nich, the owner of the motorcycle delivery location north of Kampong Speu market.
Chbar Morn City Hall found that in the past, his motorcycle depot had set up motorbikes to collect money on public roads, causing traffic congestion, causing disorder and the beauty of the city, as well as overcharging. In the charge book, it caused a series of criticisms from the public.
Therefore, the Chbar Morn Municipality would like to ask the site owners to stop arranging motorbikes to send money on public roads and to charge for sending motorbikes in excess of the limit in the charge book from the date of this notice. Hok Marady, governor of Chbar Morn, said that if the site owner refused to comply with the notice, the city administration would take legal action.
