(Battambang): As of this morning, August 16, 2018, the water level of Stung Sangke River in Battambang Province has risen to 13.75 meters, which is the water level at the alert level, while the Boeung Chhouk Market area in Battambang City has been The floodwaters gradually flowed through the drains. This was confirmed by Mr. Chan Yutha, spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources.
However, at this time, the authorities, including the military forces of the 5th Zone, are intervening to take the sandbags provided by Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, 5,000 bags to close. The lowest estuary in order to prevent the water from rising and flowing into Battambang city.
As for the water level, the spokesman claimed that at 4 or 5 pm, the water will start to recede because the water flow from the upper part was assigned by the Minister of Water Resources to prevent and drain it. Some main canals.
The water then flows to the Kanghat Dam in Banan district, then the Minister diverts the flow to two main canals that can absorb 150 cubic meters per second, so the water continues to flow to Stung Sangke level 1, 050 to 1,100 cubic meters per second, and on the morning of August 16, the Minister ordered to lower the sluice further to reduce water flow at the bottom.
According to Mr. Chan Yutha, the water level of Stung Sangke River has risen to a height of 13.75 meters, the alert level is 14.50 meters, so the water level at this point makes the lowest riverbank in the village. China, Sangkat Prek Preah Sdach may face a flood in Battambang city, which requires the Ministry and the authorities as well as the authorities to intervene in the sandbags.
