Dangkor District Governor Tells Subordinates to Provide Better Services to the People, Twice as Recommended by Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nuth Puth Dara, Governor of Dangkor District and Chairman of Khan Unity Command, instructed all subordinates, especially Sangkat Chiefs, Post Chiefs and Village Chiefs to pay attention to better public service and public administration services to the people. Double in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
This instruction was made on the afternoon of August 15, 2018 in the monthly meeting of the Dangkor District Administrative Unity Command, with the participation of the Deputy Governor, Khan Police Inspector, Commander of the Khan Gendarmerie Khan, Sangkat Chief, Post Chief, Village Chief and all school principals in Khan.
The Governor instructed the meeting on a number of important tasks, including: Paying attention to better serving the people, strengthening the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes to prevent all kinds of crimes from occurring. At the local level, especially theft, robbery, gambling and drug offenses, and continue to organize street order and environmental sanitation work.
Notice! OWSO and Citizen's Office of Kampong Speu Provincial Administration Launched
(Kampong Speu): On August 15, 2018, Mr. Yim Sokhom, Chairman of Kampong Speu Provincial Council and Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the OWSO and Office Building. People of Kampong Speu Provincial Administration.
Mr. Vy Samnang stated that the launch aims to improve the quality, efficiency, transparency and accountability of administrative services at the sub-national level through the concentration of administrative services in various sectors in one place to facilitate And respond in a timely manner to the needs and requests of the people.
The governor added that the OWSO is a place that provides administrative services that people need in a timely manner and through simple procedures. This office includes the front line for providing information, receiving and handing over documents, and the back line, which includes professional officers sent from relevant departments and institutions in various fields who have been delegated to the provincial administration to work at the OWSO. Only one.
The Citizens' Office has a mission to make the administration more efficient, transparent, accountable, reduce corruption, increase people's satisfaction and confidence in the provincial administration, as well as increase participation and provide opportunities for people to express their opinions with the provincial administration.
