(Tbong Khmum): Senior Minister Chhay Thorn, Minister of Planning, on the morning of August 15, 2018, presided over the opening ceremony of the dissemination meeting on the launch of the identification of poor families in 2018.
The event was also attended by Mr. Sak Leng, Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Council, Mr. Pen Kosal, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum, as well as representatives of departments, NGOs, development partners.
The Senior Minister stated that with the full support of the Poor Families Identification Program, since 2012, the Royal Government of Cambodia has allocated a series of contributions for the identification of poor households in rural areas, and from 2015 onwards, the Royal Government will be the sole funder. For this work.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia has contributed and increased its contribution budget from 20 percent in 2012 to 60 percent in 2014, and since 2015 has been fully responsible for the identification of poor families in the region. Rural. In particular, the process of identifying poor families in urban areas is supported by both the Royal Government of Cambodia and GIZ.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Mr. Xi Jinping and Mr. Li Keqiang for sending congratulatory messages to the Cambodian People's Party on winning the 6th mandate election.
(Phnom Penh): Immediately after receiving congratulatory messages from Xi Jinping, Secretary-General of the Communist Party of China, and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, who sent congratulatory messages to the CPP. Victory in the 6th Mandate National Assembly Election. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party, sent a message of thanks to Xi Jinping and Le Ker Chheang in separate letters.
I would like to express my strong commitment to continue to work closely with you to promote exchanges between the party and the party, the government and the government, as well as the people and the people, and will continue to promote brotherhood and cooperation. "Operating in a comprehensive strategic partnership between Cambodia and China for the benefit of both our people and for common peace and prosperity within and outside our region."
In a letter of thanks to Mr. Le Ker Chheang, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "The Cambodian people have won the 6th National Assembly election, which was held on July 29, 2018 in a peaceful, free, orderly and transparent manner."
"I would also like to take this opportunity to express my sincere gratitude to the Government for its substantial contribution to the successful conduct of the election process and for sending the largest group of observers to testify in This important event in Cambodia.
