72nd Independence Day! Indian Ambassador to Cambodia vows to increase cooperation with Cambodia in many fields
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the 72nd Independence Day of the Republic of India on August 15, 2018, the Ambassador of India to Cambodia, Ms. Manika Jen, expressed her commitment to increase cooperation in a number of areas, including strengthening ties. Diplomatic relations between Cambodia and India are also closer.
She said that the Government of India is committed to deepening and expanding its partnership with Cambodia, especially this year, Prime Minister Hun Sen visited India in January 2018 and then with the visit of the Minister of Commerce. India in May 2018 and Minister of Defense in June 2018 to Cambodia.
"Indian businesses are now showing great interest in investing in Cambodia and are also looking for other business opportunities," she said. The recent visit of the Indian Defense Minister focused on capacity building in Cambodia, demining operations and other needs of the Cambodian Ministry of Defense.
For the restoration and preservation of Cambodia's cultural heritage, India is continuing to preserve and restore Ta Prohm, the most complex project, and is committed to restoring the Temple of Preah Vihear. Apart from this, there are many other areas of cooperation that India has been cooperating with Cambodia.
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that Cambodia and India have established diplomatic ties since 1952, or can be said to date back to the Angkorian era. When Cambodia was in a difficult period after the genocide, India was the first democracy to provide assistance to Cambodia.
He emphasized that on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to New Delhi earlier this year, Cambodia-India strengthened and expanded long-term friendship and closer cooperation in many fields, including defense. National trade and energy, while the two countries are providing mutual support both in the region and in multilateral forums.
Under the leadership of Mahatma Gandhi, India officially gained independence from the United Kingdom on August 15, 1946, after being under British rule for nearly 200 years.
(Phnom Penh): Immediately after the NEC announces the official results of the 6th National Assembly Election, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister for the new term on the night of August 15. This year 2018 sent a message of thanks to the compatriots who voted for the Cambodian People's Party to win 125 seats in the National Assembly.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the 19 other political parties that competed in the democratic, free, fair and just elections and announced that the new Royal Government of the sixth mandate will be formed in the first week. Of this coming September.
It should be noted that the official results of the 6th National Assembly Election were fully disclosed at 7:30 pm on August 15, 2018 by the National Election Committee announced that the Cambodian People's Party The ruling party controlled all 125 seats in the National Assembly, while the other parties participating in the election did not win any seats.
According to the official results released by the NEC, the Cambodian People's Party of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the party's president, received an overwhelming majority of 4,889,113 votes, equivalent to about 77 percent of the vote. Total work 6,362,241. In all capitals / provinces, the ruling party for the fifth consecutive term has won the leading vote compared to the other 19 political parties contesting the election.
