Siem Reap police officer was stabbed to death by his wife because he was angry and did not help look after his child when he was sick, the perpetrator was arrested by the police 7 hours after the incident
(Siem Reap): A police officer at the Kork Chak Sangkat Administration Post of the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate was stabbed to death by his wife with a knife at around 4 am on August 15, 2108, due to a minor dispute in the family. This incident happened at Group 11, Chhlok Andong Village, Sangkat Slor Kram, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
The Siem Reap Provincial Police report states that after receiving reports from residents and with strict orders from Major General Tith Narong, Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner, as well as Brigadier General Pheng Chendareth, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning, the Siem Reap City Police led Colonel Tep Channa, Siem Reap City Police Inspector, maintained and inspected the scene and conducted a search.
According to the results of the examination at the scene and on the victim's body, there were 10 stab wounds, while the victim's property was not lost, so the police concluded that this case was a case of resentment.
Colonel Nuon Sak Chamroeunrith, Deputy Inspector in charge of Criminal Affairs, said that after a thorough search for seven hours at 13:00 on the same day, our judicial police officers identified The suspect will be brought in for questioning.
The suspect confessed that before the incident last night at 12:25 on August 15 at the suspect's house in group 11, Chhlok Andong village, Slor Kram commune, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, he took the phone. Go to the husband to come and help take the child to the hospital because the child is sick and vomiting blood, but the victim replied that wait until tomorrow.
According to the confessions of the suspects and the confiscated exhibits, the Siem Reap City Police prepared a case and sent it to the court for legal proceedings.
Korea International Cooperation Agency and KOREATECH Institute bring Cambodian trainers to Korea for capacity building
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) on August 14, 2018 organized a orientation ceremony for civil servants from the Ministry of Education who have been selected to study for a training program on building a capacity building system for local trainers. In Cambodia, in the Republic of Korea for the second year of a three-year training course on training capacity development program during service.
The second year training course will be held from August 19 to September 1, 2018 at the Korea College of Technology and Education in Seongnam & Cheonan, Republic of Korea. The training focuses on the identification, development and implementation of teacher training systems in the education system according to the main target groups of teachers for Level 1 secondary schools in Cambodia.
In this program, participants will study 5 sample lessons from Korea, including the first sample lesson: training system and services, the second sample lesson: guidance and methodology, the third sample lesson: teaching skills and curriculum, lessons Model 4: Internship for teacher training system and lessons Model 5: Action plan.
Participants will receive guidance with the trainers in this training program, and at the end of this program, participants will be able to create a direct teacher training system and they will understand how to implement the training system in Cambodia to Get a better quality of education.
In the pre-departure orientation ceremony, KOICA Cambodia officials introduced the short sessions and provided participants with important information on Korea, information about the Cambodia-Korea Alumni Association (CAMKAA) and program ethics. Training. The selected candidates expressed their gratitude to KOICA and the Government of Korea for their support, and they were committed to bringing social and policy reform in Cambodia after gaining experience from Korea.
