Ministry of Water Resources warns that the water level of Stung Sangke in Battambang province is still rising sharply, may reach the emergency level tonight
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on the evening of August 15, 2018, once again warned that the flood of Stung Sangke River in Battambang province is continuing to increase sharply, which may reach the emergency level tonight.
According to the Ministry of Water Resources, at 3:30 pm on August 15, the water level of Stung Sangke in Battambang province was 12.35 meters high, while the alert level was 13.75 meters.
Therefore, the Ministry stated that "the water level of Stung Sangke will continue to rise further and on August 15, the water level of Sangker will rise to the alert level and may cause flooding in some low-lying areas in the city." Battambang.
However, for the situation of the Sangker River, Fresh News will continue to inform the people to increase vigilance and the authorities are always ready to intervene to rescue local people who are waiting for the flood to a safe place. .
Meanwhile, this morning, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, led professional officers to prevent flooding in Battambang City. This is according to Mr. Chan Yutha, Director of the Cabinet and spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources.
However, the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology is leading a flood prevention team to protect Battambang city from flooding. Kampot Provincial Administration Organizes International Day Against Drugs, In the First Half, Authorities Detained 191 Suspects and 276 Packets of Drugs
(Kampot): Colonel Kong Sokhon, Deputy Police Commissioner of Kampot Province, said that according to the report on the results of the anti-drug work of the Secretariat of the Provincial Drug Control Committee in the first half of 2018, the authorities Detained 191 suspects, 276 packages of drugs weighing 259.50 grams, and 14 WY tablets.
The Deputy Commissioner confirmed this on the occasion of the International Day Against Drug Abuse "June 26, 2018" this morning, August 15, 2018, under the presidency of Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot Province at Preah Bida Cheat High School in Chraneang village, Kampong Trach Khang Lech commune, Kampong Trach district, Kampot province.
According to Mr. Kong Sokhorn, Kampot Province, although there are no crimes and targets of drug smuggling, production and cultivation of marijuana, drug trafficking and use continue to occur in a continuous manner. Small in all districts throughout the province, imported into the province of Kampot is out of Phnom Penh by sending equipment by taxi or mobile, meet by phone and so on.
