Techno School and 3 private companies start studying the possibility of building the first mobile phone tower made from bamboo in Cambodia
Under the agreement, Atelier Cole will be responsible for the construction of the bamboo tower structure after the completion of the study by IDC and ITC. IDC aims to build Cambodia's first bamboo telecommunication antenna tower ready for commercial use by the end of 2018.
Bamboo telephone towers are the latest innovation in which we initiate the use of natural resources and renewable resources in the construction of telecommunication infrastructure to reduce environmental impact. When these antennas are built using natural resources, carbon emissions are also reduced.
This type of tower, which was first built in Bangladesh, shows that carbon emissions have been reduced by more than 70% per tower. These antennas are up to 88% lighter than steel antennas and are easy to build and reduce the load on the building.
The Institute of Technology of Cambodia (ITC) strongly believes that renewable resources play an important role in innovating and innovating, and we are extremely pleased to be a good partner with the company. IDC for this unprecedented pioneering project in Cambodia.
Our country is rich in natural resources, and the use of these resources to contribute to the development of the nation is another new step of Cambodia in the sustainable use of its natural resources. This was confirmed by Professor Chra Rada, Dean of the Faculty of Civil Engineering of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
According to the study, unprocessed bamboo can support the weight of concrete when making scaffolding and laying foundations, making it an essential material for the telecommunications construction sector. It can withstand wind speeds of up to 210 km / h and has a lifespan of about 10 years if properly maintained.
Bamboo antenna poles take about 12 days to build and use less energy to produce compared to steel antenna poles. This construction is capable of placing up to eight antennas at the same time, allowing it to be installed in one location.
IDC supplied the world's first home-made bamboo mobile phone tower in Dhaka, Bangladesh in 2017, and has since deployed nine more. The other six are under construction.
IDC continues to deepen its commitment to reducing environmental impact through partnerships with emerging local companies aimed at bringing in mobile antenna towers. From this bamboo to many other markets where the company is operating.
