Ministry of Labor promotes health and safety at factories
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has promoted the promotion of occupational health and safety in factories to increase the working environment to be more efficient and better.
Mr. Leng Tong said that this training is to study the global supply chain, improve industrial relations, occupational risk management and prevention measures, identify new inspection methods and strategies, strengthen communication and soft skills to Have professional relations in the factory.
He said that this course will strengthen the capacity of inspection officers and stakeholders, including: Union representatives and representatives from 41 factories to improve working conditions to reduce accidents at work.
He added that the course aims to strengthen cooperation mechanisms for the public and private sectors in support of the development of labor dispute resolution skills, especially the promotion of effective law enforcement.
Ivo Speu Vinro, a pole and policy expert on the ILO's Better Programs program, said the training was an important bridge in improving the professional relationship between workers and employers. Better in the workplace.
Mr. Ivo Spovin promised that the ILO will continue to work with the Ministry of Labor and other relevant institutions to share good experiences to help improve the implementation of rights and working conditions in Cambodia.
At the same time, Dr. Huy Hansong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, instructed all participants in this morning's training to listen carefully to the trainers to gain knowledge and experience. Continue to advertise to reduce work accidents in the workplace even better.
It should be noted that the national partner training of the Better Work project, Cambodia is the first to implement, followed by Vietnam and Indonesia. The project is a one-and-a-half-year study with teachers as well as online learning and factory visits to learn about working conditions directly.
