US $ 716 billion military budget could allow North Korea to re-test missiles? (video inside) (Washington): The US Department of Defense is expected to spend a lot of money to develop air defense missile system under the framework of the 2019 military budget to prevent any possible missile attack. From Iran or North Korea. This is according to the release by CGTN on Tuesday, August 14, 2018.
The $ 716 billion military budget for 2019, signed by US President Donald Trump on Monday, will provide $ 10 billion to the US Missile Agency for the development of radar and missile defense systems. Additional air is available to counter the Iranian or North Korean missile threat.
But the approval of the massive military package comes amid a calm situation on the Korean Peninsula after North Korea agreed to suspend missile tests and nuclear tests. The military budget is also raising concerns that North Korea may resume missile and nuclear weapons development, as Pyongyang may see it as a threat to its security. Body.
In particular, in 2017, due to concerns over the rise of the US air defense missile system in North Korea, several missiles were test-fired, including the successful detonation of a hydrogen nuclear warhead.
