(Phnom Penh): On the evening of August 14, 2018, representatives of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court began questioning another case of Mr. Kim Sok, a political observer and social analyst, after reviewing the implementation. The previous conviction charged by the CPP in the first case is almost limited.
Kim Sok has been sued twice by Ky Tech, Hun Sen's defense lawyer, after he made serious allegations against the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Cambodian People's Party. In the first case, Kim Sok accused the CPP of being behind the assassination of Dr. Kem Ley. As for the second case, Mr. Kim Sok accused the Royal Government of Cambodia of creating a system to kill people but did not find the killer.
In the first case, on the afternoon of August 10, 2017, the Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Ky Bithy, sentenced to 18 months imprisonment and fined 8 million Riels, including compensation to Plaintiff 800 million Riel after he was detained on February 17, 2018.
Mr. Sieng Sok, a representative of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, who is handling the new case, confirmed to reporters that for Kim Sok's first case, the court will follow the procedure after he has served his sentence. Mr. Sieng Sok confirmed that for the second case, the court is following the interrogation procedure and will question later.
