(Phnom Penh): In order to meet the demand for genuine quality pipes, Chip Mong has invested in researching real quality pipes that are better than other pipes in the region. As a result of the research, Chip Mong decided to make pipes based on Italian technology, using a large part of the raw materials imported directly from the European Union.
After being made into a tube, it has to go through several stages of quality certification before being released to the market. Water pressure resistance test, toughness test and compressive strength test with a weight of more than 5 tons.
In addition to laboratory tests, the Chip Mong hose was tested by carrying a truck weighing more than 30 tons, crushing it to prove its toughness. The results showed that the hose remained unbroken and cracked. A little bit makes us more confident that Cambodians will use local brands with pride.
