Australia: Results come out after studying the oldest rock on the planet!
(Sydney) - The world's oldest rock has been discovered as a result of a collision between an asteroid and Earth 4 billion years ago. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday evening, August 14, 2018.
What led scientists to conclude this is that the composition of the rocks above is different from the composition of the upper layers of the planet in ancient times, and the other is the melting of those rocks. Occurred not far from the Earth's crust (not deep).
