According to sources, in the past, the suspect used to break into the door of the house of the people and took $ 600 and $ 900, but this time, the suspect came to take action again and was caught by the owner of the house. And immediately shouted loudly and then chased immediately.
The victim, Theng Van, 32, a factory worker living in Damnak Troyeung village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, lost 1 g of platinum necklace, $ 1,645 mobile phone and 4 ID cards as well.
Separately, the suspect who carried out this activity was named Nuon Khlem, male, 24 years old, living in Damnak Troyeung Village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Sen Chey. Currently, the suspect is being interrogated by the police to proceed with the procedure.
A UN report released on Monday said that between 3,000 and 4,000 ISIS fighters were maintaining their base in Libya, while key leaders of the terrorist group were working. Operations in Afghanistan. ISIS has lost a large part of its territory after being ousted from Mosul, Iraq and the Syrian city of Raqqa.
However, despite the loss of influence, ISIS militants continue to carry out frequent suicide bombings, and according to the Syrian government, ISIS is secretly operating in remote areas of the country. Syria, too.
(Nigeria): In Africa, Nigeria has the largest population compared to other countries in the continent. In a year, Nigeria needs 6 million tons of rice to eat. Of that, 3 million tons are imported rice. Chinese agricultural experts are trying to find a way to change this situation by increasing the yield of Nigerian rice.
Rice is one of the most important grains for Nigeria. But for many years, rice production here has never been able to meet the needs of the people. But today, Chinese agricultural experts in Nigeria have developed a new variety of rice that can ensure that Nigeria will be able to increase rice yields.
"We started experimenting in 2008 with several hundred different varieties of rice, both available here and imported," said Xu Yuanfang, a Chinese agricultural expert. "After eight or nine years of experimentation, we are finally able to grow this new rice and add it to the list of the National Agricultural Seed Commission of Nigeria."
"Caval rice is doing well," said Ocho Phillip Olusegan, director general of the Nigerian National Seed Commission. "We are ready to continue to support the Kaval rice project to ensure that it will support our farmers by providing good quality rice seeds."
Nigeria is implementing a three-year plan for economic growth and national economic recovery, which will end in 2020. Agriculture and food security are the top priorities of the plan. (China's CCTV)
