Mr. Kim Sok was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court this afternoon to review the prison sentence
On the afternoon of August 10, 2017, Mr. Kim Sok, also known as “Social Analyst” by the public, was sentenced by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court Judge Ky Bithy to 18 months in prison and fined 8 million Riels. Compensation of 800 million Riels to the plaintiff under the accusation of incitement to commit a crime. The conviction came after Kim Sok incited and defamed the CPP as being behind the assassination of Dr. Kem Ley.
It should be noted that Mr. Kim Sok is currently being held in Prey Sar Prison. He is also facing another lawsuit filed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen's lawyer in connection with a case in which the analyst alleged that the Royal Government of Cambodia had set up a system to kill people but never found the killer.
