(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, August 14, 2018, met with a delegation from the Ministry of Agriculture and the People's Republic of China held at the Ministry. Agriculture.
The purpose of the meeting was to implement the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the Development of Modern Agriculture in Cambodia between the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Ministry of Agriculture of the People's Republic of China. Effective January 2018.
Welcoming the delegation, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his gratitude and appreciation for the excellent results resulting from the efforts of the leaders of the two countries and relevant ministries that have supported the development of the sector. Cambodian Agriculture.
He added that the mission of the Chinese delegation is very important at the same time, while the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has been preparing a master plan for the development and modernization of the agricultural sector in Cambodia for the long term 2019-2030.
According to the plan, the mission will be divided into two groups, each with six members to study in 12 potential provinces in agriculture, six in the south and six in the south. Foot of Phnom Penh.
Please note that the mission will complete its preliminary report at the end of August and there will be a signing ceremony of this preliminary report between the Cambodian and Chinese sides.
Work results throughout the year! Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner has cracked down on crime and maintained security and order for the people throughout the province.
(Takeo): As of today, August 14, 2018, Major General Sok Samnang has been the Commissioner of Takeo Provincial Police for one year and one month after trusting and seeing Real ability from General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
According to Major General Sok Samnang, the total police force at Takeo Provincial Police is 1853, of which 15 are deputy commissioners, divided into 12 plans, 33 offices, 9 districts, 100 posts and a border battalion 603. To maintain security and order for local people.
According to the General Commissioner, the results of the work carried out over the past year have been good by following the orders and instructions of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, with the division of forces. Working 24 hours a day to intervene to help people.
In particular, the recent results relate to the work before the election, during the election campaign, during the election and after the election was successful due to the clear division of forces on duty to prevent all active attempts to commit crimes, and for the whole of Takeo province, there is no violence. Or any such threats for past election events.
(Kampong Speu): "Must be prepared before the rescue of people in case of floods in the rainy season 2018 by preparing all the means that the unit already has."
This statement was made by Brigadier General Chou Sarun, Commander of Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie, during a ceremony to disseminate the latest development situation and disseminate plans to rescue people affected by natural disasters and floods in Kampong Speu 2018 and inspect Equipment and equipment to rescue people and test the rescue operation on the morning of August 14, 2018.
The ceremony was attended by all officers, deputies and soldiers under the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie Command.
Brigadier General Chou Sarun set out measures for officers, deputies and soldiers that in case of natural disasters, wind, floods in the 2018 rainy season, we must work very carefully to transport people A safe place to take care of the property of the people to survive. In severe cases, it must be reported immediately to seek intervention from the upper level.
The brigadier general added that the force must work closely with local authorities to constantly monitor high-risk local areas to ensure our rescue. The main points to consider are the elderly, pregnant women, new women After giving birth, children, schools and pagodas.
The commander stressed that from now until the end of the rainy season, all forces must take care of the means of transporting trucks to transport equipment or boats to transport people to safety, especially the use of total force if there is a shortage. The unit will also request immediate assistance from the National Gendarmerie immediately.
