Major General Chan Sopheaktra said that all forces must pay attention to cracking down on cross-border crimes effectively, especially cracking down on drug trafficking cases and preventing illegal Cambodians from crossing the border to cut down trees. At the same time, we have to pay attention to the work of building the camp unit, staying, raising crops, as well as taking care of our health, because this is the rainy season.
Lt. Gen. Chan Sopheaktra also received a courtesy call from Lt. Gen. Chea Morn, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 4th Army Division, as well as Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Administrative Unity Command. Province.
At the same time, the Commander also donated funds for the construction of the unit and some food items to the families of the troops.
