The Constitutional Council and the NEC have not received any complaints against the provisional election results, so the official results will be announced as scheduled tomorrow, August 15.
(Phnom Penh): Both the Constitutional Council and the Constitutional Council, one of the top institutions in resolving election disputes, as well as the National Election Committee (NEC), have stated that they have not received any complaints from the party. No political objection to the results of the provisional 6th National Assembly election announced on August 11, 2018.
By not receiving the complaint, this is paving the way for the NEC to continue its procedures to announce the official election results on August 15, 2018 tomorrow as scheduled.
On August 11, 2018, the NEC announced the provisional results of the election, confirming that 6,956,900 people went to the polls for the 6th National Assembly election. And 83.02 percent of the 8,380,217 registered voters. The Cambodian People's Party received the overwhelming majority of 4,889,113 votes.
Pursuant to Article 131 of the Law on the Election of Members of the National Assembly, all political parties running in the by-elections may complain about part or all of the provisional results of the election to the NEC or directly to the Constitutional Council. 72 hours after the announcement of the provisional election results.
Along with the Constitutional Council announcing that it has not received any complaints from political parties, on August 14, 2018, Mr. Sik Bun also wrote a letter to Mr. Im Chhun Lim, informing that the NEC Received only one complaint from the Cambodian Youth Party, but that complaint was withdrawn on August 13, 2018 yesterday.
With the announcement of the Constitutional Council as well as the NEC not to receive this complaint, it paves the way for the NEC to continue its proceedings. The next procedure of the NEC is to announce the official results of the 6th National Assembly election on Wednesday, August 15, 2018 tomorrow.
