Ministry of Water Resources: The effects of Typhoon Bebinka will bring heavy rainfall, strong winds and high waves while the coastal provinces, while other provincial capitals will receive moderate to heavy rainfall!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a warning that the effects of Typhoon Bebinka will bring more rain to the coastal provinces, while other provincial capitals will receive more or less rain.
According to this forecast, the weather in Cambodia will be as follows:
Coastal areas, especially Koh Kong and Sihanoukville, will continue to receive heavy rainfall. Rain and wind in the sea, high waves
* The northeastern highlands are likely to receive moderate to heavy rainfall.
* The Mekong Basin will receive heavy rainfall from August 17 to 18, and especially after the storm has subsided.
At the same time, the Ministry of Water Resources called on fishermen and seafarers to be extra careful to avoid any possible accidents. 100 Afghan soldiers and 200 Taliban killed in clashes in Ghazni
