Kampot Provincial Governor Urges Resolution of Chronically Disputed Land to People as Soon as Possible!
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province and Chairman of the Provincial State Land Management Committee, urged the people to resolve the land dispute, which has been in dispute for many years, as soon as possible.
He said this at a meeting of the Provincial State Land Management Committee on "Results of the work of measuring land, issuing land titles and resolving disputes to people in Prey Peay village, Trapeang Phleang commune, Chhuk district 103 families and 189 families" this morning. August 13, 2018 at Kampot Provincial Hall.
He added that as the chairman of the provincial state land management committee, he will resolve land disputes quickly, transparently, fairly and acceptable to the people. Option 1: Resolve win-win situation under the coordination of the provincial administration and Option 2: Solve the problem by sending the case to the court, because otherwise the land issue will not end.
Mr. Chheng Phalla, Deputy Provincial Governor, who is the Chairman of the Land Survey Working Group, also confirmed that at the request of 103 families who applied for land titles in Prey Peay Village, Trapeang Phleang Commune, Chhuk District, Kampot Province, the working group has already measured and resolved the rest. Only 16 families.
Meanwhile, in the request of 189 families who applied for land titles according to the procedure, which is located in Prey Peay village, Trapeang Phleang commune, there are still 13 families that have not been resolved yet, for a total of only 29 families have land issues. The land title will be issued to the people soon.
