Minister of Agriculture inspects the progress of a large agricultural investment company in Kratie province, which is cultivating rubber, acacia, banana and pepper on nearly 10,000 hectares
(Kratie): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, accompanied by Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Governor of Kratie Province and other professional officials, visited and evaluated the progress of land concession development this morning. Economy of Green Island Agricultural Development Company, located in Kbal Damrey Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province.
The company has received 9,583 hectares of economic land concessions from the Royal Government, of which 8,181 hectares are for agricultural use to grow rubber and acacia.
Meanwhile, 60 hectares of pepper crops are growing and hope to bear fruit in 2019. In addition to agriculture, the company also plans to preserve and conserve natural resources, especially some of the rare and endangered species of birds and wildlife, to turn the area into an ecotourism site in the future.
Meanwhile, the company has built infrastructure such as roads, reservoirs, staff housing, administrative buildings, health centers, schools and water wells. At present, the company has 236 employees, including 20 foreigners.
In order to achieve the vision of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry, the Minister recommended to the company some important points as follows:
1: Increase attention and speed up the implementation of the main action plans of the company agreed with the Ministry to promote the cultivation and export of agricultural products in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
2. The company should cooperate with local companies, agricultural communities and farmers around this area who have the ability to cultivate potential crops in the export market by implementing contract farming, and at this point the company should cooperate with the General Department of Agriculture and Department of Agro-Industry to study the appropriate legal and technical procedures.
3. In the future, the company should study the possibility of establishing a training and promotion center for agricultural techniques, especially the promotion of good pure crops such as yellow bananas, cashews and pepper to serve the needs of both varieties and techniques of the community in this area.
4. As for the plan to turn this area into an ecotourism area, the conservation of natural resources, especially forests and wildlife, the Minister requested that the company need to better cooperate with the Forestry Administration and local authorities at all levels.
