The operation took place on August 12, 2018, led by Mr. Seng Chhuon, Chairman of the Steering Committee for Inspection of Overweight Vehicles and Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
A report from the Ministry of Public Works stated that the seizure of 14 vehicles on the 60-meter road was overweight from 8 to 40 tons.
Despite the intensive operation, it is still observed that the illegality of the weightlifting has not diminished. In fact, in the July 2018 report, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport seized more than 217 overweight trucks, an increase of five compared to June. Among the vehicles seized were overweight from 5 tons to 40 tons.
Officials involved in the operation to seize the overweight truck revealed that catching overweight trucks is not only difficult to enforce when it comes to catching the rich and influential cars, but the behavior of the transport business remains. Continuing to be disobedient to the law, they continue to be overweight, with no roads to be damaged by the weight of their vehicles.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, once claimed that one truck overweight was equivalent to 1,000 vehicles on the road, and that one truck overweight was equal to 10 tons. Tens of thousands of vehicles drove on that road.
The senior minister has often called on all drivers to respect the law, please do not drive overweight, because this overloading seriously destroys the road. The senior minister also stated that he did not want to be fined for overweight because it could not be offset by the amount of road damage.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has announced that all relevant officials will take the strictest action without exception, regardless of whether the offender has money, power or influence. At any level.
The spacecraft, the size of a small car, will travel through the sun's hot corridor, Corona, in its outer atmosphere, facing countless heat and radiation waves. This mission is the first manned mission to man, and it will completely change our understanding of the sun.
If all goes according to plan, the spacecraft will fly nearly 24 times around the Sun for the next seven years at a distance of just 6.2 million kilometers from the surface of the giant ball of fire. This distance is closer than any spacecraft that has come close to the sun seven times.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hean Vannhorn, Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, appealed to the owners of yellow banana plantations and banana packaging plantations in Cambodia who wish to export to China, please hurry up. Registration with the General Department of Agriculture for further evaluation and guidance, and then sent to the Chinese side for easy export recognition.
Hean Vanhorn's call comes after China just signed an open-door agreement to allow Cambodia to import 300,000 tonnes of yellow bananas a year.
Along with this appeal, there was also some misleading information, quoting Mr. Hean Vannhorn, saying that the Ministry of Agriculture forced all fruit farm owners in Cambodia to register with the Ministry of Agriculture, but not Therefore, the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture is only appealing to the owners of banana plantations who wish to export to China to register for easy export, as in the case of rice exports to China.
Please be informed that on August 2, 2018, Cambodia and China signed a protocol on phytosanitary requirements for the export of Cambodian bananas to China to pave the way for Cambodian bananas to be exported to China. This is the Royal Government's effort to find markets for farmers' agricultural products.
It should be noted that Cambodia's agricultural products exported to China in 2017 were nearly 200,000 tons of rice, cassava products and flour, a total of more than 58 thousand tons, 3,340 tons of rubber, 14,940 tons of sugar cane. And some other agricultural products.
