According to the London-based Syrian Observatory for Human Rights, the blast occurred Sunday on a building believed to be an arms depot belonging to a group of arms dealers in the city. Sarmada of Idlib province in northwestern Syria. Idlib province is the last stronghold of the rebels and could be the next target of Syrian government forces.
