Two of the largest US steelmakers have successfully helped the government oppose a tax cut by US companies that buy steel from abroad, claiming the tariff is to protect national security and boost steel production. Domestic.
A report points out that some top officials of US President Donald Trump's government have deep ties to local steel mills. Among them was Wilbur Ross, Secretary of State for Commerce, who bought and operated a number of steel companies, which he later sold for a profit.
