The Peterson Institute for International Economics estimates that 195,000 American workers could lose their jobs in the next three years if a 25 percent US tariff on global car imports is introduced. Effective. Worse, if other countries retaliate against the United States and raise tariffs on similar products, the United States will lose up to 624,000 jobs.
The U.S. domestic commodity market, ranging from Coca-Cola to vehicles, is being hit by a wave of rising prices under the guise of a false "American national security" term.
Immediately after the US side announced the decision to impose a 25 percent tariff on Chinese imports worth 16 billion US dollars, some commented that the measure would be equivalent to a 25 percent increase in tariffs. For American consumers, the burden falls on low-income families because they prefer Chinese products to products from other countries.
The US government is using tariffs that are not only imposing on China, but also endangering the country and the American people themselves.
