(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, led a delegation to the Northeast Zone to inspect the condition of National Road 73, 383A and other national roads in Kampong Cham, Kratie, Stung Treng, Mondulkiri, Ratanakkiri and Preah Vihear provinces. Threatened by floods.
A series of inspections have been carried out since August 9, 2018 to find out the situation and found that some sections of the road were severely and moderately damaged, and the Ministry is cooperating with the relevant authorities to take action. Prevent and plan to repair the damaged area immediately after the water recedes.
Please be informed that in the past, the sections of National Road No. 3, No. 04, No. 33, No. 41, No. 45, No. 48, No. 57 and other sections of National Road have also been affected by floods and the Ministry has also addressed the impact immediately to Facilitate the traffic of the people to improve.
The ministry called on residents to be extremely vigilant and to report to the ministry and relevant authorities about the flood threat. Do not drive too fast and travel safely.
During a visit to inspect the condition of these national roads on Friday, August 10, 2018, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol distributed humanitarian donations to 50 flood victims. The family lives in Srah Russey commune, Stung Treng city, whose houses, fields and crops were flooded.
Donations distributed to people who are in distress due to the flooding of houses, farms and fields due to the floods include: Some food items and 70,000 budget per family.
