He also said that through this good relationship, on average, about 500,000 Korean and Cambodian tourists have traveled to Cambodia and Korea, and the Cambodian people have been But the interest in Korean culture and language is growing.
In addition to excellent communication in tourism, the Korean language has also been strengthened in Cambodia. Currently, five universities in Cambodia, including the Royal University of Phnom Penh, open Korean language departments, and every year about 50,000 Cambodians take the TOPIK Korean Language Proficiency Test. Cambodians are very interested in the Korean language.
It should be noted that Cambodia and South Korea were linked in 1996 by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and President Kim Yong San. The Cambodian-South Korean relationship has grown steadily over the past 21 years. The South Korean Embassy is hosting the 23rd International Korean Speech Contest in Cambodia with participants from 15 countries.
