(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts, in collaboration with the Cambodian Climate Change Alliance of the National Council for Sustainable Development of the Ministry of Environment, organized the second training workshop on the preparation of greenhouse gas inventories in industry and handicrafts, which took place on Friday, August 14, 2018, at Angkor Davorn Hotel, Siem Reap Province.
Speaking at the opening ceremony, Dr. Toeng Sini, Undersecretary of State and Project Director, said that under the wise leadership of Honorary Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, the Ministry has been implementing a comprehensive climate change action plan. And its mission, such as:
1. Efficient use of resources and clean production will enable handicraft factories to benefit from lower production costs, increase productivity, and contribute to minimizing greenhouse gas emissions and emissions. Into the environment as well.
2. Establish an environmental management system (EMS) with sufficient data for the integration of staff training procedures and processes, monitoring, summarizing and reporting information on environmental activities.
3. Promote the reduction of greenhouse gas emissions from factories, enterprises and handicrafts by setting guidelines for producers in this sector to follow.
Mr. Toeng Sini emphasized that today's training workshop is an important participation in training the capacity of professional officers of the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts to become professional officers in order to be able to participate in the preparation of greenhouse gas inventory in the industrial sector. And handicrafts, and this training program has the following main objectives:
* Introduce the basic concept of impacts and measures that respond to climate change in accordance with the 2015 Climate Agreement.
* Build and strengthen additional capacity related methods to calculate greenhouse gas emissions in industry and handicrafts.
* Methods for evaluating and collecting necessary data and compiling greenhouse gas data in industry and handicrafts.
Classification of greenhouse gas emissions from industrial processes and production uses.
* Encouraging participants to take the above knowledge and experience for the implementation of the action plan.
