Agriculture Minister calls on Asian Food Safety and Security Association to continue to support, promote and promote agricultural development
(Siem Reap): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on August 10, 2018, requested the Asian Food Safety and Security Association to continue to support the promotion and promotion of agricultural development in all forms to ensure Food security and nutrition at the family, community, national and international levels.
The request was made on the occasion of Mr. Veng Sakhon's honorary participation in the opening ceremony of the 4th International Conference of the Food Security and Security Association in Asia under the theme: "Food Security and Food Security" held at the hotel. Angkor Parady, Siem Reap province, this morning, August 10, 2018.
The event was also attended by NGOs, development partners, members of the Food Safety and Security Association in Asia from about 18 countries, as well as more than 260 professors, scientists, researchers and students.
Mr. Ngor Ponthan, Rector of the Royal University of Agriculture, briefed the conference on the overall content and main objectives of the conference:
1: Strengthen and expand the dissemination of knowledge, technology and innovation
2: Gather experts, policy makers to address challenges related to food safety and food security
3. Strengthen the capacity of scientists, researchers, students and development agencies from developing countries to create new knowledge and expand development opportunities.
4: Facilitate partnerships to promote cooperation and joint initiatives
5. Bring together national and international experts, entrepreneurs, scientists, technicians, policy makers and civil society to address key food security and key food security issues.
Addressing the ceremony, Minister Veng Sakhon extended a warm welcome and warm welcome to the delegation of the Asian Food Safety and Security Association, all national and international guests who were invited to attend the 4th International Conference in Siem Reap. A historical city of the beloved motherland of Angkor.
Mr. Veng Sakhon highly appreciated and thanked the Royal University of Agriculture, NGOs, University Development Partners, Mekong Institute and the Asian Food Safety and Security Association for their support and sponsorship of this important international conference. This.
He hoped that the input of ideas, knowledge, experiences and recommendations of the members of the conference will be useful and continue to strengthen cooperation in research, policy development to achieve solutions and achieve. Ensure sustainable food and food security in Asia and the world.
At the same time, the Minister of Agriculture requested the conference to continue to support, promote and promote the development of the agricultural sector in all forms to ensure food security and nutrition at the household, community, national and international levels to reduce poverty and raise Productivity, production, diversification and commercialization of agriculture, focusing on:
1: Food production: Sustainable (eg modernization of agriculture, organic farming, organic agriculture, conservation agriculture), conservation of the environment and natural resources
2: Strengthen food security: reduce malnutrition and timely and effective intervention from the effects of climate change
3: Pay attention to food safety: by improving food quality, water hygiene, safety and food safety standards that can reduce food hazards, foodborne illness
4: Food management and loss prevention: innovation, storage, packaging, reduction of food waste and waste, cold chain development, use of by-products and value-added products
5: Food processing and protection: Emerging processing techniques, processing, packaging and cold chain development
6: Challenges: Risk management on food safety, nutrition, trade, food security, cooperation, research on gender policy and climate change, as well as other food issues related to and affecting food security and food security at the national level and International.
On that occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon also requested the conference to review and consider all strategies or mechanisms for systematic solutions in line with the latest developments and innovations of regional and global economic growth, especially population growth.
