(Phnom Penh): From this August, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training with stakeholders began to discuss their respective internal work to prepare to negotiate a minimum wage increase for workers in the garment and footwear sector in Cambodia for the year. 2019. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor on August 9, 2018.
The announcement, obtained by Fresh News this afternoon, states that the minimum wage negotiation schedule for the textile, garment and footwear products for 2019 will be based on the following timelines and criteria:
* August 2018 is the beginning of the discussion on the minimum wage, the internal nature of each party and bilaterally
* September 2018 marks the start of a tripartite minimum wage discussion
* All parties must use social criteria (household status, inflation rate and cost of living) and economic criteria (productivity, national competitiveness, labor market status and sector profit margins) as well as poverty lines for work. The basis for discussing the minimum wage in Cambodia.
All parties should focus on data and scientific research in accordance with the seven criteria set out in Article 5 of the Minimum Wage Law as a basis for internal coordination and a common position.
Please be informed that the minimum wage of workers in the garment and footwear sector in Cambodia has started to increase higher every year, and in 2018, workers' wages increased to 170 US dollars per month.
