Government Spokesperson: US Assistant to Cambodia Request for Release of Kem Sokha
(Phnom Penh): The spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Mr. Phay Siphan, on the afternoon of August 8, 2018, said that the request of the US Assistant to Cambodia to release Mr. Kem Sokha, former President of the Cambodia National Rescue Party, is Wrong direction because this jurisdiction does not rest on the Royal Government of Cambodia, but it is the jurisdiction of the judiciary.
According to Phay Siphan, the decision to release or not release the former CNRP president and senior party officials is not within the jurisdiction of the Royal Government, but within the jurisdiction of a separate court. Stated by the Constitution.
"The request of the aide to release Kem Sokha and some other prisoners is in the wrong direction, not within the jurisdiction of the Royal Government, but the jurisdiction of the court," he said. "Apart from Kem Sokha's case, this case is in the process of court proceedings," he said.
It should be noted that Mr. Kem Sokha was arrested by the authorities at midnight on September 3, 2017 at his home in Sangkat Boeung Kak 2, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, after CBN Australia released a video showing that he Followed by the order of the United States, which is an act of treason to seize power from the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia that emerged from the election.
Following his arrest, the court charged Kem Sokha with "peace with a foreigner", an offense of treason under Article 443 of the Penal Code, which carries a maximum sentence of 15 to 30 years in prison. Kem Sokha has also been remanded in custody. Indonesia's new ambassador to Cambodia pledges to do all possible to further strengthen and expand agricultural cooperation between the two countries
The Ambassador praised Cambodia's progress and praised the cooperation between the two countries in the past, especially in the field of agriculture, and expressed his deep gratitude to the Minister and his acquaintances. Lead ministries at all levels that have provided excellent cooperation with the Indonesian government in the past.
On the occasion of his diplomatic mission in Cambodia, the Ambassador pledged to do his best to promote, strengthen and expand agricultural cooperation between the two countries to a better level. The ambassador promised to bring the proposal to the relevant ministries or institutions, then move to exchange professional officers or set up a technical working group to find a solution.
