(Phnom Penh): People, please be very careful! From August 8 to 14, fishermen and seafarers must be extra careful to avoid any possible danger caused by the storm. This is according to the weather forecast letter of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology from August 8 to 14, 2018, which was received by Fresh News this afternoon.
The Ministry of Water Resources said that after monitoring the weather, it was found that:
* The low pressure system that is dragging across the Mekong River basin is connected to a low pressure area in the Pacific Ocean. * In the low pressure system, there is an active pressure in the South China Sea. This active low pressure will move towards Hainan Island and in the next 3-4 days it will develop into a hurricane in Hainan Island and Hong Kong * Meanwhile, the southwest monsoon will intensify the coastal areas. Cambodia.
According to the forecast, the weather in Cambodia will be as follows: * Coastal areas, especially Koh Kong and Sihanoukville, may receive more rain for several more days. Rain and strong winds over the high seas, high waves * Highlands and provinces along the Cambodian and Vietnamese borders are likely to receive moderate to heavy rainfall over the weekend * Other provinces may Moderate to heavy rain.
At the same time, the Ministry of Water Resources called on fishermen and seafarers to be extra careful to avoid any possible accidents. Cambodia exported more than 4 billion US dollars worth of garments, up 11% in the first half. 2018
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, confirmed that in the first half of 2018, Cambodia exported 4.143 million US dollars worth of garments, an increase of 11%, while agricultural products amounted to 272 million US dollars, an increase of 8%. Other exports amounted to $ 1.379 billion, up 14 percent from the same period in 2017.
Mr. Pan Sosak made this remark during a meeting with the winners of the Japan Development Master Scholarship Program in Japan 2018-2020 on August 7, 2018 at the Ministry of Commerce.
The Minister stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, through its Ministry of Commerce, has set out a policy of free market opening and economic integration into the region and the world through ASEAN membership and WTO membership. He (WTO) and the ASEAN Economic Community in late 2015.
The Ministry of Commerce has been actively working to improve the business environment and trade facilitation to ensure the growth of the private sector, which is considered the engine of national economic growth, as defined in the Rectangular Strategy Phase III and Strategic Plan. National Development NDSP 2014-2018.
With the launch of administrative reform programs, human resource development and the promotion of public service transparency, as well as a number of effective policies related to trade facilitation and the promotion of Cambodian products, the Cambodian business sector has made great strides. Better and bigger in size.
Mr. Pan Sorsak said that in 2017, the Ministry of Commerce, with the support of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, established a Permanent Mission in charge of Trade in Geneva, Switzerland to lead the negotiation of a trade agenda. Take advantage of various benefits, especially the elimination of non-tariff barriers to products imported from Cambodia.
The Ministry is currently negotiating a Free Trade Agreement (FTA) and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) between ASEAN and six other partner countries to further diversify Cambodia's export markets. More.
He added that the Ministry of Commerce was preparing to update the fourth generation of Cambodia Integration Strategy (CTIS) 2019-2023 in order to explore new potential products to develop value chains and diversify exports to target markets. Various.
He added that the ministry is implementing a market promotion project for small-scale agriculture to link farmers' products with the market, focusing on five products: rice, chicken, vegetables, cassava and luxury silk.
At the same time, in order to protect the interests of the private sector and consumers, the Ministry has been working to promote legal documents under the commercial sector, such as the law on e-commerce, the law on trade contracts, the law on competition and the law. On food safety, etc. All of these laws will enhance Cambodia's competitiveness in the global trading system in the future.
(Pursat): Police forces of Krakor district, with the coordination of the King of Pursat Provincial Court, raided a guesthouse under the brand name "59" and arrested three suspects for distributing and using illegal drugs, including exhibits. And some materials.
The above transaction took place at 9:26 am on August 08, 2018 at the "59" brand guesthouse in Village 4, Kampong Loung Commune, Krakor District, Pursat Province.
Col. Nhek Sokea, Deputy Inspector of Krakor District, said that in the above operation, the force cracked down and arrested three suspects, including the first exhibits and materials: Ear Bunly "alias Bun", male, 30 years old Second, Nget Da, male, 22 years old, and third: Khim Dany, male, 21 years old. The three suspects are currently living in Phsar village, Anlong Thnout commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
The Deputy Inspector continued that in the case of arresting the three suspects related to drugs, the force confiscated the exhibits including: white gram powder, suspected to be drugs, black Smash V motorcycle with license plate Siem Reap 1N 7443, 1 mobile phone, 5 units of foreign currency, 106 US dollars, 1050,000 Khmer Riel, 1 backpack, 1 black backpack and one suspected drug paraphernalia.
