(Banteay Meanchey): The Cambodian-Thai Drug Control Institution, led by General Chey Bopha, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Mr. Paskan Vanichsiri and Mr. Om Rath, Deputy Governor, visited on August 8, 2018. Phnom Bak New Life Addiction Treatment Center, which is managed by the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, is located in Sangkat Teuk Thla, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
On that occasion, Mr. Phea Manit, Deputy Director of the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and a representative of the center's management, said that his center has so far treated and rehabilitated more than 4,700 addicts who have been cured. Of those, 301 are women.
