Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh: The Victory Monument will be completed according to the plan as the whole monument is almost finished
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Victory Monument Construction Committee, stated that the construction of the Victory Monument is now nearing completion and will hope that the construction will Must be completed as planned while the monument is almost complete.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said this on the morning of August 8, 2018, on the occasion of Samdech accompanied by General Nem Sovath, Deputy Chairman of the Victory Monument Construction Committee, General Ith Sarath and his team continued to inspect. Check out the construction of the win-win monument as well.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said: "Therefore, there is some work that needs to be pushed further and we look at some work that can be done, we complete it to grow to respond in time, which is very important. "According to the work calendar, what we need to add, what we warm up, we let it go and the amount of work left, we can gather more energy to be ready to open on the 29th."
The Chairman of the Win-Win Monument Construction Committee continued, "We need time to build this Victory Monument and we have already done it to commemorate the 20th anniversary on December 29, 2018 and all the work left." This is obvious, today we came to check the remaining work to speed up the deadline.
The Chairman of the Victory Monument Commission stated that the construction of this Victory Monument is to commemorate the merits of Cambodian ancestors of all times who sacrificed their lives in the cause of the motherland. Moreover, this monument is also a symbol of the peace that Cambodia has achieved after the end of decades of civil war. In addition, this monument will be a legacy for future generations.
Please be reminded that the construction of this Victory Monument started in February 2016 with an area of 8 hectares in Chroy Changva district, Phnom Penh. The budget used for construction is the contribution of the Royal Government, not related to the state budget. However, it did not specify how much the construction would cost.
