(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, August 8, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to meet with a total of 18,467 workers. People from 14 factories in Kampong Speu province. The ceremony took place in Snor I Village, Sangkat Rokar Thom, Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province.
The following are the main remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulated and thanked the Cambodian people who went to the polls to rank second in the world after Belgium.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that the large turnout of the people was a sign of respect for and maintenance of the democratic process in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the Cambodian people's election to support the Cambodian People's Party as the right choice to maintain peace and development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, officially announced:
* In the morning of September 5, 2018, the first session of the National Assembly chaired by the King * In the evening of September 5, 2018, MPs were sworn in * In the morning of September 6, 2018, the locomotive of the second mandate 6 and the new Royal Government * In the evening of September 6, 2018, the new Cabinet was sworn in * In the morning of September 7, 2018, the first meeting of the new Cabinet
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that yesterday, Samdech met with the King to ask for His Majesty the King to hold the first National Assembly meeting on Wednesday, September 5 under the King. On Thursday, September 6, the locomotive of the National Assembly and the Royal Government will be formed, and on Friday morning, September 7, the first meeting of the Cabinet of the sixth mandate will be held.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the request for a royal grant to postpone the date of the first meeting of the National Assembly, as well as to form the Royal Government and open the Cabinet meeting, has already been approved by the King.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that according to the President of the Constitutional Council, it is not illegal to postpone the convening of the National Assembly and form the Royal Government. Not wrong, according to the three laws, including: convening the National Assembly under the King, 2. The convening of this meeting shall not be more than 60 days after the election day; and Convene a meeting after the National Election Committee announces the elected candidates.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the workers did not just get to know Samdech for a day, two days or a month or two, but they got to know him through their grandparents because of their grandparents and parents. Has struggled with Samdech to build this country since the time of the poor country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has only been fully developed for 20 years, that is, since 1998, after the integration of the Khmer Rouge soldiers to live under the same government.
* Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, said that Cambodia has a very difficult history in the past to maintain peace and development as it is now, having recovered from the difficult situation of war. In that, after the overthrow of the genocidal regime on January 7, 1979, Cambodia used one hand to develop the country and the other hand to prevent the return attempt of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
* Samdech Techo added that along with the development as well as efforts to prevent the genocidal regime, Samdech himself also tried to find peace and unification of the country until it achieved historical success in 1998.
* Samdech Techo stated that he did not understand the suggestion that Cambodia was getting poorer. Samdech Techo confirmed that the Cambodian people are not as poor as under the Pol Pot regime.
* The Prime Minister stated that Cambodia has moved from poverty to a low-middle-income country today and is striving to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a developed country by 2050. Samdech Techo also stated that the Prime Minister of Japan and the President of China have promised to help Cambodia achieve its ambition to become a developed country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people of Kampong Speu for voting for Hun Many as a Member of Parliament and asked the people of Kampong Speu to run to Hun Many when there was a problem.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the success that comes with hardship is a proud success and must be maintained. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that keeping the next five years is the time to strive to achieve what has been set.
* Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian People's Party, said that the burden of the Cambodian People's Party is heavier because now people have voted for it. Samdech Techo stated that the new mandate is a time to reform and strive to improve the lives of the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for extreme caution in the transportation of workers without negligence leading to accidents.
* The Prime Minister repeatedly told the "Sleep at home, win alone" movement that no one sleeps at home to get results or get food. Samdech Techo confirmed that all achievements come from hard work.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the bank to provide support to small and medium enterprises is about to emerge with a capital of 100 million US dollars.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is investing heavily in rice mills and dryers to collect rice for farmers to process into rice for export. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that Cambodia is investing in cassava processing plants with a capacity of about 14 million tons per year.
* The Prime Minister stated that industrial policy has not forgotten the agricultural sector, but is making the industrial sector a locomotive to pull the agricultural sector into the agro-industrial sector.
* The Prime Minister stated that exporting in the field of agriculture is Samdech's concept. Samdech refers to the import of agricultural products, vegetables, meat and other animals, including farmers' eggs and duck eggs into the hotel.
