Kampot International Tourism Port was inaugurated on the special day of August 8, 2018 at a cost of $ 8 million
(Kampot): As the number of international tourists increases from year to year and the transport activity is more busy, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to build a new international tourist port in Kampot to facilitate water transport and contribute to growth. More international tourists in Cambodia.
The construction site of Kampot International Tourism Port was inaugurated at 8:08 am on August 08, 2018 under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, with the participation of Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot, Representative of the Development Bank. Asia in Phnom Penh and about 800 relevant government officials.
He said that waterways are also an attractive means of transportation and tourism, which the Royal Government of Cambodia has been focusing on promoting the development of these waterway tourism facilities, especially in the ports of Sihanoukville and Kampot, as well as coastal provinces. Others to boost the movement and flow of tourism in the coastal areas and southern tourism corridors.
Mr. Tith Chantha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Director of the Kampot International Tourism Port Project, said that the construction of the Kampot International Tourism Port requires more than $ 8 million in concessional financing from the Asian Development Bank.
In particular, the coastal area in 2017 received about 3.2 million tourists, of which about 740,000 international tourists, an increase of 20%. By 2020, Cambodia is projected to receive 7 million international tourists with more than $ 5 billion in revenue and create about 1 million direct jobs and millions more indirect jobs.
