Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that yesterday, Samdech met with His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, to request His Majesty the King to change the date of the convening of the National Assembly and Formation of the Royal Government in the new mandate.
"Wednesday morning, September 5, the National Assembly will convene for the first time under the presidency of the King, and on the evening of September 5, the National Assembly will be sworn in," he said. On Thursday, September 6, the National Assembly will be formed, as well as the new Royal Government until the evening of September 6, the Royal Government will be sworn in until the morning of the 7th, which is Friday, the new Cabinet will Open the first meeting.
Samdech further explained that this amendment is not illegal or unconstitutional, because the law stipulates that the formation of the National Assembly must take place no later than 60 days after the announcement of the election results. Samdech stated that on August 15, the NEC will announce the official results, during which time there will be complaints and settlements from the NEC level to the Constitutional Council.
"So 10 days is enough for the Constitutional Council, so in early September the National Election Commission may announce the final results, divide the seats and determine the names of those elected to the position of King," he said. Must convene a meeting.
Please note that the 6th National Assembly election ended successfully on the evening of July 29, 2018 with a good security situation, no threats or violence. The election was assessed by national and international observers, the media and many political parties as free, fair and just.
Cambodia, Thailand jointly strengthen drug prevention and illegal cross-border crime
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by Mr. Thou Phea, Deputy Governor, led a delegation to attend a meeting on Border Drug Prevention and Control (BLO) with Mr. Vithurat Srinam, Governor of Chan Borei Province, Thailand at the office. Tourism and trade on the Cambodian-Thai border Banlem market to jointly strengthen cross-border drug crime, human trafficking, arms trafficking and smuggled goods along the border.
In the afternoon meeting on August 7, 2018, Mr. Phan Chanthul mentioned that the cooperation and coordination of anti-drug measures (BLO) with Cambodia-Thailand bordering to cooperate in education. Disseminate and prevent drug problems along the border and exchange information along the border on all issues related to cultivation, production, trafficking, drug use and trafficking in chemicals.
