The swearing-in ceremony of the 42-year-old former lawyer took place under the deployment of more than 12,000 troops in the capital Bogota, where the Colombian Civil Aviation Authority banned the launch of drones after A drone strike attempted to assassinate the Venezuelan president last weekend.
The inauguration of new Colombian President Iván Duque comes as Colombia is embroiled in tensions with its neighbor Venezuela after Nicolas Maduro accused outgoing Colombian President Juan Manuel Santos. Behind the assassination attempt. Maduro has also promised to release evidence soon, although Santos has denied the allegations.
Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro has claimed that he has evidence that the Colombian government was involved in his assassination attempt and has promised to release the evidence soon. Maduro made the remarks on Twitter on Tuesday after Venezuelan police arrested six suspects.
