(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, August 8, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to meet with a total of 18,467 workers. From 14 factories in Kampong Speu province. The ceremony will take place in Snor I Village, Sangkat Rokar Thom, Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province.
The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, said that the 14 factories that allow workers to participate in the talks are invested by nine investors from China, four Koreas and one Japanese. These factories include: garment factories, bag factories and animal feed factories. The products manufactured in these factories are exported to international markets and supplied to domestic markets.
The Minister claimed that the factory in Kampong Speu was built at the local level next to the people, which created many jobs and additional jobs, making it easier for young people to find jobs in their locality, renting houses, selling food, transporting Transportation and other services contribute to the economic development and livelihood of the people.
Kampong Speu is an agricultural province and was once a battlefield during the war. After the war ended under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen during 1996, Kampong Speu province became a province with high potential for agriculture and industry and attracted investment in industry and agriculture. Industry as well.
According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, up to now, Kampong Speu province has 228 factories, enterprises and establishments with 102,736 workers, with a total salary of more than 247 million dollars per year. There are 109 garment and footwear factories with 96,547 workers, earning more than $ 232 million a year.
From August 20, 2017 to August 08, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with a total of 52 workers and a total of 718,669 workers met directly. Among them, the Chief of Administration, Division Chief, Team Leader and a total of 751 assistants also met with the Prime Minister.
Through this series of meetings, the working environment in the factories has been improved, many problems and concerns of the workers have been solved continuously, and many benefits have been provided by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the workers.
